/* =====================================================================
   060_iso27001_v13_practices.sql

   Bulk load of the ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Practice catalogue v1.3 into
   GRAC_New.requirement, and of the Practice -> Statement links into
   GRAC_New.framework_statement_requirement_map.

   Source     : Import Practice & Obligation Mapping v1.3 (4).xlsx, sheet 'Practices'
   Practices  : 1218  (528 surviving, 690 merged-into-another)
   Statements : 93 Annex A controls, already loaded by 052
   Prerequisites : 058 (reset) and 059 (masters) must have run.
   Follow-on  : 061 - 065 load the five Obligation registers and resolve
                every Obligation to a Practice loaded here, so 060 must
                complete successfully before any of them is run.
   Rerunnable : yes. A Practice whose Practice Name already exists is
                skipped; its Statement mapping is still created if missing.
   Rollback   : 060_iso27001_v13_practices_rollback.sql

   FILE ENCODING
   -------------
   Saved as UTF-8 with BOM. Several Practice texts contain U+2019 (right
   single quotation mark, as in "organisation's"). Open in SSMS normally,
   or run with: sqlcmd -f 65001 -i 060_iso27001_v13_practices.sql
   All literals are N'' prefixed and embedded apostrophes are doubled.

   WHY ALL 1218 ROWS LOAD, NOT JUST THE 528 SURVIVORS
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   The sheet's 'Merge Review Status' marks 690 Practices as merged into
   another ('Merged into POL-05 - Merged'). They are still loaded. The
   five Obligation registers reference them directly: 6,713 of the 12,071
   Obligation rows hang off a merged Practice. Dropping them would mean
   redirecting more than half the catalogue through the Merged Practices
   traceability sheet, which maps source Practice IDs -- not the Practice
   Names the registers actually carry.

   The merge status is preserved on every row: it is written into
   requirement.remarks-equivalent provenance (see the audit trail below)
   and staged in #prac.merge_status, so a report can separate the 528
   surviving Practices from the 690 absorbed ones at any time.

   HOW A STATEMENT IS RESOLVED
   ---------------------------
   The sheet's 'framework_statement_id' column carries the real
   GRAC_New.framework_statement key. It is the authoritative link and this
   script uses it directly: @resolve_by_statement_id = 1 (the default).

   Every row is still cross-checked. The reference parsed from
   'ISO 27001 Control No and Name' -- the leading token with the 'A.'
   prefix stripped ('A.5.10 Acceptable use ...' -> '5.10') -- must equal
   the statement_reference of the row that ID resolves to. Any
   disagreement aborts the whole load and lists every offending pair.

   That check is the point. framework_statement_id is an IDENTITY column,
   so its values belong to ONE database. Run this script against a
   different environment -- a rebuilt UAT, a fresh developer instance,
   statements reloaded in another order -- and the same IDs will name
   different controls. Without the cross-check the load would succeed and
   silently attach 1218 Practices to the wrong Annex A controls, which no
   constraint would catch and no screen would make obvious.

   For such an environment set @resolve_by_statement_id = 0. The script
   then matches on statement_reference within the resolved release and
   ignores the ID column entirely.

   PRACTICE CODE IS NOT TAKEN FROM THE SHEET
   -----------------------------------------
   The sheet's 'Practice ID' column (POL-01, ROL-01, AUT-01 ...) is NOT
   loaded as requirement_code. Since migration 050 the Practice Code is
   system-generated -- PR-001, PR-002, PR-003 ... -- and
   cm_manage_repository assigns it on save. This script follows the same
   rule and the same numbering, continuing from the highest PR-### already
   in GRAC_New.requirement.

   The sheet's IDs could not be used even if the convention allowed it:
   16 of them are reused across unrelated controls --

       AUT-01 .. AUT-05   A.5.5  Contact with authorities
                          A.5.17 Authentication information
       DSP-01 .. DSP-12   A.6.4  Disciplinary process
                          A.7.14 Secure disposal or re-use of equipment

   -- and requirement_code is UNIQUE, so half of each pair would have been
   rejected. Generated codes make all 1218 rows loadable. The sheet's ID is
   still staged in #prac.practice_ref and written to the audit trail, so a
   row can be traced back to the spreadsheet.

   HOW A PRACTICE IS IDENTIFIED ON RE-RUN
   --------------------------------------
   By requirement_name. All 1218 Practice Names in this workbook revision are
   distinct -- v1.3 (4) fixed the two collisions earlier revisions had --
   so the name is a safe natural key for the skip test, and it is what
   061-065 join on. Validation step 6 re-proves it before writing anything.
   Do not rename a loaded Practice before running 061-065.

   MAKER-CHECKER
   -------------
   'requirements' is registered with is_maker_checker = 1, so interactive
   saves route through change_management. This script is a controlled bulk
   load and writes directly, exactly as 052 and 053 do. An audit_trace row
   is written per inserted Practice and per inserted mapping, so the load
   is visible in the trail.

   COLUMN MAPPING
   --------------
     Practice Name        -> requirement.requirement_name
     Practice Description -> requirement.requirement_statement
     Practice Objective   -> requirement.objective
     Practice Keywords    -> requirement.keywords          (added by 023)
     Practice ID          -> audit trail only
     Merge Review Status  -> audit trail only

   NOT SUPPLIED BY THE SHEET
   -------------------------
   control mapping : control_requirement_map is not written. The sheet maps
                     Practices to Framework Statements, not to internal
                     Controls.
   ===================================================================== */

SET NOCOUNT ON;
SET XACT_ABORT ON;
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Clear stale temp tables -- SEPARATE BATCH, ON PURPOSE
--
-- # temp tables live for the whole session, not the script. If an earlier
-- run of a different revision of this file left #prac or #stmt behind
-- with different columns, SQL Server binds the INSERT statements further
-- down against THAT table when it compiles the batch -- before the
-- CREATE TABLE below has had a chance to run -- and the load dies with
-- "Invalid column name" on a column this file plainly declares.
--
-- The GO after this block is what fixes it: the drops complete in their
-- own batch, so the batch that follows compiles against nothing and the
-- CREATE TABLE statements define the shape.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
IF OBJECT_ID('tempdb..#prac') IS NOT NULL DROP TABLE #prac;
IF OBJECT_ID('tempdb..#stmt') IS NOT NULL DROP TABLE #stmt;
GO

CREATE TABLE #prac(
    seq                INT           NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    sheet_statement_id BIGINT        NOT NULL,
    statement_reference NVARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    practice_ref       NVARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    practice_name      NVARCHAR(300) NOT NULL,
    practice_statement NVARCHAR(MAX) NOT NULL,
    objective          NVARCHAR(MAX) NULL,
    keywords           NVARCHAR(MAX) NULL,
    is_merged          BIT           NOT NULL,
    merge_status       NVARCHAR(200) NULL);
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Staged sheet rows
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
INSERT #prac(seq,sheet_statement_id,statement_reference,practice_ref,practice_name,practice_statement,objective,keywords,is_merged,merge_status) VALUES
(1,1,N'5.1',N'POL-01',N'Establish the information security policy',N'The organisation must define a high-level information security policy that explains the organisation’s security approach, objectives, guiding principles, commitments, responsibilities and method for handling exceptions. It must consider business needs, legal and contractual duties, and current and expected risks and threats. It must assign policy ownership and approval. The purpose is to provide clear management direction and support for information security. It also aims to make policy accountability and approval authority clear.',N'Provide clear management direction and support for information security. Make policy accountability and approval authority clear.',N'information security policy; objectives; principles; requirements; improvement; exceptions; policy owner; responsibility; competence; top management; approval; change approval',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(2,1,N'5.1',N'POL-02',N'Maintain topic-specific policies',N'The organisation must create detailed policies where needed for security areas and target groups, such as access control, backup, incident management, cryptography, classification, vulnerability management and secure development. Keep them aligned with the main policy. The purpose is to turn the organisation’s security direction into clear requirements for specific areas and users.',N'Turn the organisation’s security direction into clear requirements for specific areas and users.',N'topic-specific policy; access control; backup; incident; cryptography; classification; secure development',1,N'Merged into POL-05 — Merged'),
(3,1,N'5.1',N'POL-03',N'Assign policy ownership and approval',N'The organisation must assign competent owners to develop and review policies. Obtain approval from top management for the main policy and its changes, and from the appropriate management level for topic-specific policies. The purpose is to make policy accountability and approval authority clear.',N'Make policy accountability and approval authority clear.',N'policy owner; responsibility; competence; top management; approval; change approval',1,N'Merged into POL-01 — Merged'),
(4,1,N'5.1',N'POL-04',N'Publish and communicate policies',N'The organisation must publish policies in a form that is relevant, accessible and understandable. Communicate them to relevant personnel and interested parties, obtain acknowledgement where applicable, and protect confidential content when policies are shared externally. The purpose is to ensure people know, understand and agree to follow the policies that apply to them.',N'Ensure people know, understand and agree to follow the policies that apply to them.',N'publication; communication; accessibility; acknowledgement; interested parties; confidentiality',1,N'Merged into POL-05 — Merged'),
(5,1,N'5.1',N'POL-05',N'Review and improve policies',N'The organisation must review policies at planned intervals and after significant changes. It must consider changes in business, technology, laws, contracts, risks, threats, incidents, audits and management reviews, and update related policies to keep them consistent. It must maintain topic-specific policies. It must publish and communicate policies. The purpose is to keep policies suitable, adequate, effective and aligned with changing needs. It also aims to turn the organisation’s security direction into clear requirements for specific areas and users. It also aims to ensure people know, understand and agree to follow the policies that apply to them.',N'Keep policies suitable, adequate, effective and aligned with changing needs. Turn the organisation’s security direction into clear requirements for specific areas and users; Ensure people know, understand and agree to follow the policies that apply to them.',N'topic-specific policy; access control; backup; incident; cryptography; classification; secure development; publication; communication; accessibility; acknowledgement; interested parties; confidentiality; policy review',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(6,2,N'5.2',N'ROL-01',N'Define the security role structure',N'The organisation must define and document the information security roles needed to implement, operate and manage information security. It must align the structure with the main security policy and supporting topic-specific policies. It must define authority and delegation. It must maintain role competence and awareness. The purpose is to create a clear and approved structure for managing information security. It also aims to make security decisions, delegation and accountability clear and controlled. It also aims to ensure security responsibilities are understood and performed by competent people.',N'Create a clear and approved structure for managing information security. Make security decisions, delegation and accountability clear and controlled; Ensure security responsibilities are understood and performed by competent people.',N'security roles; role structure; governance; policy alignment; accountability; authority level; delegation; task verification; approval; competence; skills; role communication; training; professional development',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(7,2,N'5.2',N'ROL-02',N'Allocate security responsibilities',N'The organisation must assign responsibility for protecting information and assets, operating security processes, and ensuring that all personnel follow their security duties. It must add site-specific or facility-specific guidance where needed. It must assign risk and asset ownership. The purpose is to ensure every important security activity and asset has a responsible role. It also aims to place security risks and assets under clear ownership and decision authority.',N'Ensure every important security activity and asset has a responsible role. Place security risks and assets under clear ownership and decision authority.',N'responsibility allocation; asset protection; security process; personnel duties; site guidance; risk owner; residual risk; risk acceptance; asset owner; protection',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(8,2,N'5.2',N'ROL-03',N'Assign risk and asset ownership',N'The organisation must assign owners for information security risks, residual-risk acceptance and the day-to-day protection of important information and other assets. The purpose is to place security risks and assets under clear ownership and decision authority.',N'Place security risks and assets under clear ownership and decision authority.',N'risk owner; residual risk; risk acceptance; asset owner; protection',1,N'Merged into ROL-02 — Merged'),
(9,2,N'5.2',N'ROL-04',N'Define authority and delegation',N'The organisation must document each role’s security area and authority level. Allow tasks to be delegated only while the assigned role remains accountable and checks that the work was completed correctly. The purpose is to make security decisions, delegation and accountability clear and controlled.',N'Make security decisions, delegation and accountability clear and controlled.',N'authority level; delegation; accountability; task verification; approval',1,N'Merged into ROL-01 — Merged'),
(10,2,N'5.2',N'ROL-05',N'Maintain role competence and awareness',N'The organisation must assign security roles to people with the required knowledge and skills. Communicate responsibilities and support role holders in keeping their knowledge current. The purpose is to ensure security responsibilities are understood and performed by competent people.',N'Ensure security responsibilities are understood and performed by competent people.',N'competence; skills; role communication; training; professional development',1,N'Merged into ROL-01 — Merged'),
(11,3,N'6.1',N'PR-HR-01',N'Perform Personnel Background Screening',N'The organisation must define checks required to confirm the identity, history and suitability of personnel before engagement. The purpose is to engage only personnel whose identity, background and qualifications have been appropriately verified.',N'Engage only personnel whose identity, background and qualifications have been appropriately verified.',N'personnel screening, background check, identity, references, qualifications',1,N'Merged into PR-HR-02 — Merged'),
(12,3,N'6.1',N'PR-HR-02',N'Manage Third-Party Personnel Screening',N'The organisation must defines screening controls for supplier and third-party personnel who may access company information or systems. It must perform Personnel Background Screening. It must conduct Legally Compliant Screening. It must perform Periodic Re-Screening. The purpose is to ensure supplier personnel meet equivalent screening and compliance requirements. It also aims to engage only personnel whose identity, background and qualifications have been appropriately verified. It also aims to meet applicable legal, privacy, consent and notification requirements during screening. It also aims to keep personnel trust and access decisions current as risks or roles change.',N'Ensure supplier personnel meet equivalent screening and compliance requirements. Engage only personnel whose identity, background and qualifications have been appropriately verified; Meet applicable legal, privacy, consent and notification requirements during screening; Keep personnel trust and access decisions current as risks or roles change.',N'personnel screening; background check; identity; references; qualifications; third party; supplier personnel; contract; compliance; screening; legal compliance; privacy; consent; candidate notice',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(13,3,N'6.1',N'PR-HR-03',N'Conduct Legally Compliant Screening',N'The organisation must ensure personnel screening is performed lawfully, fairly and with required candidate communication. The purpose is to meet applicable legal, privacy, consent and notification requirements during screening.',N'Meet applicable legal, privacy, consent and notification requirements during screening.',N'legal compliance, privacy, consent, candidate notice, screening',1,N'Merged into PR-HR-02 — Merged'),
(14,3,N'6.1',N'PR-HR-04',N'Assess Suitability for Information Security Roles',N'The organisation must assesses whether personnel assigned to information-security roles are competent and trustworthy. The purpose is to assign security responsibilities only to personnel with suitable competence and trustworthiness.',N'Assign security responsibilities only to personnel with suitable competence and trustworthiness.',N'security roles; competence; suitability; trustworthiness; role assignment',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(15,3,N'6.1',N'PR-HR-05',N'Perform Enhanced Verification for Sensitive Access Roles',N'The organisation must apply enhanced checks before granting sensitive, privileged or high-risk access. The purpose is to reduce access risk by completing additional verification before sensitive access is approved.',N'Reduce access risk by completing additional verification before sensitive access is approved.',N'sensitive access, privileged role, enhanced verification, access approval',1,N'Merged into PR-HR-07 — Merged'),
(16,3,N'6.1',N'PR-HR-06',N'Manage Verification Procedures',N'The organisation must establish consistent screening methods, criteria and authorized responsibilities. The purpose is to maintain a documented and controlled personnel-verification process.',N'Maintain a documented and controlled personnel-verification process.',N'screening procedure, methodology, criteria, authorization, governance',1,N'Merged into PR-HR-07 — Merged'),
(17,3,N'6.1',N'PR-HR-07',N'Apply Mitigating Controls for Incomplete Verification',N'The organisation must defines temporary safeguards when verification is incomplete or delayed. It must perform Enhanced Verification for Sensitive Access Roles. It must manage Verification Procedures. The purpose is to prevent unverified personnel from receiving uncontrolled access while checks remain pending. It also aims to reduce access risk by completing additional verification before sensitive access is approved. It also aims to maintain a documented and controlled personnel-verification process.',N'Prevent unverified personnel from receiving uncontrolled access while checks remain pending. Reduce access risk by completing additional verification before sensitive access is approved; Maintain a documented and controlled personnel-verification process.',N'sensitive access; privileged role; enhanced verification; access approval; screening procedure; methodology; criteria; authorization; governance; pending verification; temporary controls; restricted access; risk mitigation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(18,3,N'6.1',N'PR-HR-08',N'Perform Periodic Re-Screening',N'The organisation must define periodic and event-based reassessment of personnel suitability. The purpose is to keep personnel trust and access decisions current as risks or roles change.',N'Keep personnel trust and access decisions current as risks or roles change.',N're-screening, periodic review, role change, reassessment, personnel risk',1,N'Merged into PR-HR-02 — Merged'),
(19,4,N'5.3',N'SOD-01',N'Identify conflicting duties',N'The organisation must identify duties and responsibility areas that could allow one person to cause or hide fraud, error or control bypass. It must document the conflict, affected process, risk and required separation. It must apply alternative controls. The purpose is to maintain a clear view of activities that must not be performed by one person alone. It also aims to reduce the remaining risk when duties cannot be fully separated.',N'Maintain a clear view of activities that must not be performed by one person alone. Reduce the remaining risk when duties cannot be fully separated.',N'conflicting duties; conflict register; fraud; error; control bypass; risk; compensating control; monitoring; audit trail; supervision; collusion; exception',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(20,4,N'5.3',N'SOD-02',N'Separate critical activities',N'The organisation must assign different people to conflicting steps such as requesting, approving and implementing access. It must initiating, approving and executing changes. It must and designing, building and reviewing code or controls. It must prevent conflicting access roles. It must review and correct conflicts. The purpose is to prevent one person from controlling an entire sensitive transaction or process. It also aims to stop access combinations that allow unauthorised or unreviewed activity. It also aims to keep segregation effective as people, systems and responsibilities change.',N'Prevent one person from controlling an entire sensitive transaction or process. Stop access combinations that allow unauthorised or unreviewed activity; Keep segregation effective as people, systems and responsibilities change.',N'request; approval; execution; change; access; code; independent review; role-based access; toxic combination; application; database; production; administration; access review',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(21,4,N'5.3',N'SOD-03',N'Prevent conflicting access roles',N'The organisation must define roles carefully and prevent users from receiving incompatible application, database, development, production, administration or assurance roles. The purpose is to stop access combinations that allow unauthorised or unreviewed activity.',N'Stop access combinations that allow unauthorised or unreviewed activity.',N'role-based access; toxic combination; application; database; production; administration',1,N'Merged into SOD-02 — Merged'),
(22,4,N'5.3',N'SOD-04',N'Apply alternative controls',N'The organisation must when full separation is not practical, document the reason and apply approved alternatives such as activity monitoring, audit trails, independent review and management supervision. Consider the risk of collusion. The purpose is to reduce the remaining risk when duties cannot be fully separated.',N'Reduce the remaining risk when duties cannot be fully separated.',N'compensating control; monitoring; audit trail; supervision; collusion; exception',1,N'Merged into SOD-01 — Merged'),
(23,4,N'5.3',N'SOD-05',N'Review and correct conflicts',N'The organisation must review duty assignments and access roles regularly and after role changes. Remove conflicts promptly, verify corrections and retain evidence of approved exceptions. The purpose is to keep segregation effective as people, systems and responsibilities change.',N'Keep segregation effective as people, systems and responsibilities change.',N'access review; role change; conflict removal; remediation; exception review',1,N'Merged into SOD-02 — Merged'),
(24,5,N'5.4',N'MGT-01',N'Set management security expectations',N'The organisation must managers should visibly support information security and require personnel to follow the organisation’s security policies, topic-specific policies and procedures. The purpose is to make management direction and expected security behaviour clear.',N'Make management direction and expected security behaviour clear.',N'management support; security expectations; policies; procedures; role model',1,N'Merged into MGT-03 — Merged'),
(25,5,N'5.4',N'MGT-02',N'Brief personnel before access',N'The organisation must explain security roles, responsibilities, acceptable behaviour and working methods before people receive access to information or other assets. It must provide security resources and time. The purpose is to ensure people understand their security duties before they begin work or receive access. It also aims to prevent security work from failing because of inadequate resources or planning.',N'Ensure people understand their security duties before they begin work or receive access. Prevent security work from failing because of inadequate resources or planning.',N'briefing; responsibilities; acceptable use; access; onboarding; resources; budget; staffing; tools; project time; security controls',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(26,5,N'5.4',N'MGT-03',N'Maintain awareness and competence — Management responsibilities',N'The organisation must ensure personnel receive suitable awareness, guidance, training and ongoing support, and maintain the knowledge and skills needed for their security responsibilities. It must set management security expectations. It must monitor compliance and support reporting. The purpose is to help personnel perform their security duties correctly and confidently. It also aims to make management direction and expected security behaviour clear. It also aims to detect and correct security failures while enabling safe reporting of concerns.',N'Help personnel perform their security duties correctly and confidently. Make management direction and expected security behaviour clear; Detect and correct security failures while enabling safe reporting of concerns.',N'management support; security expectations; policies; procedures; role model; awareness; training; guidance; competence; skills; support; compliance; supervision; violation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(27,5,N'5.4',N'MGT-04',N'Provide security resources and time',N'The organisation must provide the people, funding, tools and project time needed to implement and operate information security processes and controls. The purpose is to prevent security work from failing because of inadequate resources or planning.',N'Prevent security work from failing because of inadequate resources or planning.',N'resources; budget; staffing; tools; project time; security controls',1,N'Merged into MGT-02 — Merged'),
(28,5,N'5.4',N'MGT-05',N'Monitor compliance and support reporting',N'The organisation must monitor whether personnel meet their security responsibilities, address non-compliance and provide a confidential way to report suspected policy or security violations where possible. The purpose is to detect and correct security failures while enabling safe reporting of concerns.',N'Detect and correct security failures while enabling safe reporting of concerns.',N'compliance; supervision; violation; confidential reporting; corrective action',1,N'Merged into MGT-03 — Merged'),
(29,6,N'5.5',N'AUT-01',N'Identify and maintain authority contacts',N'The organisation must identify relevant legal, regulatory, supervisory, law-enforcement, emergency and utility authorities. Keep accurate contact details and reasons for contact. The purpose is to ensure the correct authority can be reached quickly when needed.',N'Ensure the correct authority can be reached quickly when needed.',N'authorities; regulator; law enforcement; emergency; utilities; contact register',1,N'Merged into AUT-02 — Merged'),
(30,6,N'5.5',N'AUT-02',N'Define authority contact responsibilities',N'The organisation must document who is authorised to contact each authority, the approval route and alternate contacts. It must identify and maintain authority contacts. It must use authority contacts for readiness and response. It must review and test authority arrangements. The purpose is to make external authority communication controlled and accountable. It also aims to ensure the correct authority can be reached quickly when needed. It also aims to improve incident response, continuity and preparation for regulatory change. It also aims to keep authority contact arrangements current and ready for use.',N'Make external authority communication controlled and accountable. Ensure the correct authority can be reached quickly when needed; Improve incident response, continuity and preparation for regulatory change; Keep authority contact arrangements current and ready for use.',N'authorities; regulator; law enforcement; emergency; utilities; contact register; authorised contact; responsibility; approval; alternate contact; escalation; incident response; attack; continuity',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(31,6,N'5.5',N'AUT-03',N'Define reporting triggers and timelines',N'The organisation must document which security incidents and events require authority contact, how they must be reported and the required reporting time. The purpose is to support complete and timely reporting to authorities.',N'Support complete and timely reporting to authorities.',N'reporting trigger; incident; notification; timeline; regulatory reporting',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(32,6,N'5.5',N'AUT-04',N'Use authority contacts for readiness and response',N'The organisation must include authority contact in incident, continuity and recovery plans. Use contacts to request help during attacks and understand current or upcoming requirements. The purpose is to improve incident response, continuity and preparation for regulatory change.',N'Improve incident response, continuity and preparation for regulatory change.',N'incident response; attack; continuity; recovery; regulatory change; assistance',1,N'Merged into AUT-02 — Merged'),
(33,6,N'5.5',N'AUT-05',N'Review and test authority arrangements',N'The organisation must review contact details, reporting duties and assigned contacts regularly and after changes. Test that response teams can use the process. The purpose is to keep authority contact arrangements current and ready for use.',N'Keep authority contact arrangements current and ready for use.',N'review; contact test; exercise; reporting duty; improvement',1,N'Merged into AUT-02 — Merged'),
(34,7,N'5.6',N'SIG-01',N'Identify relevant security groups',N'The organisation must identify special interest groups, specialist security forums and professional associations that match the organisation’s technologies, services, sector, locations and risks. The purpose is to connect with groups that provide useful and relevant security knowledge.',N'Connect with groups that provide useful and relevant security knowledge.',N'special interest group; security forum; professional association; relevance; membership',1,N'Merged into SIG-05 — Merged'),
(35,7,N'5.6',N'SIG-02',N'Maintain group contacts and participation',N'The organisation must assign owners for memberships and liaison contacts. Keep membership, contact details, access and participation arrangements current. The purpose is to maintain reliable access to selected security communities and specialists.',N'Maintain reliable access to selected security communities and specialists.',N'membership; liaison; contact; participation; owner; renewal',1,N'Merged into SIG-05 — Merged'),
(36,7,N'5.6',N'SIG-03',N'Use security updates and specialist advice',N'The organisation must receive and review best practices, alerts, advisories, patches and specialist advice, and send relevant items to responsible teams for action. The purpose is to keep security knowledge current and act on useful warnings and advice.',N'Keep security knowledge current and act on useful warnings and advice.',N'best practice; alert; advisory; patch; specialist advice; action',1,N'Merged into SIG-05 — Merged'),
(37,7,N'5.6',N'SIG-04',N'Exchange information safely',N'The organisation must share information about technologies, products, services, threats and vulnerabilities only through approved contacts and with suitable confidentiality and disclosure controls. The purpose is to gain value from information exchange without exposing sensitive information.',N'Gain value from information exchange without exposing sensitive information.',N'information sharing; technology; threat; vulnerability; confidentiality; approval',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(38,7,N'5.6',N'SIG-05',N'Use specialist contacts for incidents',N'The organisation must maintain suitable liaison points for incident support and periodically review whether memberships, contacts and received information remain useful. It must identify relevant security groups. It must maintain group contacts and participation. It must use security updates and specialist advice. The purpose is to improve incident response and keep external security relationships effective. It also aims to connect with groups that provide useful and relevant security knowledge. It also aims to maintain reliable access to selected security communities and specialists. It also aims to keep security knowledge current and act on useful warnings and advice.',N'Improve incident response and keep external security relationships effective. Connect with groups that provide useful and relevant security knowledge; Maintain reliable access to selected security communities and specialists; Keep security knowledge current and act on useful warnings and advice.',N'special interest group; security forum; professional association; relevance; membership; liaison; contact; participation; owner; renewal; best practice; alert; advisory; patch',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(39,8,N'5.7',N'THR-01',N'Govern threat intelligence',N'The organisation must define the purpose, scope, objectives, responsibilities and expected outputs for threat-intelligence activities so they support prevention, detection and response. It must communicate threat intelligence. It must use intelligence in security activities. It must share and improve threat intelligence. The purpose is to provide clear direction and ownership for producing and using threat intelligence. It also aims to ensure decision-makers and operational teams can understand and use the intelligence. It also aims to turn intelligence into actions that prevent harm or reduce its impact. It also aims to improve collective awareness and maintain effective threat-intelligence activities.',N'Provide clear direction and ownership for producing and using threat intelligence. Ensure decision-makers and operational teams can understand and use the intelligence; Turn intelligence into actions that prevent harm or reduce its impact; Improve collective awareness and maintain effective threat-intelligence activities.',N'objectives; scope; ownership; governance; prevention; detection; response; communication; audience; report; timely; understandable; handling; risk management',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(40,8,N'5.7',N'THR-02',N'Cover all intelligence levels',N'The organisation must consider strategic intelligence about the changing threat landscape, tactical intelligence about attacker methods and tools, and operational intelligence about specific attacks and technical indicators. The purpose is to maintain a complete view of threats from business-level trends to attack details.',N'Maintain a complete view of threats from business-level trends to attack details.',N'strategic; tactical; operational; attacker; attack method; indicator',1,N'Merged into THR-05 — Merged'),
(41,8,N'5.7',N'THR-03',N'Select and manage intelligence sources',N'The organisation must identify, assess and select suitable internal and external sources, including providers, advisers, government agencies and collaborative groups. The purpose is to use reliable sources that provide the information needed by the organisation.',N'Use reliable sources that provide the information needed by the organisation.',N'source; vetting; provider; government; internal; external; reliability',1,N'Merged into THR-05 — Merged'),
(42,8,N'5.7',N'THR-04',N'Collect and prepare threat information',N'The organisation must collect information from approved sources and prepare it for analysis through translation, formatting, normalisation and corroboration. The purpose is to provide analysts with complete and usable threat information.',N'Provide analysts with complete and usable threat information.',N'collection; translation; formatting; normalisation; corroboration; preparation',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(43,8,N'5.7',N'THR-05',N'Analyse and quality-check intelligence',N'The organisation must analyse threats in relation to the organisation and ensure intelligence is relevant, insightful, contextual and actionable. It must cover all intelligence levels. It must select and manage intelligence sources. The purpose is to produce accurate intelligence that explains the threat and supports timely action. It also aims to maintain a complete view of threats from business-level trends to attack details. It also aims to use reliable sources that provide the information needed by the organisation.',N'Produce accurate intelligence that explains the threat and supports timely action. Maintain a complete view of threats from business-level trends to attack details; Use reliable sources that provide the information needed by the organisation.',N'strategic; tactical; operational; attacker; attack method; indicator; source; vetting; provider; government; internal; external; reliability; analysis',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(44,8,N'5.7',N'THR-06',N'Communicate threat intelligence',N'The organisation must provide relevant intelligence to the right people in a clear, understandable and timely format, with suitable handling controls. The purpose is to ensure decision-makers and operational teams can understand and use the intelligence.',N'Ensure decision-makers and operational teams can understand and use the intelligence.',N'communication; audience; report; timely; understandable; handling',1,N'Merged into THR-01 — Merged'),
(45,8,N'5.7',N'THR-07',N'Use intelligence in security activities',N'The organisation must use threat intelligence in risk management, technical preventive and detective controls, security testing and incident activities. The purpose is to turn intelligence into actions that prevent harm or reduce its impact.',N'Turn intelligence into actions that prevent harm or reduce its impact.',N'risk management; firewall; intrusion detection; anti-malware; testing; incident',1,N'Merged into THR-01 — Merged'),
(46,8,N'5.7',N'THR-08',N'Share and improve threat intelligence',N'The organisation must share appropriate threat intelligence with other organisations on a mutual basis and regularly review the sources, products and actions for usefulness and improvement. The purpose is to improve collective awareness and maintain effective threat-intelligence activities.',N'Improve collective awareness and maintain effective threat-intelligence activities.',N'mutual sharing; collaboration; review; effectiveness; improvement; lessons',1,N'Merged into THR-01 — Merged'),
(47,9,N'5.8',N'ISPM-01',N'Govern project security',N'The organisation must include security in the project method, plan, stage gates and decisions. Assign named owners for security work, approvals and escalation. The purpose is to make security part of every project from start to closure, with clear accountability.',N'Make security part of every project from start to closure, with clear accountability.',N'governance; project plan; stage gates; roles; accountability',1,N'Merged into ISPM-02 — Merged'),
(48,9,N'5.8',N'ISPM-02',N'Manage project security risks',N'The organisation must assess security risks early, review them during the project and after major changes, and track treatment actions and remaining risk. It must govern project security. It must protect project communications. It must test and approve security. The purpose is to find and address security risks throughout the project life cycle. It also aims to make security part of every project from start to closure, with clear accountability. It also aims to prevent project information from being lost, exposed or shared with the wrong people. It also aims to release or close the project only when security is effective and remaining risk is accepted.',N'Find and address security risks throughout the project life cycle. Make security part of every project from start to closure, with clear accountability; Prevent project information from being lost, exposed or shared with the wrong people; Release or close the project only when security is effective and remaining risk is accepted.',N'governance; project plan; stage gates; roles; accountability; risk assessment; risk treatment; change; residual risk; tracking; communications; collaboration; information transfer; documents',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(49,9,N'5.8',N'ISPM-03',N'Define security requirements',N'The organisation must set security requirements during planning and design. It must cover information classification, confidentiality, integrity, availability, laws, contracts, logging and business needs. The purpose is to build the right protection into the product or service before delivery.',N'Build the right protection into the product or service before delivery.',N'security requirements; classification; CIA; compliance; logging; design',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(50,9,N'5.8',N'ISPM-04',N'Control access and user duties',N'The organisation must define identity checks, access approval, privileged access, access review and removal. Tell project members, users, operations teams and suppliers about their security duties. The purpose is to give access only to approved people and make responsibilities clear.',N'Give access only to approved people and make responsibilities clear.',N'identity; access approval; privileged access; access removal; responsibilities',1,N'Merged into ISPM-07 — Merged'),
(51,9,N'5.8',N'ISPM-05',N'Protect project communications',N'The organisation must protect project documents, collaboration spaces and internal or external information exchanges by using approved sharing methods and access settings. The purpose is to prevent project information from being lost, exposed or shared with the wrong people.',N'Prevent project information from being lost, exposed or shared with the wrong people.',N'communications; collaboration; information transfer; documents; confidentiality',1,N'Merged into ISPM-02 — Merged'),
(52,9,N'5.8',N'ISPM-06',N'Manage supplier security',N'The organisation must check supplier security before engagement, include clear security terms in agreements and confirm suppliers meet them during the project. The purpose is to ensure third parties protect project information and services as required.',N'Ensure third parties protect project information and services as required.',N'supplier; third party; due diligence; contract; assurance',1,N'Merged into ISPM-07 — Merged'),
(53,9,N'5.8',N'ISPM-07',N'Plan for incidents and continuity',N'The organisation must use threat reviews, incident lessons, vulnerability limits and contingency planning to make project deliverables resilient. It must control access and user duties. It must manage supplier security. The purpose is to prepare the project and its deliverables for security events and disruption. It also aims to give access only to approved people and make responsibilities clear. It also aims to ensure third parties protect project information and services as required.',N'Prepare the project and its deliverables for security events and disruption. Give access only to approved people and make responsibilities clear; Ensure third parties protect project information and services as required.',N'identity; access approval; privileged access; access removal; responsibilities; supplier; third party; due diligence; contract; assurance; threat review; incident; vulnerability; contingency',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(54,9,N'5.8',N'ISPM-08',N'Test and approve security',N'The organisation must at planned stages and before go-live or closure, check that security requirements and risk treatments work, resolve gaps and keep approval evidence. The purpose is to release or close the project only when security is effective and remaining risk is accepted.',N'Release or close the project only when security is effective and remaining risk is accepted.',N'security testing; assurance; go-live; closure; evidence; risk acceptance',1,N'Merged into ISPM-02 — Merged'),
(55,10,N'5.9',N'AST-01',N'Identify information and associated assets',N'The organisation must identify organisational information and other associated assets and determine their importance to information security. The purpose is to ensure assets requiring protection are known and prioritised.',N'Ensure assets requiring protection are known and prioritised.',N'information asset; associated asset; identification; importance; security value',1,N'Merged into AST-06 — Merged'),
(56,10,N'5.9',N'AST-02',N'Maintain suitable asset inventories',N'The organisation must record assets in dedicated or existing inventories, including location where appropriate, and coordinate the inventories maintained by relevant functions. The purpose is to maintain usable records covering all important asset types and locations.',N'Maintain usable records covering all important asset types and locations.',N'asset inventory; location; hardware; software; virtual machine; facility; record',1,N'Merged into AST-05 — Merged'),
(57,10,N'5.9',N'AST-03',N'Keep inventories accurate and current',N'The organisation must keep inventories accurate, up to date, consistent and aligned with other inventories through regular review and updates when assets are installed, changed or removed. The purpose is to ensure inventory information reflects the assets that actually exist.',N'Ensure inventory information reflects the assets that actually exist.',N'accuracy; current; consistency; reconciliation; install; change; removal',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(58,10,N'5.9',N'AST-04',N'Set classification and inventory detail',N'The organisation must identify asset classification based on associated information and maintain inventory detail at a level suitable for organisational needs, including short-lived assets where practical. The purpose is to apply suitable protection and maintain useful inventory detail.',N'Apply suitable protection and maintain useful inventory detail.',N'classification; granularity; short-lived asset; information life cycle; protection',1,N'Merged into AST-06 — Merged'),
(59,10,N'5.9',N'AST-05',N'Assign and maintain asset ownership',N'The organisation must assign each asset to an individual or group when created or transferred, and reassign ownership promptly when owners leave or change roles. It must maintain suitable asset inventories. It must control asset use and access. It must link dependencies, risks and accountability. The purpose is to keep every asset under clear and current accountability. It also aims to maintain usable records covering all important asset types and locations. It also aims to ensure assets are used and accessed only as permitted by their sensitivity. It also aims to preserve complete asset relationships, risk ownership and accountability.',N'Keep every asset under clear and current accountability. Maintain usable records covering all important asset types and locations; Ensure assets are used and accessed only as permitted by their sensitivity; Preserve complete asset relationships, risk ownership and accountability.',N'asset inventory; location; hardware; software; virtual machine; facility; record; asset owner; assignment; transfer; role change; leaver; accountability; acceptable use',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(60,10,N'5.9',N'AST-06',N'Manage assets through their life cycle',N'The organisation must require asset owners to ensure assets are inventoried, classified, protected, periodically reviewed and securely removed from inventories when deleted or disposed. It must identify information and associated assets. It must set classification and inventory detail. The purpose is to manage assets securely from creation or receipt through disposal. It also aims to ensure assets requiring protection are known and prioritised. It also aims to apply suitable protection and maintain useful inventory detail.',N'Manage assets securely from creation or receipt through disposal. Ensure assets requiring protection are known and prioritised; Apply suitable protection and maintain useful inventory detail.',N'information asset; associated asset; identification; importance; security value; classification; granularity; short-lived asset; information life cycle; protection; life cycle; review; deletion; disposal',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(61,10,N'5.9',N'AST-07',N'Control asset use and access',N'The organisation must require owners to establish acceptable-use requirements and ensure access restrictions match the asset classification and are periodically reviewed. The purpose is to ensure assets are used and accessed only as permitted by their sensitivity.',N'Ensure assets are used and accessed only as permitted by their sensitivity.',N'acceptable use; access restriction; classification; access review; owner',1,N'Merged into AST-05 — Merged'),
(62,10,N'5.9',N'AST-08',N'Link dependencies, risks and accountability',N'The organisation must link supporting technology components, involve owners in asset risks, support custodians and information managers, and retain owner or service-owner accountability when tasks are delegated. The purpose is to preserve complete asset relationships, risk ownership and accountability.',N'Preserve complete asset relationships, risk ownership and accountability.',N'dependency; component; risk; custodian; delegation; service owner; support',1,N'Merged into AST-05 — Merged'),
(63,11,N'5.10',N'USE-01',N'Establish acceptable-use rules',N'The organisation must identify, document and implement rules and procedures for the acceptable use and handling of information and other associated assets. It must define acceptable-use policy content. The purpose is to provide clear and enforceable direction for protecting, using and handling assets. It also aims to make acceptable and unacceptable conduct clear and transparent.',N'Provide clear and enforceable direction for protecting, using and handling assets. Make acceptable and unacceptable conduct clear and transparent.',N'acceptable use; handling; rules; procedures; implementation; behaviour; permitted use; prohibited use; monitoring; policy',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(64,11,N'5.10',N'USE-02',N'Communicate responsibilities to users',N'The organisation must make personnel and external-party users aware of protection and handling requirements and their responsibility for using information-processing facilities. It must control access and authorised users. It must protect copies, storage and media. It must control external and collaborative assets. The purpose is to ensure every user understands and accepts their security responsibilities. It also aims to limit use and access to people with approved and appropriate authority. It also aims to preserve protection when information is copied, stored or transported on media. It also aims to maintain protection when assets are externally owned, hosted or shared.',N'Ensure every user understands and accepts their security responsibilities. Limit use and access to people with approved and appropriate authority; Preserve protection when information is copied, stored or transported on media; Maintain protection when assets are externally owned, hosted or shared.',N'awareness; personnel; external party; responsibility; information processing facility; access restriction; authorised user; classification; access record; approval; copy; storage; manufacturer; media marking',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(65,11,N'5.10',N'USE-03',N'Define acceptable-use policy content',N'The organisation must state expected and unacceptable behaviour, permitted and prohibited use, and the monitoring activities performed by the organisation. The purpose is to make acceptable and unacceptable conduct clear and transparent.',N'Make acceptable and unacceptable conduct clear and transparent.',N'behaviour; permitted use; prohibited use; monitoring; policy',1,N'Merged into USE-01 — Merged'),
(66,11,N'5.10',N'USE-04',N'Manage use through the information life cycle',N'The organisation must define handling procedures for the full information life cycle according to classification and identified risks. It must authorise disposal and deletion. The purpose is to apply suitable protection from creation or receipt through deletion and disposal. It also aims to prevent unauthorised or insecure destruction and disposal.',N'Apply suitable protection from creation or receipt through deletion and disposal. Prevent unauthorised or insecure destruction and disposal.',N'information life cycle; classification; risk; handling; protection; disposal; deletion; authorisation; method; evidence',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(67,11,N'5.10',N'USE-05',N'Control access and authorised users',N'The organisation must apply access restrictions for each classification level and maintain records of authorised users of information and associated assets. The purpose is to limit use and access to people with approved and appropriate authority.',N'Limit use and access to people with approved and appropriate authority.',N'access restriction; authorised user; classification; access record; approval',1,N'Merged into USE-02 — Merged'),
(68,11,N'5.10',N'USE-06',N'Protect copies, storage and media',N'The organisation must protect temporary and permanent copies like the originals, store associated assets according to manufacturer requirements, and clearly mark storage media for authorised recipients. The purpose is to preserve protection when information is copied, stored or transported on media.',N'Preserve protection when information is copied, stored or transported on media.',N'copy; storage; manufacturer; media marking; authorised recipient',1,N'Merged into USE-02 — Merged'),
(69,11,N'5.10',N'USE-07',N'Authorise disposal and deletion',N'The organisation must require authorised disposal and use supported deletion methods for information and other associated assets. The purpose is to prevent unauthorised or insecure destruction and disposal.',N'Prevent unauthorised or insecure destruction and disposal.',N'disposal; deletion; authorisation; method; evidence',1,N'Merged into USE-04 — Merged'),
(70,11,N'5.10',N'USE-08',N'Control external and collaborative assets',N'The organisation must identify and control the use of third-party assets and organisational assets linked to them, including cloud services and collaborative working environments. The purpose is to maintain protection when assets are externally owned, hosted or shared.',N'Maintain protection when assets are externally owned, hosted or shared.',N'third party; cloud service; collaborative environment; agreement; external asset',1,N'Merged into USE-02 — Merged'),
(71,12,N'5.11',N'RET-01',N'Formalise the asset-return process',N'The organisation must include asset return in formal employment, contract and agreement change or termination processes for personnel and other interested parties. The purpose is to make asset return a required and controlled part of every relevant change or exit.',N'Make asset return a required and controlled part of every relevant change or exit.',N'return process; employment change; termination; contract; agreement',1,N'Merged into RET-02 — Merged'),
(72,12,N'5.11',N'RET-02',N'Identify assets to be returned',N'The organisation must clearly identify and document all organisational information and associated assets held by each person or party, including issued physical and electronic assets. It must formalise the asset-return process. It must control information that cannot be returned. The purpose is to know exactly what must be returned before a change or termination is completed. It also aims to make asset return a required and controlled part of every relevant change or exit. It also aims to protect information that remains outside organisation-owned assets.',N'Know exactly what must be returned before a change or termination is completed. Make asset return a required and controlled part of every relevant change or exit; Protect information that remains outside organisation-owned assets.',N'return process; employment change; termination; contract; agreement; asset list; issued asset; physical asset; electronic asset; reconciliation; non-owned asset; access rights; cryptography; residual information',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(73,12,N'5.11',N'RET-03',N'Recover and verify returned assets',N'The organisation must recover endpoint devices, portable media, specialist equipment, authentication hardware, physical information and other entrusted assets, and verify their return. The purpose is to restore organisational control of all returnable assets.',N'Restore organisational control of all returnable assets.',N'endpoint; portable media; specialist equipment; token; key; physical copy',1,N'Merged into RET-04 — Merged'),
(74,12,N'5.11',N'RET-04',N'Recover information from equipment not returned',N'The organisation must for personal or purchased equipment, trace relevant information, transfer it to the organisation and securely delete it from the equipment. It must recover and verify returned assets. It must transfer important operational knowledge. The purpose is to protect organisational information when equipment will not be returned. It also aims to restore organisational control of all returnable assets. It also aims to preserve knowledge needed to continue operations.',N'Protect organisational information when equipment will not be returned. Restore organisational control of all returnable assets; Preserve knowledge needed to continue operations.',N'endpoint; portable media; specialist equipment; token; key; physical copy; personal equipment; purchased equipment; trace; transfer; secure deletion; knowledge transfer; documentation; ongoing operations',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(75,12,N'5.11',N'RET-05',N'Transfer important operational knowledge',N'The organisation must identify knowledge important to ongoing operations, document it and transfer it before responsibilities end or change. The purpose is to preserve knowledge needed to continue operations.',N'Preserve knowledge needed to continue operations.',N'knowledge transfer; documentation; ongoing operations; handover',1,N'Merged into RET-04 — Merged'),
(76,12,N'5.11',N'RET-06',N'Prevent unauthorised copying',N'The organisation must during the notice period and afterwards, prevent unauthorised copying of relevant information, including intellectual property. The purpose is to protect sensitive information from being copied during and after exit.',N'Protect sensitive information from being copied during and after exit.',N'notice period; unauthorised copying; intellectual property; monitoring',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(77,12,N'5.11',N'RET-07',N'Control information that cannot be returned',N'The organisation must when information remains on non-organisational assets, restrict its use through controls such as access-right removal or cryptography. The purpose is to protect information that remains outside organisation-owned assets.',N'Protect information that remains outside organisation-owned assets.',N'non-owned asset; access rights; cryptography; residual information',1,N'Merged into RET-02 — Merged'),
(78,13,N'5.12',N'CLS-01',N'Establish the classification policy and scheme',N'The organisation must define and communicate a topic-specific information-classification policy and a scheme that reflects organisational security needs. The purpose is to provide one approved basis for classifying information.',N'Provide one approved basis for classifying information.',N'classification policy; scheme; communication; security need; governance',1,N'Merged into CLS-08 — Merged'),
(79,13,N'5.12',N'CLS-02',N'Assess protection requirements',N'The organisation must classify information using confidentiality, integrity, availability, business, legal and relevant interested-party requirements. The purpose is to match classification and protection to the information’s actual needs.',N'Match classification and protection to the information’s actual needs.',N'confidentiality; integrity; availability; business; legal; interested party',1,N'Merged into CLS-05 — Merged'),
(80,13,N'5.12',N'CLS-03',N'Assign classification accountability',N'The organisation must make information owners accountable for classification decisions and ensure associated assets inherit suitable classification from the information they handle or protect. The purpose is to keep classification decisions owned, recorded and consistently applied to related assets.',N'Keep classification decisions owned, recorded and consistently applied to related assets.',N'information owner; accountability; associated asset; inherited classification',1,N'Merged into CLS-08 — Merged'),
(81,13,N'5.12',N'CLS-04',N'Define meaningful classification levels',N'The organisation must define conventions, clear level names and impact-based criteria that suit organisational business needs and align with access-control requirements. The purpose is to make classification decisions understandable, repeatable and useful.',N'Make classification decisions understandable, repeatable and useful.',N'classification level; convention; impact; business need; access control',1,N'Merged into CLS-08 — Merged'),
(82,13,N'5.12',N'CLS-05',N'Apply classification consistently',N'The organisation must include the scheme in procedures and apply it consistently across the organisation so everyone understands and follows the same protection requirements. It must assess protection requirements. It must map external classification schemes. The purpose is to prevent inconsistent classification and protection across functions and systems. It also aims to match classification and protection to the information’s actual needs. It also aims to protect exchanged information correctly when classification schemes differ.',N'Prevent inconsistent classification and protection across functions and systems. Match classification and protection to the information’s actual needs; Protect exchanged information correctly when classification schemes differ.',N'confidentiality; integrity; availability; business; legal; interested party; consistency; procedure; common understanding; protection requirement; external scheme; information sharing; agreement; mapping',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(83,13,N'5.12',N'CLS-06',N'Review classification through the life cycle',N'The organisation must set review criteria and update classifications as information value, sensitivity, criticality or publication status changes over time. The purpose is to avoid both excessive and insufficient protection as information changes.',N'Avoid both excessive and insufficient protection as information changes.',N'life cycle; review; reclassification; value; sensitivity; criticality',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(84,13,N'5.12',N'CLS-07',N'Map external classification schemes',N'The organisation must include procedures in information-sharing agreements to identify and interpret other organisations’ classifications and map equivalent handling and protection. The purpose is to protect exchanged information correctly when classification schemes differ.',N'Protect exchanged information correctly when classification schemes differ.',N'external scheme; information sharing; agreement; mapping; equivalence',1,N'Merged into CLS-05 — Merged'),
(85,13,N'5.12',N'CLS-08',N'Assure classification effectiveness',N'The organisation must monitor classification accuracy, protective-control alignment, user understanding and correction of over-classification or under-classification. It must establish the classification policy and scheme. It must assign classification accountability. It must define meaningful classification levels. The purpose is to confirm the scheme produces suitable and cost-effective protection. It also aims to provide one approved basis for classifying information. It also aims to keep classification decisions owned, recorded and consistently applied to related assets. It also aims to make classification decisions understandable, repeatable and useful.',N'Confirm the scheme produces suitable and cost-effective protection. Provide one approved basis for classifying information; Keep classification decisions owned, recorded and consistently applied to related assets; Make classification decisions understandable, repeatable and useful.',N'classification policy; scheme; communication; security need; governance; information owner; accountability; associated asset; inherited classification; classification level; convention; impact; business need; access control',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(86,14,N'5.13',N'LBL-01',N'Establish information-labelling procedures',N'The organisation must develop, approve and implement labelling procedures aligned with the organisation’s information-classification scheme. It must manage omissions and technical limitations. It must maintain awareness and competence. The purpose is to provide consistent rules for communicating information classification. It also aims to control labelling exceptions without weakening information protection. It also aims to ensure people understand and apply labelling requirements.',N'Provide consistent rules for communicating information classification. Control labelling exceptions without weakening information protection; Ensure people understand and apply labelling requirements.',N'labelling procedure; classification scheme; approval; implementation; omission; exception; technical restriction; alternative control; awareness; training; interested party; correct labelling; handling',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(87,14,N'5.13',N'LBL-02',N'Cover all information and asset formats',N'The organisation must apply labelling procedures to information and associated assets in electronic, physical and other applicable formats. The purpose is to ensure classification remains visible regardless of format or storage medium.',N'Ensure classification remains visible regardless of format or storage medium.',N'electronic; physical; format; associated asset; storage media',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(88,14,N'5.13',N'LBL-03',N'Define recognisable labels and placement',N'The organisation must define approved, easily recognisable labels and explain where and how they are attached based on access, handling and media type. The purpose is to make classification labels visible, understandable and practical.',N'Make classification labels visible, understandable and practical.',N'recognisable label; placement; attachment; access; handling; media',1,N'Merged into LBL-06 — Merged'),
(89,14,N'5.13',N'LBL-04',N'Manage omissions and technical limitations',N'The organisation must define when labels may be omitted and how to protect information when labelling is not technically possible. The purpose is to control labelling exceptions without weakening information protection.',N'Control labelling exceptions without weakening information protection.',N'omission; exception; technical restriction; alternative control',1,N'Merged into LBL-01 — Merged'),
(90,14,N'5.13',N'LBL-05',N'Use metadata for digital information',N'The organisation must use metadata to identify, manage, control and find digital information and to enable systems to act on classification labels. The purpose is to support automated and reliable management of classified digital information.',N'Support automated and reliable management of classified digital information.',N'metadata; digital information; search; automation; classification',1,N'Merged into LBL-06 — Merged'),
(91,14,N'5.13',N'LBL-06',N'Align metadata and data handling',N'The organisation must define metadata attachment, label values and data-handling rules in line with the information model and technology architecture. It must define recognisable labels and placement. It must use metadata for digital information. It must label sensitive and critical system outputs. The purpose is to ensure classification metadata works consistently across systems and processes. It also aims to make classification labels visible, understandable and practical. It also aims to support automated and reliable management of classified digital information. It also aims to prevent classified output from being used or shared without clear protection instructions.',N'Ensure classification metadata works consistently across systems and processes. Make classification labels visible, understandable and practical; Support automated and reliable management of classified digital information; Prevent classified output from being used or shared without clear protection instructions.',N'recognisable label; placement; attachment; access; handling; media; metadata; digital information; search; automation; classification; metadata attachment; information model; ICT architecture',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(92,14,N'5.13',N'LBL-07',N'Maintain awareness and competence — Labelling of information',N'The organisation must make personnel and other interested parties aware of labelling procedures and train personnel to label and handle information correctly. The purpose is to ensure people understand and apply labelling requirements.',N'Ensure people understand and apply labelling requirements.',N'awareness; training; interested party; correct labelling; handling',1,N'Merged into LBL-01 — Merged'),
(93,14,N'5.13',N'LBL-08',N'Label sensitive and critical system outputs',N'The organisation must ensure system output containing sensitive or critical information carries the appropriate classification label and verify labelling effectiveness. The purpose is to prevent classified output from being used or shared without clear protection instructions.',N'Prevent classified output from being used or shared without clear protection instructions.',N'system output; sensitive; critical; label; assurance',1,N'Merged into LBL-06 — Merged'),
(94,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-01',N'Govern information transfer',N'The organisation must establish and communicate policy, rules, procedures and agreements for information transfers within the organisation and with external parties. It must maintain accountability and transfer governance. It must manage transfer records and obligations. It must review transfer effectiveness. The purpose is to provide one controlled framework for all information-transfer methods. It also aims to keep transfers attributable, understandable and recoverable. It also aims to meet information-governance and compliance duties for transfers. It also aims to keep transfer arrangements current and effective.',N'Provide one controlled framework for all information-transfer methods. Keep transfers attributable, understandable and recoverable; Meet information-governance and compliance duties for transfers; Keep transfer arrangements current and effective.',N'transfer policy; procedure; agreement; internal; external; traceability; non-repudiation; custody; contact; incident; label; reliability; acceptable use; retention',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(95,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-02',N'Apply classification and third-party agreements',N'The organisation must match transfer protection to information classification and maintain agreements, including recipient authentication, for third-party transfers. The purpose is to apply suitable protection and accountability to external transfers.',N'Apply suitable protection and accountability to external transfers.',N'classification; third party; agreement; recipient authentication',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(96,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-03',N'Protect information in transit',N'The organisation must protect transferred information against interception, unauthorised access, copying, modification, misrouting, destruction and denial of service. The purpose is to preserve confidentiality, integrity and availability during transfer.',N'Preserve confidentiality, integrity and availability during transfer.',N'interception; access; copying; modification; misrouting; destruction; denial',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(97,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-04',N'Maintain accountability and transfer governance',N'The organisation must ensure traceability, non-repudiation, chain of custody, responsible contacts, incident duties, labelling and reliable transfer services. The purpose is to keep transfers attributable, understandable and recoverable.',N'Keep transfers attributable, understandable and recoverable.',N'traceability; non-repudiation; custody; contact; incident; label; reliability',1,N'Merged into XFR-01 — Merged'),
(98,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-05',N'Manage transfer records and obligations',N'The organisation must define acceptable use, retention, disposal and applicable legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual requirements for transferred records and messages. The purpose is to meet information-governance and compliance duties for transfers.',N'Meet information-governance and compliance duties for transfers.',N'acceptable use; retention; disposal; law; regulation; contract; signature',1,N'Merged into XFR-01 — Merged'),
(99,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-06',N'Secure electronic transfers',N'The organisation must protect electronic communications against malware, attachment exposure, wrong recipients and unsafe public services, and apply suitable authentication and restrictions. The purpose is to reduce security risks in email, messaging, file-sharing, cloud and fax transfers.',N'Reduce security risks in email, messaging, file-sharing, cloud and fax transfers.',N'electronic transfer; malware; attachment; recipient; public service; authentication',1,N'Merged into XFR-08 — Merged'),
(100,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-07',N'Secure physical-media transfers',N'The organisation must control dispatch, transport, packaging, couriers, tamper protection, recipients and records for physical storage media and paper. The purpose is to protect and track physical information throughout transit.',N'Protect and track physical information throughout transit.',N'physical media; paper; packaging; courier; tamper; dispatch; receipt',1,N'Merged into XFR-08 — Merged'),
(101,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-08',N'Secure verbal transfers',N'The organisation must prevent confidential conversations and messages from being overheard or replayed and apply screening, room controls and sensitive-conversation notices. It must secure electronic transfers. It must secure physical-media transfers. The purpose is to protect information communicated verbally. It also aims to reduce security risks in email, messaging, file-sharing, cloud and fax transfers. It also aims to protect and track physical information throughout transit.',N'Protect information communicated verbally. Reduce security risks in email, messaging, file-sharing, cloud and fax transfers; Protect and track physical information throughout transit.',N'electronic transfer; malware; attachment; recipient; public service; authentication; physical media; paper; packaging; courier; tamper; dispatch; receipt; verbal',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(102,15,N'5.14',N'XFR-09',N'Review transfer effectiveness',N'The organisation must review transfer controls, agreements, incidents and user compliance, and correct failures. The purpose is to keep transfer arrangements current and effective.',N'Keep transfer arrangements current and effective.',N'review; test; incident; compliance; remediation',1,N'Merged into XFR-01 — Merged'),
(103,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-01',N'Govern access control',N'The organisation must define, approve, communicate and maintain access-control policy, rules and procedures based on business and information security needs. The purpose is to provide one clear and current framework for controlling physical and logical access.',N'Provide one clear and current framework for controlling physical and logical access.',N'access policy; rules; procedure; approval; communication; review',1,N'Merged into ACL-02 — Merged'),
(104,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-02',N'Determine access requirements',N'The organisation must identify asset owners, the human and technical entities that need access, the type of access required and the business reason for it. It must govern access control. It must authorize and administer access. It must restrict privileged access and segregate duties. The purpose is to grant access only where a documented business and security need exists. It also aims to provide one clear and current framework for controlling physical and logical access. It also aims to make every access grant, change and removal authorized, traceable and correctly implemented. It also aims to prevent one person or account from gaining unchecked control over critical access.',N'Grant access only where a documented business and security need exists. Provide one clear and current framework for controlling physical and logical access; Make every access grant, change and removal authorized, traceable and correctly implemented; Prevent one person or account from gaining unchecked control over critical access.',N'access policy; rules; procedure; approval; communication; review; asset owner; entity; access need; access type; justification; requirement; access request; authorization',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(105,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-03',N'Apply need-to-know, need-to-use and least privilege',N'The organisation must limit information and technology access to the minimum needed for assigned tasks, roles and approved business purposes, using a default-deny approach. The purpose is to prevent unnecessary access and reduce the impact of misuse or compromise.',N'Prevent unnecessary access and reduce the impact of misuse or compromise.',N'need-to-know; need-to-use; least privilege; default deny; role profile',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(106,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-04',N'Authorize and administer access',N'The organisation must use formal requests and approvals, separate requesting, authorizing and administering access, and keep rights aligned with approved decisions. The purpose is to make every access grant, change and removal authorized, traceable and correctly implemented.',N'Make every access grant, change and removal authorized, traceable and correctly implemented.',N'access request; authorization; administration; provisioning; change; removal',1,N'Merged into ACL-02 — Merged'),
(107,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-05',N'Align logical, application and physical access',N'The organisation must keep access rights consistent with information classification, application security and physical perimeter and entry-control requirements. It must apply classification, legal and contractual restrictions. It must log, monitor and review access. It must use risk-based dynamic and granular controls. The purpose is to prevent gaps between data, system and location protection. It also aims to prevent access that would breach handling rules or external duties. It also aims to detect unauthorized or incorrect access and keep controls effective. It also aims to apply stronger and more precise access decisions where the risk justifies them.',N'Prevent gaps between data, system and location protection. Prevent access that would breach handling rules or external duties; Detect unauthorized or incorrect access and keep controls effective; Apply stronger and more precise access decisions where the risk justifies them.',N'classification; application security; physical access; perimeter; alignment; dissemination; law; regulation; contract; access restriction; logging; monitoring; review; reconciliation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(108,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-06',N'Restrict privileged access and segregate duties',N'The organisation must apply tighter restrictions to privileged rights and separate conflicting access-control activities and sensitive duties. The purpose is to prevent one person or account from gaining unchecked control over critical access.',N'Prevent one person or account from gaining unchecked control over critical access.',N'privileged access; segregation; conflict; independent approval; administration',1,N'Merged into ACL-02 — Merged'),
(109,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-07',N'Control entities, roles and connections',N'The organisation must map rights and restrictions to human users, machines, devices and services, use roles where suitable, and cover every available connection in distributed environments. The purpose is to ensure every entity and connection reaches only approved information, networks and services.',N'Ensure every entity and connection reaches only approved information, networks and services.',N'human; machine; device; service; role; network; distributed connection',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(110,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-08',N'Apply classification, legal and contractual restrictions',N'The organisation must apply access and dissemination limits from information classification, legislation, regulation, contracts and other obligations. The purpose is to prevent access that would breach handling rules or external duties.',N'Prevent access that would breach handling rules or external duties.',N'classification; dissemination; law; regulation; contract; access restriction',1,N'Merged into ACL-05 — Merged'),
(111,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-09',N'Log, monitor and review access',N'The organisation must log access and access administration, compare actual rights with approvals, investigate anomalies and regularly review rules, rights and approvals. The purpose is to detect unauthorized or incorrect access and keep controls effective.',N'Detect unauthorized or incorrect access and keep controls effective.',N'logging; monitoring; review; reconciliation; anomaly; remediation',1,N'Merged into ACL-05 — Merged'),
(112,16,N'5.15',N'ACL-10',N'Use risk-based dynamic and granular controls',N'The organisation must select suitable access-control models and granularity, including dynamic factors such as role, attributes, location, connection and previous access, based on business need, risk and cost. The purpose is to apply stronger and more precise access decisions where the risk justifies them.',N'Apply stronger and more precise access decisions where the risk justifies them.',N'RBAC; ABAC; MAC; DAC; dynamic access; location; network; granularity; risk',1,N'Merged into ACL-05 — Merged'),
(113,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-01',N'Govern the identity life cycle',N'The organisation must define and maintain a controlled process covering identity request, verification, creation, configuration, activation, change, review, disabling and removal. The purpose is to manage every identity consistently from initial need through final removal.',N'Manage every identity consistently from initial need through final removal.',N'identity lifecycle; process; governance; creation; change; removal',1,N'Merged into IDM-08 — Merged'),
(114,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-02',N'Confirm the business need for identities',N'The organisation must require a documented business or operational need, accountable sponsor, defined purpose, scope and expected lifetime before an identity is established. It must establish, configure and activate identities. The purpose is to create identities only where a valid and approved need exists. It also aims to ensure new identities are correctly configured and securely enabled.',N'Create identities only where a valid and approved need exists. Ensure new identities are correctly configured and securely enabled.',N'business need; sponsor; purpose; scope; lifetime; approval; establish; configure; activate; enrolment; authentication service; setup',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(115,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-03',N'Verify entities before identity allocation',N'The organisation must verify the person, system or other entity before assigning a logical identity, using trusted evidence and stronger checks where risk is higher. The purpose is to prevent false, mistaken or fraudulent identity creation.',N'Prevent false, mistaken or fraudulent identity creation.',N'identity proofing; verification; trusted document; entity; risk',1,N'Merged into IDM-08 — Merged'),
(116,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-04',N'Maintain unique personal identities',N'The organisation must link each personal identity to one individual, preserve accountability for actions and avoid generic or ambiguous personal accounts. The purpose is to make actions attributable to the correct individual.',N'Make actions attributable to the correct individual.',N'unique identity; single person; accountability; named account; attribution',1,N'Merged into IDM-05 — Merged'),
(117,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-05',N'Control shared identities',N'The organisation must permit identities used by multiple people only when necessary for business or operations, with dedicated approval, documentation, accountability and monitoring. It must maintain unique personal identities. It must control non-human identities. It must assure third-party identities. The purpose is to limit shared identities and retain accountability where they cannot be avoided. It also aims to make actions attributable to the correct individual. It also aims to keep technical identities authorized, owned and independently monitored. It also aims to prevent weak or untrusted external identities from accessing organizational assets.',N'Limit shared identities and retain accountability where they cannot be avoided. Make actions attributable to the correct individual; Keep technical identities authorized, owned and independently monitored; Prevent weak or untrusted external identities from accessing organizational assets.',N'unique identity; single person; accountability; named account; attribution; shared identity; necessity; dedicated approval; documentation; non-human identity; machine; device; service; application',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(118,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-06',N'Control non-human identities',N'The organisation must manage identities for machines, devices, applications, services and automation using segregated approval, named ownership and independent ongoing oversight. The purpose is to keep technical identities authorized, owned and independently monitored.',N'Keep technical identities authorized, owned and independently monitored.',N'non-human identity; machine; device; service; application; oversight',1,N'Merged into IDM-05 — Merged'),
(119,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-07',N'Establish, configure and activate identities',N'The organisation must create, configure and activate identities through controlled steps, including the initial setup of related authentication services. The purpose is to ensure new identities are correctly configured and securely enabled.',N'Ensure new identities are correctly configured and securely enabled.',N'establish; configure; activate; enrolment; authentication service; setup',1,N'Merged into IDM-02 — Merged'),
(120,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-08',N'Manage identity information changes',N'The organisation must control changes to identity information, validate requests and re-verify trusted personal documents or attributes when needed. It must govern the identity life cycle. It must verify entities before identity allocation. It must record identity and authentication events. The purpose is to keep identity records accurate and trustworthy as details change. It also aims to manage every identity consistently from initial need through final removal. It also aims to prevent false, mistaken or fraudulent identity creation. It also aims to provide reliable evidence for accountability, investigation and review.',N'Keep identity records accurate and trustworthy as details change. Manage every identity consistently from initial need through final removal; Prevent false, mistaken or fraudulent identity creation; Provide reliable evidence for accountability, investigation and review.',N'identity lifecycle; process; governance; creation; change; removal; identity proofing; verification; trusted document; entity; risk; identity data; validation; reverification',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(121,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-09',N'Disable and remove identities promptly',N'The organisation must disable or remove identities when no longer required, including leavers, role changes and retired or deleted systems, services and devices. It must prevent and resolve duplicate identities. The purpose is to prevent continued use of obsolete or unauthorized identities. It also aims to maintain reliable identity-to-entity mapping and avoid duplicate accounts.',N'Prevent continued use of obsolete or unauthorized identities. Maintain reliable identity-to-entity mapping and avoid duplicate accounts.',N'disable; remove; leaver; role change; deleted entity; timely; duplicate identity; single entity; domain; mapping; reconciliation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(122,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-10',N'Prevent and resolve duplicate identities',N'The organisation must map one identity to one entity within each domain, detect multiple identities for the same entity and resolve unauthorized duplicates. The purpose is to maintain reliable identity-to-entity mapping and avoid duplicate accounts.',N'Maintain reliable identity-to-entity mapping and avoid duplicate accounts.',N'duplicate identity; single entity; domain; mapping; reconciliation',1,N'Merged into IDM-09 — Merged'),
(123,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-11',N'Record identity and authentication events',N'The organisation must keep protected records of significant events involving identity use, identity management and associated authentication information. The purpose is to provide reliable evidence for accountability, investigation and review.',N'Provide reliable evidence for accountability, investigation and review.',N'identity event; authentication event; audit trail; record; retention; protection',1,N'Merged into IDM-08 — Merged'),
(124,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-12',N'Assure third-party identities',N'The organisation must accept externally issued identities only where their trust level meets requirements and related provider, authentication and security risks are known and treated. The purpose is to prevent weak or untrusted external identities from accessing organizational assets.',N'Prevent weak or untrusted external identities from accessing organizational assets.',N'third-party identity; federation; trust level; provider; risk; treatment',1,N'Merged into IDM-05 — Merged'),
(125,17,N'5.16',N'IDM-13',N'Link identities to authorized access rights',N'The organisation must provide, change or revoke access rights for an identity only after an appropriate authorization or entitlement decision, and keep the identity and rights synchronized. The purpose is to ensure every identity has only the rights formally authorized for it.',N'Ensure every identity has only the rights formally authorized for it.',N'access right; entitlement; authorization; provision; revoke; synchronization',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(126,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-01',N'Govern authentication information',N'The organisation must define and operate an approved process for allocating, managing, handling, changing and withdrawing authentication information. It must protect authentication management records. It must manage non-password authentication information. It must control authentication tools and exceptions. The purpose is to control authentication information throughout its life cycle. It also aims to retain trustworthy evidence without exposing authentication secrets. It also aims to apply equivalent protection to every form of authentication information. It also aims to gain the benefit of authentication tools without creating unmanaged single points of compromise.',N'Control authentication information throughout its life cycle. Retain trustworthy evidence without exposing authentication secrets; Apply equivalent protection to every form of authentication information; Gain the benefit of authentication tools without creating unmanaged single points of compromise.',N'authentication management; policy; process; allocation; withdrawal; event record; confidentiality; approved method; password vault; audit trail; cryptographic key; token; smart card; authentication code',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(127,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-02',N'Control temporary authentication secrets',N'The organisation must generate temporary passwords and PINs that are unique and hard to guess, and require their replacement after first use. It must verify users before issuing secrets. The purpose is to prevent temporary enrolment secrets from enabling unauthorized access. It also aims to provide authentication information only to the correct verified user.',N'Prevent temporary enrolment secrets from enabling unauthorized access. Provide authentication information only to the correct verified user.',N'temporary password; PIN; unique; non-guessable; first use; identity verification; new secret; replacement; temporary; proofing',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(128,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-03',N'Verify users before issuing secrets',N'The organisation must verify a user’s identity before providing new, replacement or temporary authentication information. The purpose is to provide authentication information only to the correct verified user.',N'Provide authentication information only to the correct verified user.',N'identity verification; new secret; replacement; temporary; proofing',1,N'Merged into AUT-02 — Merged'),
(129,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-04',N'Deliver authentication information securely',N'The organisation must transmit authentication information through authenticated and protected channels, avoid clear-text email and obtain receipt acknowledgement. The purpose is to prevent interception, misdelivery or unnoticed loss during distribution.',N'Prevent interception, misdelivery or unnoticed loss during distribution.',N'secure delivery; protected channel; clear text; acknowledgement; receipt',1,N'Merged into AUT-08 — Merged'),
(130,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-05',N'Replace vendor and default authentication information',N'The organisation must change predefined or vendor-supplied authentication information immediately after installing systems or software. The purpose is to prevent use of known default credentials.',N'Prevent use of known default credentials.',N'default credential; vendor password; installation; immediate change',1,N'Merged into AUT-08 — Merged'),
(131,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-06',N'Protect authentication management records',N'The organisation must keep confidential records of significant allocation and management events using an approved record-keeping method such as an approved vault. The purpose is to retain trustworthy evidence without exposing authentication secrets.',N'Retain trustworthy evidence without exposing authentication secrets.',N'event record; confidentiality; approved method; password vault; audit trail',1,N'Merged into AUT-01 — Merged'),
(132,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-07',N'Maintain user secrecy and authorized sharing',N'The organisation must require users to keep personal authentication information confidential and restrict shared or non-personal secrets to authorized persons. The purpose is to prevent disclosure and uncontrolled sharing of authentication information.',N'Prevent disclosure and uncontrolled sharing of authentication information.',N'confidentiality; personal secret; sharing; authorized person; shared identity',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(133,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-08',N'Respond to compromised authentication information',N'The organisation must change, revoke or replace affected authentication information immediately when compromise is reported or suspected. It must deliver authentication information securely. It must replace vendor and default authentication information. The purpose is to contain authentication compromise before it can be misused. It also aims to prevent interception, misdelivery or unnoticed loss during distribution. It also aims to prevent use of known default credentials.',N'Contain authentication compromise before it can be misused. Prevent interception, misdelivery or unnoticed loss during distribution; Prevent use of known default credentials.',N'secure delivery; protected channel; clear text; acknowledgement; receipt; default credential; vendor password; installation; immediate change; compromise; revoke; replace; incident response',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(134,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-09',N'Require strong passwords and passphrases',N'The organisation must require passwords that are sufficiently long, not based on personal details or dictionary words, and designed as memorable strong passphrases where suitable. It must protect passwords in display, storage and transmission. The purpose is to reduce successful password guessing and cracking. It also aims to prevent passwords from being observed, recovered or intercepted.',N'Reduce successful password guessing and cracking. Prevent passwords from being observed, recovered or intercepted.',N'strong password; passphrase; minimum length; dictionary; personal data; password masking; protected storage; protected transmission; encryption; hashing',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(135,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-10',N'Prevent password reuse and formalize duties',N'The organisation must prevent reuse of the same passwords across distinct systems and services and include authentication-handling duties in employment terms. The purpose is to limit credential-stuffing impact and make user duties explicit.',N'Limit credential-stuffing impact and make user duties explicit.',N'password reuse; distinct service; employment terms; user obligation',1,N'Merged into AUT-12 — Merged'),
(136,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-11',N'Enable controlled password selection and first-use change',N'The organisation must allow users to select and change passwords, confirm entries to prevent errors and force changes at first login. The purpose is to ensure user-chosen passwords are entered correctly and temporary secrets do not remain active.',N'Ensure user-chosen passwords are entered correctly and temporary secrets do not remain active.',N'password selection; confirmation; input error; first login; change',1,N'Merged into AUT-12 — Merged'),
(137,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-12',N'Enforce password quality and change controls',N'The organisation must enforce strong passwords, necessary event-driven changes, password history, and blocking of common or known-compromised credentials. It must prevent password reuse and formalize duties. It must enable controlled password selection and first-use change. The purpose is to prevent weak, repeated or exposed passwords from remaining usable. It also aims to limit credential-stuffing impact and make user duties explicit. It also aims to ensure user-chosen passwords are entered correctly and temporary secrets do not remain active.',N'Prevent weak, repeated or exposed passwords from remaining usable. Limit credential-stuffing impact and make user duties explicit; Ensure user-chosen passwords are entered correctly and temporary secrets do not remain active.',N'password reuse; distinct service; employment terms; user obligation; password selection; confirmation; input error; first login; change; password enforcement; incident change; history; common password; breached credential',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(138,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-13',N'Protect passwords in display, storage and transmission',N'The organisation must mask passwords during entry and protect stored and transmitted passwords using approved encryption and hashing techniques. The purpose is to prevent passwords from being observed, recovered or intercepted.',N'Prevent passwords from being observed, recovered or intercepted.',N'password masking; protected storage; protected transmission; encryption; hashing',1,N'Merged into AUT-09 — Merged'),
(139,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-14',N'Manage non-password authentication information',N'The organisation must protect cryptographic keys, hardware-token data, authentication codes and biometric information according to their risks and handling needs. The purpose is to apply equivalent protection to every form of authentication information.',N'Apply equivalent protection to every form of authentication information.',N'cryptographic key; token; smart card; authentication code; biometric',1,N'Merged into AUT-01 — Merged'),
(140,18,N'5.17',N'AUT-15',N'Control authentication tools and exceptions',N'The organisation must assess SSO and vault concentration risk, protect authentication tools and document cases where an independent authority assigns passwords. The purpose is to gain the benefit of authentication tools without creating unmanaged single points of compromise.',N'Gain the benefit of authentication tools without creating unmanaged single points of compromise.',N'SSO; password vault; concentration risk; independent authority; exception',1,N'Merged into AUT-01 — Merged'),
(141,19,N'5.18',N'ART-01',N'Govern the access-right life cycle',N'The organisation must define and operate an approved process to provision, review, modify and remove physical and logical access rights under the access-control policy. The purpose is to keep every access right controlled from request through removal.',N'Keep every access right controlled from request through removal.',N'access rights; lifecycle; policy; provisioning; review; removal',1,N'Merged into ART-13 — Merged'),
(142,19,N'5.18',N'ART-02',N'Obtain owner and management authorization',N'The organisation must obtain authorization from the information or asset owner and, where appropriate, separate management approval before access is granted. The purpose is to ensure access is approved by accountable decision-makers.',N'Ensure access is approved by accountable decision-makers.',N'asset owner; authorization; management approval; access request',1,N'Merged into ART-13 — Merged'),
(143,19,N'5.18',N'ART-03',N'Validate business need and policy compliance',N'The organisation must check each request against business requirements, access-control rules and other security requirements before approval. The purpose is to grant only necessary and policy-compliant access.',N'Grant only necessary and policy-compliant access.',N'business need; policy check; access rules; security requirement',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(144,19,N'5.18',N'ART-04',N'Separate access approval and implementation',N'The organisation must separate approval from technical implementation and prevent conflicting roles when assigning or changing access. It must activate rights only after approval. The purpose is to prevent one person from approving and implementing unchecked access. It also aims to stop premature or unauthorized access activation.',N'Prevent one person from approving and implementing unchecked access. Stop premature or unauthorized access activation.',N'segregation; approval; implementation; conflicting roles; activation; completed approval; provisioning; service provider',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(145,19,N'5.18',N'ART-05',N'Activate rights only after approval',N'The organisation must provision and activate physical or logical access only after all required authorization steps are successfully completed. The purpose is to stop premature or unauthorized access activation.',N'Stop premature or unauthorized access activation.',N'activation; completed approval; provisioning; service provider',1,N'Merged into ART-04 — Merged'),
(146,19,N'5.18',N'ART-06',N'Maintain a central access-right record',N'The organisation must keep a current central record linking each user identifier to its approved physical and logical access rights. It must withdraw physical and logical access mechanisms. It must record access-right changes. It must set sanctions for unauthorized access attempts. The purpose is to provide one reliable view of who can access what. It also aims to close every practical route to withdrawn access. It also aims to make access decisions and changes traceable. It also aims to deter unauthorized access and support consistent action.',N'Provide one reliable view of who can access what. Close every practical route to withdrawn access; Make access decisions and changes traceable; Deter unauthorized access and support consistent action.',N'central register; user ID; physical access; logical access; entitlement; keys; credentials; ID card; subscription; revoke; replace; change record; approval; audit trail',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(147,19,N'5.18',N'ART-07',N'Control temporary access rights',N'The organisation must issue temporary rights for a defined period and revoke them automatically or promptly at the approved expiry date. The purpose is to prevent temporary access from becoming permanent.',N'Prevent temporary access from becoming permanent.',N'temporary access; expiry; time limit; contractor; revocation',1,N'Merged into ART-17 — Merged'),
(148,19,N'5.18',N'ART-08',N'Adjust rights after role or job changes',N'The organisation must review and modify access promptly when responsibilities, roles, jobs, promotions or demotions change. It must govern access-role changes. The purpose is to keep access aligned with current duties. It also aims to prevent hidden or excessive access from role design changes.',N'Keep access aligned with current duties. Prevent hidden or excessive access from role design changes.',N'role change; job change; promotion; demotion; access adjustment; profile maintenance; approval; testing; impact review',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(149,19,N'5.18',N'ART-09',N'Remove unnecessary and leaver access',N'The organisation must remove access that is no longer needed and revoke leaver access in a timely manner. The purpose is to prevent continued access after need or employment ends.',N'Prevent continued access after need or employment ends.',N'leaver; termination; unnecessary access; timely revocation',1,N'Merged into ART-17 — Merged'),
(150,19,N'5.18',N'ART-10',N'Withdraw physical and logical access mechanisms',N'The organisation must remove, revoke or replace keys, authentication information, identification cards and subscriptions when access changes or ends. The purpose is to close every practical route to withdrawn access.',N'Close every practical route to withdrawn access.',N'keys; credentials; ID card; subscription; revoke; replace',1,N'Merged into ART-06 — Merged'),
(151,19,N'5.18',N'ART-11',N'Record access-right changes',N'The organisation must maintain complete records of grants, modifications, reviews, removals and related approvals for physical and logical access. The purpose is to make access decisions and changes traceable.',N'Make access decisions and changes traceable.',N'change record; approval; audit trail; grant; modification; removal',1,N'Merged into ART-06 — Merged'),
(152,19,N'5.18',N'ART-12',N'Review access rights regularly',N'The organisation must perform scheduled reviews of physical and logical rights and correct rights that are excessive, obsolete or unsupported. The purpose is to confirm that access remains needed and authorized.',N'Confirm that access remains needed and authorized.',N'periodic review; recertification; excessive access; remediation',1,N'Merged into ART-13 — Merged'),
(153,19,N'5.18',N'ART-13',N'Review privileged access authorization',N'The organisation must review privileged rights and their authorizations more closely and at an appropriate risk-based frequency. It must govern the access-right life cycle. It must obtain owner and management authorization. It must review access rights regularly. The purpose is to keep powerful access limited and explicitly approved. It also aims to keep every access right controlled from request through removal. It also aims to ensure access is approved by accountable decision-makers. It also aims to confirm that access remains needed and authorized.',N'Keep powerful access limited and explicitly approved. Keep every access right controlled from request through removal; Ensure access is approved by accountable decision-makers; Confirm that access remains needed and authorized.',N'access rights; lifecycle; policy; provisioning; review; removal; asset owner; authorization; management approval; access request; periodic review; recertification; excessive access; remediation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(154,19,N'5.18',N'ART-14',N'Act before change or termination',N'The organisation must review and adjust or remove access before a job change or termination, based on who initiated it, the reason, current duties and asset value. The purpose is to reduce misuse, sabotage or information-removal risk during sensitive transitions.',N'Reduce misuse, sabotage or information-removal risk during sensitive transitions.',N'pre-termination; risk review; initiator; responsibilities; asset value',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(155,19,N'5.18',N'ART-15',N'Use controlled access roles and profiles',N'The organisation must define business-based access roles that group approved rights into manageable user access profiles. The purpose is to make access assignment and review consistent and efficient.',N'Make access assignment and review consistent and efficient.',N'access role; user profile; business requirement; role design',1,N'Merged into ART-17 — Merged'),
(156,19,N'5.18',N'ART-16',N'Govern access-role changes',N'The organisation must approve, test, document and review changes to access roles and profiles before they affect users. The purpose is to prevent hidden or excessive access from role design changes.',N'Prevent hidden or excessive access from role design changes.',N'role change; profile maintenance; approval; testing; impact review',1,N'Merged into ART-08 — Merged'),
(157,19,N'5.18',N'ART-17',N'Control access cloning',N'The organisation must clone access only from a verified role profile, check every copied right and remove excess access before activation. It must control temporary access rights. It must remove unnecessary and leaver access. It must use controlled access roles and profiles. The purpose is to avoid copying another user’s unnecessary rights. It also aims to prevent temporary access from becoming permanent. It also aims to prevent continued access after need or employment ends. It also aims to make access assignment and review consistent and efficient.',N'Avoid copying another user’s unnecessary rights. Prevent temporary access from becoming permanent; Prevent continued access after need or employment ends; Make access assignment and review consistent and efficient.',N'temporary access; expiry; time limit; contractor; revocation; leaver; termination; unnecessary access; timely revocation; access role; user profile; business requirement; role design; access cloning',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(158,19,N'5.18',N'ART-18',N'Set sanctions for unauthorized access attempts',N'The organisation must include clear consequences for attempted unauthorized access in relevant personnel and service contracts. The purpose is to deter unauthorized access and support consistent action.',N'Deter unauthorized access and support consistent action.',N'sanction; unauthorized attempt; personnel contract; service contract',1,N'Merged into ART-06 — Merged'),
(159,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-01',N'Govern supplier information security',N'The organisation must establish, approve, communicate and maintain a supplier-security policy, processes and procedures covering the full relationship life cycle. It must identify and classify supplier types. It must define supplier access and use. It must prepare for supplier failure and unavoidable gaps. The purpose is to maintain an agreed level of security across all supplier relationships. It also aims to apply controls according to the supplier type and its potential impact. It also aims to limit supplier activity to clearly approved assets and purposes. It also aims to maintain security and continuity when a supplier fails or cannot meet required controls.',N'Maintain an agreed level of security across all supplier relationships. Apply controls according to the supplier type and its potential impact; Limit supplier activity to clearly approved assets and purposes; Maintain security and continuity when a supplier fails or cannot meet required controls.',N'supplier policy; governance; process; procedure; lifecycle; supplier inventory; supplier type; ICT; logistics; utilities; finance; CIA; supplier access; information',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(160,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-02',N'Identify and classify supplier types',N'The organisation must identify and document supplier categories that can affect the confidentiality, integrity or availability of information. The purpose is to apply controls according to the supplier type and its potential impact.',N'Apply controls according to the supplier type and its potential impact.',N'supplier inventory; supplier type; ICT; logistics; utilities; finance; CIA',1,N'Merged into SUP-01 — Merged'),
(161,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-03',N'Evaluate and select suppliers',N'The organisation must define and apply security-based supplier evaluation and selection methods using information sensitivity, references, documents, assessments and certifications. The purpose is to choose suppliers whose security capability matches the risk.',N'Choose suppliers whose security capability matches the risk.',N'selection; due diligence; reference; assessment; certification; sensitivity',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(162,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-04',N'Assess supplier products and services',N'The organisation must evaluate whether proposed products and services have adequate, accurate and complete security controls before use and during review. It must identify supplier-provided ICT components and services. It must assess product and service vulnerabilities. It must ensure supplier resilience and recovery. The purpose is to prevent weak supplier offerings from undermining organizational security. It also aims to understand technology dependencies and their security impact. It also aims to prevent supplier weaknesses from causing breaches, malware or harm. It also aims to continue critical services when a supplier or its service is disrupted.',N'Prevent weak supplier offerings from undermining organizational security. Understand technology dependencies and their security impact; Prevent supplier weaknesses from causing breaches, malware or harm; Continue critical services when a supplier or its service is disrupted.',N'product security; service security; control adequacy; accuracy; completeness; ICT component; service dependency; infrastructure; confidentiality; integrity; availability; vulnerability; malfunction; software component',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(163,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-05',N'Include cloud services in supplier risk management',N'The organisation must apply supplier-security processes to cloud service providers and the cloud resources used by the organization. The purpose is to manage cloud-provider risk as part of the supplier relationship.',N'Manage cloud-provider risk as part of the supplier relationship.',N'cloud provider; cloud resource; shared responsibility; supplier risk',1,N'Merged into SUP-12 — Merged'),
(164,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-06',N'Define supplier access and use',N'The organisation must define the information, ICT services and physical infrastructure each supplier may access, monitor, control or use. The purpose is to limit supplier activity to clearly approved assets and purposes.',N'Limit supplier activity to clearly approved assets and purposes.',N'supplier access; information; ICT service; infrastructure; monitoring; control',1,N'Merged into SUP-01 — Merged'),
(165,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-07',N'Identify supplier-provided ICT components and services',N'The organisation must document supplier-provided infrastructure components and services that can affect information confidentiality, integrity or availability. The purpose is to understand technology dependencies and their security impact.',N'Understand technology dependencies and their security impact.',N'ICT component; service dependency; infrastructure; confidentiality; integrity; availability',1,N'Merged into SUP-04 — Merged'),
(166,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-08',N'Assess supplier use of information and assets',N'The organisation must assess and treat risks arising from suppliers using organizational information and other assets, including malicious supplier personnel. The purpose is to protect assets from misuse by supplier organizations or personnel.',N'Protect assets from misuse by supplier organizations or personnel.',N'supplier personnel; malicious insider; asset use; information use; risk treatment',1,N'Merged into SUP-19 — Merged'),
(167,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-09',N'Assess product and service vulnerabilities',N'The organisation must assess and treat risks from malfunctioning or vulnerable supplier products, software components, subcomponents and services. The purpose is to prevent supplier weaknesses from causing breaches, malware or harm.',N'Prevent supplier weaknesses from causing breaches, malware or harm.',N'vulnerability; malfunction; software component; subcomponent; malware; product risk',1,N'Merged into SUP-04 — Merged'),
(168,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-10',N'Monitor supplier security compliance',N'The organisation must monitor each supplier and access type against established requirements using evidence, third-party review and product validation. It must remediate supplier non-compliance. The purpose is to detect whether supplier controls remain effective and compliant. It also aims to restore the agreed security level and prevent recurrence.',N'Detect whether supplier controls remain effective and compliant. Restore the agreed security level and prevent recurrence.',N'compliance monitoring; third-party review; product validation; evidence; access type; non-compliance; remediation; escalation; corrective action; closure',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(169,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-11',N'Remediate supplier non-compliance',N'The organisation must record, assess, escalate and correct supplier non-compliance identified through monitoring or other means. The purpose is to restore the agreed security level and prevent recurrence.',N'Restore the agreed security level and prevent recurrence.',N'non-compliance; remediation; escalation; corrective action; closure',1,N'Merged into SUP-10 — Merged'),
(170,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-12',N'Manage supplier incidents and contingencies',N'The organisation must define and operate joint responsibilities, communication and response arrangements for incidents and contingencies involving supplier products or services. It must include cloud services in supplier risk management. It must secure supplier transitions and transfers. The purpose is to coordinate effective response to supplier-related disruption or compromise. It also aims to manage cloud-provider risk as part of the supplier relationship. It also aims to avoid security gaps during transition periods.',N'Coordinate effective response to supplier-related disruption or compromise. Manage cloud-provider risk as part of the supplier relationship; Avoid security gaps during transition periods.',N'cloud provider; cloud resource; shared responsibility; supplier risk; supplier incident; contingency; responsibility; communication; response; transition; transfer; supplier change; insourcing; information security',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(171,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-13',N'Ensure supplier resilience and recovery',N'The organisation must plan, test and maintain resilience, recovery and contingency measures that preserve the availability of supplier-supported information processing. The purpose is to continue critical services when a supplier or its service is disrupted.',N'Continue critical services when a supplier or its service is disrupted.',N'resilience; recovery; contingency; availability; continuity; testing',1,N'Merged into SUP-04 — Merged'),
(172,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-14',N'Train personnel who work with suppliers',N'The organisation must train organizational personnel on supplier rules of engagement, policies, procedures and expected behaviour according to supplier type and access level. The purpose is to ensure staff manage supplier interactions securely.',N'Ensure staff manage supplier interactions securely.',N'awareness; training; rules of engagement; behaviour; supplier access',1,N'Merged into SUP-19 — Merged'),
(173,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-15',N'Secure supplier transitions and transfers',N'The organisation must plan and control transfers of information, assets, responsibilities and services so security is maintained throughout a supplier change or insourcing. The purpose is to avoid security gaps during transition periods.',N'Avoid security gaps during transition periods.',N'transition; transfer; supplier change; insourcing; information security',1,N'Merged into SUP-12 — Merged'),
(174,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-16',N'De-provision access and control information at termination',N'The organisation must securely terminate relationships by removing supplier access and defining continued handling of organizational information. The purpose is to prevent access or misuse after the supplier relationship ends.',N'Prevent access or misuse after the supplier relationship ends.',N'termination; de-provision; access removal; information handling',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(175,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-17',N'Protect ownership, portability and records at exit',N'The organisation must determine intellectual-property ownership, preserve information portability and manage required records during supplier exit. It must return and securely dispose of assets at exit. The purpose is to protect organizational rights and enable an orderly move to another provider or in-house service. It also aims to close the relationship without leaving organizational assets or information exposed.',N'Protect organizational rights and enable an orderly move to another provider or in-house service. Close the relationship without leaving organizational assets or information exposed.',N'intellectual property; portability; records; exit; handover; asset return; secure disposal; confidentiality; termination; evidence',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(176,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-18',N'Return and securely dispose of assets at exit',N'The organisation must ensure assets are returned, information and associated assets are securely disposed of, and ongoing confidentiality duties remain effective. The purpose is to close the relationship without leaving organizational assets or information exposed.',N'Close the relationship without leaving organizational assets or information exposed.',N'asset return; secure disposal; confidentiality; termination; evidence',1,N'Merged into SUP-17 — Merged'),
(177,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-19',N'Set supplier personnel and facility security expectations',N'The organisation must define and verify the personnel-security and physical-security level expected from supplier staff and facilities. It must assess supplier use of information and assets. It must train personnel who work with suppliers. The purpose is to ensure people and locations supporting the service meet the required protection level. It also aims to protect assets from misuse by supplier organizations or personnel. It also aims to ensure staff manage supplier interactions securely.',N'Ensure people and locations supporting the service meet the required protection level. Protect assets from misuse by supplier organizations or personnel; Ensure staff manage supplier interactions securely.',N'supplier personnel; malicious insider; asset use; information use; risk treatment; awareness; training; rules of engagement; behaviour; supplier access; personnel security; physical security; supplier facility; screening',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(178,20,N'5.19',N'SUP-20',N'Prepare for supplier failure and unavoidable gaps',N'The organisation must plan replacement or alternate supply and apply risk-based compensating controls where requirements cannot be imposed on a supplier. The purpose is to maintain security and continuity when a supplier fails or cannot meet required controls.',N'Maintain security and continuity when a supplier fails or cannot meet required controls.',N'supplier failure; alternate supplier; replacement; compensating control; residual risk',1,N'Merged into SUP-01 — Merged'),
(179,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-01',N'Govern supplier security agreements',N'The organisation must establish and document supplier agreements that clearly assign both parties’ information security obligations according to the relationship type. The purpose is to create a shared and enforceable understanding of required security.',N'Create a shared and enforceable understanding of required security.',N'supplier agreement; obligations; relationship type; governance',1,N'Merged into SAG-04 — Merged'),
(180,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-02',N'Describe information and access methods',N'The organisation must state what information will be provided or accessed and how physical or logical access will occur. The purpose is to make the information flow and access route explicit.',N'Make the information flow and access route explicit.',N'information description; access method; data flow; supplier access',1,N'Merged into SAG-06 — Merged'),
(181,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-03',N'Specify information classification',N'The organisation must apply the organization’s classification scheme to information handled under the agreement. The purpose is to ensure supplier handling matches information sensitivity.',N'Ensure supplier handling matches information sensitivity.',N'classification; sensitivity; handling; supplier information',1,N'Merged into SAG-04 — Merged'),
(182,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-04',N'Map supplier classification schemes',N'The organisation must map the organization’s classifications to the supplier’s classification scheme and resolve differences. It must govern supplier security agreements. It must specify information classification. It must set supplier ICT infrastructure requirements. The purpose is to preserve protection when classification terms differ. It also aims to create a shared and enforceable understanding of required security. It also aims to ensure supplier handling matches information sensitivity. It also aims to ensure supplier technology provides suitable protection.',N'Preserve protection when classification terms differ. Create a shared and enforceable understanding of required security; Ensure supplier handling matches information sensitivity; Ensure supplier technology provides suitable protection.',N'supplier agreement; obligations; relationship type; governance; classification; sensitivity; handling; supplier information; classification mapping; equivalence; supplier scheme; protection; ICT infrastructure; minimum security',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(183,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-05',N'Include legal regulatory and contractual duties',N'The organisation must document applicable law, regulation, data protection, PII, intellectual-property, copyright and contractual requirements and how they will be met. The purpose is to make external obligations clear and enforceable.',N'Make external obligations clear and enforceable.',N'legal; regulatory; PII; data protection; intellectual property; copyright',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(184,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-06',N'Agree required security controls',N'The organisation must define each party’s duties for access control, performance review, monitoring, reporting, auditing and compliance with organizational requirements. It must describe information and access methods. It must preserve the right to audit. The purpose is to ensure all required controls have an accountable party. It also aims to make the information flow and access route explicit. It also aims to allow direct verification of supplier compliance.',N'Ensure all required controls have an accountable party. Make the information flow and access route explicit; Allow direct verification of supplier compliance.',N'information description; access method; data flow; supplier access; security controls; access control; monitoring; reporting; audit; compliance; right to audit; supplier process; control; inspection',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(185,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-07',N'Define acceptable and prohibited use',N'The organisation must state permitted and prohibited uses of organizational information and other associated assets. The purpose is to prevent misuse of information and assets by suppliers.',N'Prevent misuse of information and assets by suppliers.',N'acceptable use; prohibited use; information; assets; supplier',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(186,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-08',N'Control supplier personnel authorization',N'The organisation must define conditions for authorizing and removing supplier personnel and maintain an explicit authorized-person list where appropriate. The purpose is to limit supplier access to approved individuals.',N'Limit supplier access to approved individuals.',N'supplier personnel; authorization; removal; authorized list; access',1,N'Merged into SAG-15 — Merged'),
(187,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-09',N'Set supplier ICT infrastructure requirements',N'The organisation must define minimum security requirements for supplier infrastructure by information type, access type, business need and risk. The purpose is to ensure supplier technology provides suitable protection.',N'Ensure supplier technology provides suitable protection.',N'ICT infrastructure; minimum security; information type; access type; risk',1,N'Merged into SAG-04 — Merged'),
(188,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-10',N'Define indemnity and remediation',N'The organisation must state indemnities, remedies and corrective duties when the supplier fails to meet requirements. The purpose is to provide clear consequences and recovery actions for supplier failure.',N'Provide clear consequences and recovery actions for supplier failure.',N'indemnity; remediation; failure; corrective action; liability',1,N'Merged into SAG-11 — Merged'),
(189,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-11',N'Define incident management obligations',N'The organisation must set incident notification, coordination, evidence, communication and remediation requirements for both parties. It must define indemnity and remediation. It must require security training and awareness. The purpose is to enable timely and coordinated response to supplier-related incidents. It also aims to provide clear consequences and recovery actions for supplier failure. It also aims to ensure relevant personnel understand their security responsibilities.',N'Enable timely and coordinated response to supplier-related incidents. Provide clear consequences and recovery actions for supplier failure; Ensure relevant personnel understand their security responsibilities.',N'indemnity; remediation; failure; corrective action; liability; incident; notification; collaboration; evidence; training; awareness; incident response; authorization; procedure',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(190,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-12',N'Require security training and awareness',N'The organisation must define training and awareness duties for incident response, authorization and other supplier-specific procedures. The purpose is to ensure relevant personnel understand their security responsibilities.',N'Ensure relevant personnel understand their security responsibilities.',N'training; awareness; incident response; authorization; procedure',1,N'Merged into SAG-11 — Merged'),
(191,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-13',N'Control subcontracting and sub-suppliers',N'The organisation must require approval or agreement for subcontracting, equivalent downstream obligations, a sub-supplier list and advance change notification. The purpose is to extend required protection throughout the supplier chain.',N'Extend required protection throughout the supplier chain.',N'subcontracting; sub-supplier; flow-down; approval; notification',1,N'Merged into SAG-15 — Merged'),
(192,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-14',N'Maintain security contacts',N'The organisation must name relevant operational and information-security contacts and keep their details current. It must define defect and conflict resolution. The purpose is to enable prompt communication and escalation. It also aims to resolve failures and disagreements consistently and promptly.',N'Enable prompt communication and escalation. Resolve failures and disagreements consistently and promptly.',N'security contact; operational contact; escalation; contact details; defect resolution; conflict resolution; timescale',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(193,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-15',N'Set supplier personnel screening requirements',N'The organisation must define legally permitted screening, responsibility for checks and notification of missing or concerning results. It must control supplier personnel authorization. It must control subcontracting and sub-suppliers. It must control supplier changes. The purpose is to reduce personnel risk in supplier-delivered services. It also aims to limit supplier access to approved individuals. It also aims to extend required protection throughout the supplier chain. It also aims to prevent supplier changes from introducing unaccepted risk.',N'Reduce personnel risk in supplier-delivered services. Limit supplier access to approved individuals; Extend required protection throughout the supplier chain; Prevent supplier changes from introducing unaccepted risk.',N'supplier personnel; authorization; removal; authorized list; access; subcontracting; sub-supplier; flow-down; approval; notification; screening; legal permission; concern; change management',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(194,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-16',N'Define evidence and independent assurance',N'The organisation must require suitable attestations, evidence and independent reports on the effectiveness of relevant supplier controls. The purpose is to obtain reliable assurance that controls operate effectively.',N'Obtain reliable assurance that controls operate effectively.',N'attestation; assurance; independent report; control effectiveness; evidence',1,N'Merged into SAG-26 — Merged'),
(195,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-17',N'Preserve the right to audit',N'The organisation must include the organization’s right to audit supplier processes and controls related to the agreement. The purpose is to allow direct verification of supplier compliance.',N'Allow direct verification of supplier compliance.',N'right to audit; supplier process; control; inspection; evidence',1,N'Merged into SAG-06 — Merged'),
(196,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-18',N'Require control-effectiveness reporting',N'The organisation must require periodic supplier reports on control effectiveness and timely correction of issues raised. The purpose is to maintain visibility of control performance and remediation.',N'Maintain visibility of control performance and remediation.',N'periodic report; effectiveness; issue; timely correction; supplier',1,N'Merged into SAG-26 — Merged'),
(197,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-19',N'Define defect and conflict resolution',N'The organisation must document processes, responsibilities and timescales for resolving service defects and disputes. The purpose is to resolve failures and disagreements consistently and promptly.',N'Resolve failures and disagreements consistently and promptly.',N'defect resolution; conflict resolution; escalation; timescale',1,N'Merged into SAG-14 — Merged'),
(198,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-20',N'Specify backup requirements',N'The organisation must require backups that meet organizational needs for frequency, type, protection and storage location. The purpose is to ensure supplier-held information can be recovered as required.',N'Ensure supplier-held information can be recovered as required.',N'backup; frequency; type; storage location; recovery',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(199,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-21',N'Require alternate facilities and fallback controls',N'The organisation must require a disaster-recovery facility not exposed to the same threats and fallback controls when primary controls fail. It must require exit and handover support. The purpose is to maintain service and protection during disruption. It also aims to maintain security and continuity through service transition.',N'Maintain service and protection during disruption. Maintain security and continuity through service transition.',N'alternate facility; disaster recovery; common threat; fallback control; handover; exit support; supplier transition; insourcing; continuity',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(200,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-22',N'Control supplier changes',N'The organisation must require advance change notification and preserve the organization’s right to reject unacceptable changes. The purpose is to prevent supplier changes from introducing unaccepted risk.',N'Prevent supplier changes from introducing unaccepted risk.',N'change management; advance notice; reject change; supplier risk',1,N'Merged into SAG-15 — Merged');

INSERT #prac(seq,sheet_statement_id,statement_reference,practice_ref,practice_name,practice_statement,objective,keywords,is_merged,merge_status) VALUES
(201,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-23',N'Set physical security requirements',N'The organisation must require physical controls proportionate to the classification of information and assets. It must protect information transfers. The purpose is to protect supplier facilities and physical assets appropriately. It also aims to prevent loss, alteration or disclosure while information moves.',N'Protect supplier facilities and physical assets appropriately. Prevent loss, alteration or disclosure while information moves.',N'physical security; classification; facility; physical asset; information transfer; physical transfer; transmission; protection',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(202,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-24',N'Protect information transfers',N'The organisation must require controls for protecting information during physical transfer and logical transmission. The purpose is to prevent loss, alteration or disclosure while information moves.',N'Prevent loss, alteration or disclosure while information moves.',N'information transfer; physical transfer; transmission; protection',1,N'Merged into SAG-23 — Merged'),
(203,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-25',N'Define secure termination clauses',N'The organisation must include records management, asset return, secure disposal and continuing confidentiality obligations at contract end. The purpose is to ensure supplier exit does not leave information or assets exposed.',N'Ensure supplier exit does not leave information or assets exposed.',N'termination; records; asset return; secure disposal; confidentiality',1,N'Merged into SAG-26 — Merged'),
(204,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-26',N'Require secure destruction — Addressing information security within supplier agreements',N'The organisation must define a verifiable method for securely destroying organizational information when it is no longer required. It must define evidence and independent assurance. It must require control-effectiveness reporting. It must define secure termination clauses. The purpose is to prevent retained supplier copies from exposing information. It also aims to obtain reliable assurance that controls operate effectively. It also aims to maintain visibility of control performance and remediation. It also aims to ensure supplier exit does not leave information or assets exposed.',N'Prevent retained supplier copies from exposing information. Obtain reliable assurance that controls operate effectively; Maintain visibility of control performance and remediation; Ensure supplier exit does not leave information or assets exposed.',N'attestation; assurance; independent report; control effectiveness; evidence; periodic report; effectiveness; issue; timely correction; supplier; termination; records; asset return; secure disposal',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(205,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-27',N'Require exit and handover support',N'The organisation must require support at contract end for handover to another supplier or back to the organization. The purpose is to maintain security and continuity through service transition.',N'Maintain security and continuity through service transition.',N'handover; exit support; supplier transition; insourcing; continuity',1,N'Merged into SAG-21 — Merged'),
(206,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-28',N'Maintain an external-agreement register',N'The organisation must keep a current register of contracts, memoranda and information-sharing agreements showing where organizational information goes. It must review validate and update agreements. The purpose is to provide visibility and accountability for external information sharing. It also aims to keep supplier agreements aligned with changing risks and needs.',N'Provide visibility and accountability for external information sharing. Keep supplier agreements aligned with changing risks and needs.',N'agreement register; contract; memorandum; information sharing; data location; agreement review; validation; update; fit for purpose; security clause',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(207,21,N'5.20',N'SAG-29',N'Review validate and update agreements',N'The organisation must regularly confirm agreements remain necessary, fit for purpose and contain relevant current security clauses. The purpose is to keep supplier agreements aligned with changing risks and needs.',N'Keep supplier agreements aligned with changing risks and needs.',N'agreement review; validation; update; fit for purpose; security clause',1,N'Merged into SAG-28 — Merged'),
(208,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-01',N'Govern ICT supply-chain security',N'The organisation must define and implement processes and procedures for managing security risks across ICT product and service supply chains. It must share supply-chain risk information. It must understand the extended ICT supply chain. The purpose is to maintain agreed security throughout the ICT supply chain. It also aims to enable timely coordinated response to supply-chain risk. It also aims to understand entities and dependencies that affect delivered ICT.',N'Maintain agreed security throughout the ICT supply chain. Enable timely coordinated response to supply-chain risk; Understand entities and dependencies that affect delivered ICT.',N'ICT supply chain; governance; risk; process; procedure; information sharing; compromise; issue; supplier communication; escalation; extended supply chain; cloud; telecom; hardware',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(209,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-02',N'Set security requirements for ICT acquisition',N'The organisation must define security requirements for acquiring ICT products and services according to business need and risk. It must assure required ICT security levels. It must acquire ICT from reputable sources. The purpose is to ensure security is built into purchasing decisions. It also aims to confirm product assurance matches organizational requirements. It also aims to make reliable sourcing decisions using credible evidence.',N'Ensure security is built into purchasing decisions. Confirm product assurance matches organizational requirements; Make reliable sourcing decisions using credible evidence.',N'ICT acquisition; security requirement; procurement; business need; risk; security level; certification; evaluation; Common Criteria; assurance; reputable source; vendor reputation; quality control; sourcing',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(210,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-03',N'Flow requirements through ICT service chains',N'The organisation must require ICT service suppliers to pass organizational security requirements to subcontractors supporting the service. The purpose is to preserve required controls throughout outsourced service layers.',N'Preserve required controls throughout outsourced service layers.',N'service supplier; subcontractor; flow-down; security requirement',1,N'Merged into ISC-04 — Merged'),
(211,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-04',N'Flow security practices through product chains',N'The organisation must require ICT product suppliers to pass appropriate security practices to software developers, hardware providers and other component suppliers. It must flow requirements through ICT service chains. It must maintain software-component information. It must prepare alternate suppliers and capability transfer. The purpose is to protect products whose components come from other entities. It also aims to preserve required controls throughout outsourced service layers. It also aims to provide visibility of software composition and provenance. It also aims to maintain continuity when the original supply source fails.',N'Protect products whose components come from other entities. Preserve required controls throughout outsourced service layers; Provide visibility of software composition and provenance; Maintain continuity when the original supply source fails.',N'service supplier; subcontractor; flow-down; security requirement; product supplier; software developer; hardware provider; component; software component; inventory; provenance; SWID; supplier information; alternative supplier',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(212,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-05',N'Maintain software-component information',N'The organisation must require suppliers to describe software components used in products and keep the information current. The purpose is to provide visibility of software composition and provenance.',N'Provide visibility of software composition and provenance.',N'software component; inventory; provenance; SWID; supplier information',1,N'Merged into ISC-04 — Merged'),
(213,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-06',N'Document security functions and secure configuration',N'The organisation must require suppliers to describe product security functions and the configuration needed for secure operation. It must verify expected product behaviour. The purpose is to enable products to be deployed and operated securely. It also aims to prevent hidden, unauthorized or harmful product functionality.',N'Enable products to be deployed and operated securely. Prevent hidden, unauthorized or harmful product functionality.',N'security function; secure configuration; product documentation; operation; expected function; unwanted feature; product assurance; acceptance',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(214,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-07',N'Validate delivered products and services',N'The organisation must monitor and validate delivered ICT products and services against stated security requirements using approved methods. The purpose is to confirm delivered ICT meets agreed security requirements.',N'Confirm delivered ICT meets agreed security requirements.',N'validation; monitoring; penetration test; attestation; compliance',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(215,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-08',N'Identify and protect critical components',N'The organisation must identify and document components essential to functionality and apply increased scrutiny, especially when externally built or outsourced. It must trace critical components and origin. It must ensure components are genuine and unaltered. The purpose is to focus assurance on components whose failure would have serious impact. It also aims to maintain reliable component provenance and accountability. It also aims to prevent counterfeit, substituted or tampered components.',N'Focus assurance on components whose failure would have serious impact. Maintain reliable component provenance and accountability; Prevent counterfeit, substituted or tampered components.',N'critical component; functionality; scrutiny; outsourced; follow-up; traceability; origin; provenance; supply chain; authenticity; tamper; counterfeit; hash; digital signature',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(216,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-09',N'Trace critical components and origin',N'The organisation must obtain assurance that critical components and their origin can be traced throughout the supply chain. The purpose is to maintain reliable component provenance and accountability.',N'Maintain reliable component provenance and accountability.',N'traceability; origin; provenance; critical component; supply chain',1,N'Merged into ISC-08 — Merged'),
(217,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-10',N'Verify expected product behaviour',N'The organisation must obtain assurance that delivered ICT products work as expected and contain no unexpected or unwanted features. The purpose is to prevent hidden, unauthorized or harmful product functionality.',N'Prevent hidden, unauthorized or harmful product functionality.',N'expected function; unwanted feature; product assurance; acceptance',1,N'Merged into ISC-06 — Merged'),
(218,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-11',N'Ensure components are genuine and unaltered',N'The organisation must use processes such as anti-tamper labels, cryptographic hashes and digital signatures to confirm supplier components are authentic and unchanged. The purpose is to prevent counterfeit, substituted or tampered components.',N'Prevent counterfeit, substituted or tampered components.',N'authenticity; tamper; counterfeit; hash; digital signature',1,N'Merged into ISC-08 — Merged'),
(219,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-12',N'Detect tampering across the life cycle',N'The organisation must prevent and detect tampering during design, development, integration, operations and maintenance, including monitoring abnormal performance. It must manage component life cycle and availability. The purpose is to protect component integrity at every life-cycle stage. It also aims to avoid security and service failure from unavailable or obsolete components.',N'Protect component integrity at every life-cycle stage. Avoid security and service failure from unavailable or obsolete components.',N'tamper detection; design; development; integration; operations; maintenance; component lifecycle; availability; obsolescence; support; security risk',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(220,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-13',N'Assure required ICT security levels',N'The organisation must obtain evidence that ICT products achieve required security levels through certification or suitable evaluation schemes. The purpose is to confirm product assurance matches organizational requirements.',N'Confirm product assurance matches organizational requirements.',N'security level; certification; evaluation; Common Criteria; assurance',1,N'Merged into ISC-02 — Merged'),
(221,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-14',N'Share supply-chain risk information',N'The organisation must define rules for sharing supply-chain information, issues and compromises between the organization and suppliers. The purpose is to enable timely coordinated response to supply-chain risk.',N'Enable timely coordinated response to supply-chain risk.',N'information sharing; compromise; issue; supplier communication; escalation',1,N'Merged into ISC-01 — Merged'),
(222,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-15',N'Manage component life cycle and availability',N'The organisation must manage component support, availability, obsolescence and security risks throughout the ICT life cycle. The purpose is to avoid security and service failure from unavailable or obsolete components.',N'Avoid security and service failure from unavailable or obsolete components.',N'component lifecycle; availability; obsolescence; support; security risk',1,N'Merged into ISC-12 — Merged'),
(223,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-16',N'Prepare alternate suppliers and capability transfer',N'The organisation must identify alternative suppliers and plan transfer of software, information and competence if a supplier or component becomes unavailable. The purpose is to maintain continuity when the original supply source fails.',N'Maintain continuity when the original supply source fails.',N'alternative supplier; transfer; software; competence; continuity',1,N'Merged into ISC-04 — Merged'),
(224,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-17',N'Understand the extended ICT supply chain',N'The organisation must work with suppliers to map important dependencies, including cloud, telecommunications, hardware, software, IoT and support providers. The purpose is to understand entities and dependencies that affect delivered ICT.',N'Understand entities and dependencies that affect delivered ICT.',N'extended supply chain; cloud; telecom; hardware; software; IoT; support',1,N'Merged into ISC-01 — Merged'),
(225,22,N'5.21',N'ISC-18',N'Acquire ICT from reputable sources',N'The organisation must assess supplier reputation and available quality evidence when direct inspection of vendor quality controls is not possible. The purpose is to make reliable sourcing decisions using credible evidence.',N'Make reliable sourcing decisions using credible evidence.',N'reputable source; vendor reputation; quality control; sourcing; evidence',1,N'Merged into ISC-02 — Merged'),
(226,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-01',N'Govern supplier monitoring and change management',N'The organisation must define a controlled process to monitor, review, evaluate and manage changes in supplier security practices and service delivery. The purpose is to maintain agreed security and service levels throughout supplier relationships.',N'Maintain agreed security and service levels throughout supplier relationships.',N'supplier monitoring; review; evaluation; change management; governance',1,N'Merged into SMC-20 — Merged'),
(227,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-02',N'Verify agreement compliance',N'The organisation must check that supplier services comply with all applicable security terms and conditions in the agreement. It must require supplier compliance ownership. The purpose is to ensure contractual security requirements operate in practice. It also aims to create clear supplier accountability for security compliance.',N'Ensure contractual security requirements operate in practice. Create clear supplier accountability for security compliance.',N'agreement compliance; security terms; supplier service; verification; supplier responsibility; compliance review; enforcement; accountability',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(228,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-03',N'Monitor service performance levels',N'The organisation must measure supplier service levels and compare results with agreed performance commitments. The purpose is to detect service shortfalls before they affect security or operations.',N'Detect service shortfalls before they affect security or operations.',N'service level; performance; SLA; monitoring; supplier',1,N'Merged into SMC-04 — Merged'),
(229,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-04',N'Monitor service enhancements',N'The organisation must assess security effects of enhancements to existing supplier services before acceptance. It must monitor service performance levels. It must monitor service-facility location changes. The purpose is to prevent enhancements from weakening agreed protection. It also aims to detect service shortfalls before they affect security or operations. It also aims to manage physical, jurisdictional and continuity risks from relocation.',N'Prevent enhancements from weakening agreed protection. Detect service shortfalls before they affect security or operations; Manage physical, jurisdictional and continuity risks from relocation.',N'service level; performance; SLA; monitoring; supplier; service enhancement; security impact; supplier change; acceptance; facility location; relocation; physical risk; jurisdiction',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(230,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-05',N'Monitor new supplier applications and systems',N'The organisation must review security implications of applications and systems newly developed by the supplier. It must monitor adoption of new technologies. The purpose is to control risk introduced by new supplier technology. It also aims to understand and treat risks from emerging technology.',N'Control risk introduced by new supplier technology. Understand and treat risks from emerging technology.',N'new application; new system; supplier development; security review; new technology; adoption; risk assessment; supplier service',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(231,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-06',N'Monitor supplier policy and procedure changes',N'The organisation must review modifications to supplier policies and procedures for their effect on agreed security. It must monitor network changes. It must monitor product versions and releases. It must monitor sub-supplier and subcontracting changes. The purpose is to keep supplier governance aligned with agreement requirements. It also aims to prevent network changes from creating unaccepted risk. It also aims to control risks from product and release changes. It also aims to maintain visibility and control across downstream providers.',N'Keep supplier governance aligned with agreement requirements. Prevent network changes from creating unaccepted risk; Control risks from product and release changes; Maintain visibility and control across downstream providers.',N'supplier policy; procedure change; impact; agreement; network change; enhancement; supplier network; security impact; product version; release; upgrade; supplier change; sub-supplier; subcontractor',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(232,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-07',N'Monitor changed security controls',N'The organisation must assess new or changed supplier controls introduced after incidents or for security improvement. It must monitor development tools and environments. The purpose is to confirm control changes are suitable and effective. It also aims to prevent development changes from weakening service security.',N'Confirm control changes are suitable and effective. Prevent development changes from weakening service security.',N'security control; incident improvement; control change; effectiveness; development tool; environment; platform; supplier change',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(233,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-08',N'Monitor network changes',N'The organisation must review changes and enhancements to supplier networks that support the service. The purpose is to prevent network changes from creating unaccepted risk.',N'Prevent network changes from creating unaccepted risk.',N'network change; enhancement; supplier network; security impact',1,N'Merged into SMC-06 — Merged'),
(234,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-09',N'Monitor adoption of new technologies',N'The organisation must assess supplier use of new technologies before or during service introduction. The purpose is to understand and treat risks from emerging technology.',N'Understand and treat risks from emerging technology.',N'new technology; adoption; risk assessment; supplier service',1,N'Merged into SMC-05 — Merged'),
(235,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-10',N'Monitor product versions and releases',N'The organisation must review supplier adoption of new products, versions and releases for security and service impact. The purpose is to control risks from product and release changes.',N'Control risks from product and release changes.',N'product version; release; upgrade; supplier change; impact',1,N'Merged into SMC-06 — Merged'),
(236,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-11',N'Monitor development tools and environments',N'The organisation must assess changes to supplier development tools, platforms and environments affecting delivered services. The purpose is to prevent development changes from weakening service security.',N'Prevent development changes from weakening service security.',N'development tool; environment; platform; supplier change',1,N'Merged into SMC-07 — Merged'),
(237,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-12',N'Monitor service-facility location changes',N'The organisation must review changes to the physical locations from which supplier services are delivered. The purpose is to manage physical, jurisdictional and continuity risks from relocation.',N'Manage physical, jurisdictional and continuity risks from relocation.',N'facility location; relocation; physical risk; jurisdiction; supplier',1,N'Merged into SMC-04 — Merged'),
(238,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-13',N'Monitor sub-supplier and subcontracting changes',N'The organisation must review replacement, addition or use of sub-suppliers and subcontractors. The purpose is to maintain visibility and control across downstream providers.',N'Maintain visibility and control across downstream providers.',N'sub-supplier; subcontractor; change; downstream provider',1,N'Merged into SMC-06 — Merged'),
(239,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-14',N'Review supplier reports and hold progress meetings',N'The organisation must review required service and security reports and conduct regular progress meetings. It must exchange and review incident information. The purpose is to maintain evidence-based oversight and timely communication. It also aims to support shared awareness and coordinated incident handling.',N'Maintain evidence-based oversight and timely communication. Support shared awareness and coordinated incident handling.',N'service report; security report; progress meeting; supplier review; incident information; notification; review; agreement; supplier',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(240,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-15',N'Audit suppliers and sub-suppliers',N'The organisation must conduct supplier audits, review available independent audit reports and follow up identified issues. It must review supplier audit trails and service records. The purpose is to obtain independent evidence and close assurance findings. It also aims to use operational evidence to identify service and security weaknesses.',N'Obtain independent evidence and close assurance findings. Use operational evidence to identify service and security weaknesses.',N'supplier audit; sub-supplier; independent report; finding; follow-up; audit trail; event record; operational problem; fault; disruption',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(241,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-16',N'Exchange and review incident information',N'The organisation must provide and review supplier-related security incident information as required by agreements and procedures. The purpose is to support shared awareness and coordinated incident handling.',N'Support shared awareness and coordinated incident handling.',N'incident information; notification; review; agreement; supplier',1,N'Merged into SMC-14 — Merged'),
(242,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-17',N'Review supplier audit trails and service records',N'The organisation must review logs and records of security events, operational problems, failures, fault tracing and disruptions. The purpose is to use operational evidence to identify service and security weaknesses.',N'Use operational evidence to identify service and security weaknesses.',N'audit trail; event record; operational problem; fault; disruption',1,N'Merged into SMC-15 — Merged'),
(243,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-18',N'Respond to supplier security events and incidents',N'The organisation must manage identified supplier-related security events and incidents through containment, remediation and closure. The purpose is to limit impact and restore secure service promptly.',N'Limit impact and restore secure service promptly.',N'supplier incident; event response; containment; remediation; closure',1,N'Merged into SMC-19 — Merged'),
(244,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-19',N'Identify and manage supplier vulnerabilities',N'The organisation must identify, assess, prioritize and remediate vulnerabilities affecting supplier-delivered services. It must respond to supplier security events and incidents. It must correct supplier service deficiencies. The purpose is to reduce exposure from known supplier-service weaknesses. It also aims to limit impact and restore secure service promptly. It also aims to restore compliance and prevent recurrence of supplier failures.',N'Reduce exposure from known supplier-service weaknesses. Limit impact and restore secure service promptly; Restore compliance and prevent recurrence of supplier failures.',N'supplier incident; event response; containment; remediation; closure; vulnerability; supplier service; assessment; priority; service deficiency; corrective action; escalation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(245,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-20',N'Review supplier relationships with their suppliers',N'The organisation must assess security aspects of the supplier’s dependencies and arrangements with its own suppliers. It must govern supplier monitoring and change management. It must evaluate supplier security levels regularly. It must assign skilled supplier-relationship management. The purpose is to control risks inherited from the extended supplier chain. It also aims to maintain agreed security and service levels throughout supplier relationships. It also aims to confirm supplier protection remains suitable over time. It also aims to ensure supplier requirements are monitored by capable and accountable staff.',N'Control risks inherited from the extended supplier chain. Maintain agreed security and service levels throughout supplier relationships; Confirm supplier protection remains suitable over time; Ensure supplier requirements are monitored by capable and accountable staff.',N'supplier monitoring; review; evaluation; change management; governance; supplier relationship; downstream supplier; dependency; supply chain; security level; regular evaluation; adequacy; supplier assurance; relationship owner',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(246,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-21',N'Assure supplier capacity and continuity plans',N'The organisation must confirm the supplier has sufficient service capability and workable plans to maintain agreed continuity after failure or disaster. The purpose is to preserve agreed service continuity under severe disruption.',N'Preserve agreed service continuity under severe disruption.',N'service capability; continuity plan; disaster; major failure; capacity',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(247,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-22',N'Require supplier compliance ownership',N'The organisation must ensure suppliers assign responsibility for reviewing compliance and enforcing agreement requirements. The purpose is to create clear supplier accountability for security compliance.',N'Create clear supplier accountability for security compliance.',N'supplier responsibility; compliance review; enforcement; accountability',1,N'Merged into SMC-02 — Merged'),
(248,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-23',N'Evaluate supplier security levels regularly',N'The organisation must regularly evaluate whether suppliers maintain adequate information security levels. The purpose is to confirm supplier protection remains suitable over time.',N'Confirm supplier protection remains suitable over time.',N'security level; regular evaluation; adequacy; supplier assurance',1,N'Merged into SMC-20 — Merged'),
(249,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-24',N'Assign skilled supplier-relationship management',N'The organisation must assign a designated person or team and provide sufficient technical skills and resources for supplier oversight. The purpose is to ensure supplier requirements are monitored by capable and accountable staff.',N'Ensure supplier requirements are monitored by capable and accountable staff.',N'relationship owner; technical skill; resource; supplier oversight',1,N'Merged into SMC-20 — Merged'),
(250,23,N'5.22',N'SMC-25',N'Correct supplier service deficiencies',N'The organisation must record, assess, escalate and correct deficiencies observed in supplier security or service delivery. The purpose is to restore compliance and prevent recurrence of supplier failures.',N'Restore compliance and prevent recurrence of supplier failures.',N'service deficiency; corrective action; escalation; remediation; closure',1,N'Merged into SMC-19 — Merged'),
(251,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-01',N'Govern the cloud-service life cycle',N'The organisation must define controlled processes for acquiring, using, managing, changing and exiting cloud services according to security requirements. The purpose is to manage cloud security consistently from selection through exit.',N'Manage cloud security consistently from selection through exit.',N'cloud lifecycle; acquisition; use; management; exit',1,N'Merged into CLD-04 — Merged'),
(252,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-02',N'Establish a cloud security policy',N'The organisation must approve and communicate a topic-specific policy for cloud-service use to relevant interested parties. The purpose is to provide clear direction for secure cloud use.',N'Provide clear direction for secure cloud use.',N'cloud policy; communication; interested party; governance',1,N'Merged into CLD-06 — Merged'),
(253,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-03',N'Define the cloud risk-management approach',N'The organisation must define and communicate how cloud security risks will be identified, assessed, treated and monitored. It must monitor and review cloud use. It must assess and accept cloud risks. The purpose is to apply a consistent risk-based approach to cloud services. It also aims to keep cloud risk within approved limits over time. It also aims to make cloud risk decisions explicit and accountable.',N'Apply a consistent risk-based approach to cloud services. Keep cloud risk within approved limits over time; Make cloud risk decisions explicit and accountable.',N'cloud risk; assessment; treatment; communication; monitoring; cloud monitoring; review; evaluation; ongoing use; risk; cloud risk assessment; residual risk; management acceptance',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(254,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-04',N'Define cloud security requirements',N'The organisation must document all relevant information-security requirements for each cloud service. It must govern the cloud-service life cycle. It must manage multi-cloud controls and interfaces. It must control cloud subcontracting. The purpose is to ensure cloud services meet organizational protection needs. It also aims to manage cloud security consistently from selection through exit. It also aims to prevent security gaps between interconnected cloud environments. It also aims to preserve protection when other providers support the cloud service.',N'Ensure cloud services meet organizational protection needs. Manage cloud security consistently from selection through exit; Prevent security gaps between interconnected cloud environments; Preserve protection when other providers support the cloud service.',N'cloud lifecycle; acquisition; use; management; exit; cloud requirement; confidentiality; integrity; availability; handling; multi-cloud; interface; control; service change',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(255,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-05',N'Set cloud selection criteria and usage scope',N'The organisation must define security-based selection criteria and the approved scope of use for each cloud service. The purpose is to use cloud services only where suitability and boundaries are clear.',N'Use cloud services only where suitability and boundaries are clear.',N'selection criteria; usage scope; approval; cloud service',1,N'Merged into CLD-06 — Merged'),
(256,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-06',N'Assign cloud roles and responsibilities',N'The organisation must define accountable roles for acquiring, configuring, operating, monitoring and exiting cloud services. It must establish a cloud security policy. It must set cloud selection criteria and usage scope. It must manage cloud access controls. The purpose is to ensure every cloud-security activity has a clear owner. It also aims to provide clear direction for secure cloud use. It also aims to use cloud services only where suitability and boundaries are clear. It also aims to restrict cloud access to authorized entities and purposes.',N'Ensure every cloud-security activity has a clear owner. Provide clear direction for secure cloud use; Use cloud services only where suitability and boundaries are clear; Restrict cloud access to authorized entities and purposes.',N'cloud policy; communication; interested party; governance; selection criteria; usage scope; approval; cloud service; cloud role; responsibility; accountability; management; cloud access; authorization',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(257,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-07',N'Maintain the shared-responsibility model',N'The organisation must document which controls are managed by the provider and which remain with the organization as customer. The purpose is to prevent control gaps or duplicated assumptions.',N'Prevent control gaps or duplicated assumptions.',N'shared responsibility; provider control; customer control; matrix',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(258,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-08',N'Use provider security capabilities',N'The organisation must identify, configure and use relevant security capabilities offered by the cloud provider. It must assess peer-provider and subcontractor changes. It must maintain close provider contact. The purpose is to gain the intended protection from available cloud controls. It also aims to maintain visibility and approval of downstream cloud dependencies. It also aims to support rapid mutual communication about cloud security.',N'Gain the intended protection from available cloud controls. Maintain visibility and approval of downstream cloud dependencies; Support rapid mutual communication about cloud security.',N'provider capability; security feature; configuration; utilization; peer provider; subcontractor change; downstream dependency; provider contact; communication; escalation; relationship',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(259,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-09',N'Obtain cloud-control assurance',N'The organisation must define and apply methods for obtaining assurance over provider-implemented security controls. It must support cloud digital evidence. The purpose is to confirm provider controls are suitably designed and effective. It also aims to preserve usable evidence for investigation and legal needs.',N'Confirm provider controls are suitably designed and effective. Preserve usable evidence for investigation and legal needs.',N'cloud assurance; attestation; audit; provider control; evidence; digital evidence; cloud provider; jurisdiction; investigation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(260,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-10',N'Manage multi-cloud controls and interfaces',N'The organisation must coordinate controls, interfaces and service changes across multiple cloud services and providers. The purpose is to prevent security gaps between interconnected cloud environments.',N'Prevent security gaps between interconnected cloud environments.',N'multi-cloud; interface; control; service change; provider',1,N'Merged into CLD-04 — Merged'),
(261,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-11',N'Manage cloud security incidents',N'The organisation must define procedures and responsibilities for cloud-related security incidents. It must require cloud malware protection. It must require dedicated cloud incident support. The purpose is to enable coordinated and timely cloud incident response. It also aims to detect and prevent malicious software affecting cloud services. It also aims to obtain timely provider assistance for containment and recovery.',N'Enable coordinated and timely cloud incident response. Detect and prevent malicious software affecting cloud services; Obtain timely provider assistance for containment and recovery.',N'cloud incident; procedure; responsibility; response; escalation; cloud malware; monitoring; protection; detection; incident support; cloud provider; recovery',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(262,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-12',N'Monitor and review cloud use',N'The organisation must regularly monitor, review and evaluate ongoing cloud use and related security risks. The purpose is to keep cloud risk within approved limits over time.',N'Keep cloud risk within approved limits over time.',N'cloud monitoring; review; evaluation; ongoing use; risk',1,N'Merged into CLD-03 — Merged'),
(263,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-13',N'Plan cloud change and exit',N'The organisation must define how cloud use will be changed or stopped, including tested exit strategies. It must require cloud exit support and availability. The purpose is to maintain security, portability and continuity when leaving a service. It also aims to avoid disruption or data loss during cloud exit.',N'Maintain security, portability and continuity when leaving a service. Avoid disruption or data loss during cloud exit.',N'cloud exit; change; portability; termination; strategy; exit support; service availability; migration; cloud termination',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(264,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-14',N'Review cloud service agreements',N'The organisation must review every cloud agreement for confidentiality, integrity, availability, information handling and suitable service objectives. It must monitor cloud commitments and failures. The purpose is to ensure even standard non-negotiable terms are understood and assessed. It also aims to detect and correct cloud-service commitment failures.',N'Ensure even standard non-negotiable terms are understood and assessed. Detect and correct cloud-service commitment failures.',N'cloud agreement; CIA; information handling; service objective; service characteristic; commitment; failure reporting; monitoring',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(265,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-15',N'Assess and accept cloud risks',N'The organisation must perform cloud risk assessments, identify residual risks clearly and obtain appropriate management acceptance. The purpose is to make cloud risk decisions explicit and accountable.',N'Make cloud risk decisions explicit and accountable.',N'cloud risk assessment; residual risk; management acceptance',1,N'Merged into CLD-03 — Merged'),
(266,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-16',N'Require accepted architecture standards',N'The organisation must require cloud architecture and infrastructure solutions based on accepted industry standards. The purpose is to use credible and supportable cloud foundations.',N'Use credible and supportable cloud foundations.',N'industry standard; architecture; infrastructure; cloud solution',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(267,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-17',N'Manage cloud access controls',N'The organisation must ensure cloud access controls meet organizational requirements. The purpose is to restrict cloud access to authorized entities and purposes.',N'Restrict cloud access to authorized entities and purposes.',N'cloud access; authorization; identity; least privilege',1,N'Merged into CLD-06 — Merged'),
(268,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-18',N'Require cloud malware protection',N'The organisation must require suitable malware monitoring and protection in the cloud environment. The purpose is to detect and prevent malicious software affecting cloud services.',N'Detect and prevent malicious software affecting cloud services.',N'cloud malware; monitoring; protection; detection',1,N'Merged into CLD-11 — Merged'),
(269,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-19',N'Control cloud data locations and jurisdictions',N'The organisation must process and store sensitive information only in approved geographic locations and legal jurisdictions. It must protect cloud data and configuration backups. The purpose is to meet location, legal and regulatory handling requirements. It also aims to enable reliable cloud recovery without exposing backup information.',N'Meet location, legal and regulatory handling requirements. Enable reliable cloud recovery without exposing backup information.',N'data location; jurisdiction; sensitive information; residency; cloud backup; data; configuration; secure management; recovery',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(270,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-20',N'Require dedicated cloud incident support',N'The organisation must ensure the provider supplies appropriate support during cloud security incidents. The purpose is to obtain timely provider assistance for containment and recovery.',N'Obtain timely provider assistance for containment and recovery.',N'incident support; cloud provider; response; recovery',1,N'Merged into CLD-11 — Merged'),
(271,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-21',N'Control cloud subcontracting',N'The organisation must require security obligations to flow to cloud subcontractors or prohibit subcontracting where necessary. The purpose is to preserve protection when other providers support the cloud service.',N'Preserve protection when other providers support the cloud service.',N'cloud subcontractor; flow-down; external supplier; prohibition',1,N'Merged into CLD-04 — Merged'),
(272,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-22',N'Support cloud digital evidence',N'The organisation must require provider support for gathering digital evidence across applicable legal jurisdictions. The purpose is to preserve usable evidence for investigation and legal needs.',N'Preserve usable evidence for investigation and legal needs.',N'digital evidence; cloud provider; jurisdiction; investigation',1,N'Merged into CLD-09 — Merged'),
(273,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-23',N'Require cloud exit support and availability',N'The organisation must require sufficient provider support and service availability during the approved exit period. The purpose is to avoid disruption or data loss during cloud exit.',N'Avoid disruption or data loss during cloud exit.',N'exit support; service availability; migration; cloud termination',1,N'Merged into CLD-13 — Merged'),
(274,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-24',N'Protect cloud data and configuration backups',N'The organisation must require suitable backups of data and configurations and secure management of those backups. The purpose is to enable reliable cloud recovery without exposing backup information.',N'Enable reliable cloud recovery without exposing backup information.',N'cloud backup; data; configuration; secure management; recovery',1,N'Merged into CLD-19 — Merged'),
(275,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-25',N'Return organization-owned cloud information',N'The organisation must require providers to supply and return owned data, configurations and source code during service and at termination. The purpose is to preserve ownership, access and portability of organizational information.',N'Preserve ownership, access and portability of organizational information.',N'data return; configuration; source code; ownership; portability',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(276,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-26',N'Require advance notice of material cloud changes',N'The organisation must require notice before substantive customer-impacting changes to cloud-service delivery. The purpose is to allow risk assessment and action before material changes occur.',N'Allow risk assessment and action before material changes occur.',N'advance notice; material change; customer impact; cloud service',1,N'Merged into CLD-27 — Merged'),
(277,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-27',N'Assess cloud infrastructure changes',N'The organisation must review provider relocation, reconfiguration and hardware or software changes affecting the service. It must require advance notice of material cloud changes. It must assess cloud jurisdiction changes. The purpose is to control risk from changes to the technical cloud foundation. It also aims to allow risk assessment and action before material changes occur. It also aims to prevent unauthorized location or jurisdiction exposure.',N'Control risk from changes to the technical cloud foundation. Allow risk assessment and action before material changes occur; Prevent unauthorized location or jurisdiction exposure.',N'advance notice; material change; customer impact; cloud service; relocation; reconfiguration; hardware; software; infrastructure change; jurisdiction change; geographic location; processing; storage',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(278,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-28',N'Assess cloud jurisdiction changes',N'The organisation must review proposed movement of information processing or storage into a new geographic or legal jurisdiction. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized location or jurisdiction exposure.',N'Prevent unauthorized location or jurisdiction exposure.',N'jurisdiction change; geographic location; processing; storage',1,N'Merged into CLD-27 — Merged'),
(279,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-29',N'Assess peer-provider and subcontractor changes',N'The organisation must review new or changed peer cloud providers and other subcontractors before they affect the service. The purpose is to maintain visibility and approval of downstream cloud dependencies.',N'Maintain visibility and approval of downstream cloud dependencies.',N'peer provider; subcontractor change; downstream dependency',1,N'Merged into CLD-08 — Merged'),
(280,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-30',N'Maintain close provider contact',N'The organisation must maintain current operational and security contacts with each cloud provider. The purpose is to support rapid mutual communication about cloud security.',N'Support rapid mutual communication about cloud security.',N'provider contact; communication; escalation; relationship',1,N'Merged into CLD-08 — Merged'),
(281,24,N'5.23',N'CLD-31',N'Monitor cloud commitments and failures',N'The organisation must operate a mutual mechanism to monitor service characteristics and report failures against agreement commitments. The purpose is to detect and correct cloud-service commitment failures.',N'Detect and correct cloud-service commitment failures.',N'service characteristic; commitment; failure reporting; monitoring',1,N'Merged into CLD-14 — Merged'),
(282,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-01',N'Govern incident management preparedness',N'The organisation must define, establish, approve and maintain processes for planning and preparing to manage information security incidents. It must restrict incident handling to competent personnel. It must set management-approved incident objectives. It must maintain a scenario-based incident plan. The purpose is to enable quick, effective, consistent and orderly incident handling. It also aims to prevent ineffective or harmful unqualified response actions. It also aims to align incident handling with organizational priorities. It also aims to prepare the organization for credible incident situations.',N'Enable quick, effective, consistent and orderly incident handling. Prevent ineffective or harmful unqualified response actions; Align incident handling with organizational priorities; Prepare the organization for credible incident situations.',N'incident management; planning; preparation; governance; process; competence; authorization; incident handler; restriction; management objective; priority; approval; incident governance; incident plan',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(283,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-02',N'Define incident roles and responsibilities',N'The organisation must assign accountable roles, authorities, deputies and responsibilities for incident management procedures. It must communicate incident arrangements. It must log incident management activities. It must use incident forms reports and reporter feedback. The purpose is to ensure incident duties and decision rights are clear. It also aims to ensure all parties know how to act and coordinate. It also aims to preserve accountability and evidence for review. It also aims to support complete reporting and reinforce reporting behaviour.',N'Ensure incident duties and decision rights are clear. Ensure all parties know how to act and coordinate; Preserve accountability and evidence for review; Support complete reporting and reinforce reporting behaviour.',N'incident role; responsibility; authority; deputy; accountability; incident communication; interested party; role; procedure; incident log; action; decision; timestamp; protection',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(284,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-03',N'Communicate incident arrangements',N'The organisation must communicate incident processes, roles and responsibilities to relevant internal and external interested parties. The purpose is to ensure all parties know how to act and coordinate.',N'Ensure all parties know how to act and coordinate.',N'incident communication; interested party; role; procedure',1,N'Merged into IRP-02 — Merged'),
(285,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-04',N'Provide a common event-reporting method',N'The organisation must establish accessible and consistent channels, instructions and points of contact for reporting security events. It must define immediate event-reporting actions. The purpose is to make event reporting simple, prompt and reliable. It also aims to protect evidence and prevent uncontrolled responses.',N'Make event reporting simple, prompt and reliable. Protect evidence and prevent uncontrolled responses.',N'event reporting; channel; point of contact; instruction; immediate action; event details; report; coordinated action',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(286,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-05',N'Administer and document incidents',N'The organisation must define case administration and documentation requirements throughout the incident life cycle. The purpose is to maintain complete, controlled and traceable incident records.',N'Maintain complete, controlled and traceable incident records.',N'incident administration; documentation; case record; lifecycle',1,N'Merged into IRP-08 — Merged'),
(287,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-06',N'Prepare incident detection and intake',N'The organisation must define how human and automated alerts are received, acknowledged and entered into the incident process. It must prepare monitoring detection classification and reporting. The purpose is to ensure potential incidents enter the process without delay. It also aims to create an end-to-end path from observation to reported incident.',N'Ensure potential incidents enter the process without delay. Create an end-to-end path from observation to reported incident.',N'detection; alert; intake; acknowledgement; automation; monitoring; classification; analysis; reporting',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(288,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-07',N'Prepare triage and prioritization',N'The organisation must define triage, severity, consequence and priority methods for potential incidents. It must define severity-based resolution targets. The purpose is to direct urgent and serious incidents to the right response level. It also aims to drive timely action according to incident risk.',N'Direct urgent and serious incidents to the right response level. Drive timely action according to incident risk.',N'triage; priority; severity; consequence; incident; resolution time; escalation; target',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(289,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-08',N'Prepare incident analysis',N'The organisation must define analysis methods, information needs and specialist support for understanding incidents. It must administer and document incidents. It must prepare incident communications and coordination. It must define event-to-incident evaluation criteria. The purpose is to support accurate and timely incident decisions. It also aims to maintain complete, controlled and traceable incident records. It also aims to maintain controlled information flow and coordinated action. It also aims to support consistent incident identification.',N'Support accurate and timely incident decisions. Maintain complete, controlled and traceable incident records; Maintain controlled information flow and coordinated action; Support consistent incident identification.',N'incident administration; documentation; case record; lifecycle; incident analysis; information; specialist; assessment; incident communication; coordination; responder; stakeholder; event evaluation; incident criteria',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(290,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-09',N'Prepare incident communications and coordination',N'The organisation must define communication and coordination arrangements among responders and interested parties. The purpose is to maintain controlled information flow and coordinated action.',N'Maintain controlled information flow and coordinated action.',N'incident communication; coordination; responder; stakeholder',1,N'Merged into IRP-08 — Merged'),
(291,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-10',N'Establish the incident response process',N'The organisation must define procedures for assessing, responding to, recovering from and learning from incidents. The purpose is to provide a complete and repeatable response framework.',N'Provide a complete and repeatable response framework.',N'incident response; assessment; recovery; learning; procedure',1,N'Merged into IRP-19 — Merged'),
(292,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-11',N'Restrict incident handling to competent personnel',N'The organisation must permit incident handling only by personnel with approved competence and authority. The purpose is to prevent ineffective or harmful unqualified response actions.',N'Prevent ineffective or harmful unqualified response actions.',N'competence; authorization; incident handler; restriction',1,N'Merged into IRP-01 — Merged'),
(293,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-12',N'Provide responder procedures and training',N'The organisation must give incident personnel current procedure documentation and periodic role-based training. It must manage responder development and certification. The purpose is to equip responders to perform their duties correctly. It also aims to sustain suitable incident-response capability over time.',N'Equip responders to perform their duties correctly. Sustain suitable incident-response capability over time.',N'responder procedure; periodic training; documentation; competence; certification; training need; professional development; responder',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(294,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-13',N'Manage responder development and certification',N'The organisation must identify and maintain required training, certification and continuing professional development for responders. The purpose is to sustain suitable incident-response capability over time.',N'Sustain suitable incident-response capability over time.',N'certification; training need; professional development; responder',1,N'Merged into IRP-12 — Merged'),
(295,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-14',N'Set management-approved incident objectives',N'The organisation must agree incident-management objectives, priorities and governance expectations with management. The purpose is to align incident handling with organizational priorities.',N'Align incident handling with organizational priorities.',N'management objective; priority; approval; incident governance',1,N'Merged into IRP-01 — Merged'),
(296,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-15',N'Define severity-based resolution targets',N'The organisation must set resolution and escalation time frames based on potential consequence and severity. The purpose is to drive timely action according to incident risk.',N'Drive timely action according to incident risk.',N'resolution time; escalation; severity; consequence; target',1,N'Merged into IRP-07 — Merged'),
(297,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-16',N'Maintain a scenario-based incident plan',N'The organisation must create and maintain an incident-management plan covering relevant threat and disruption scenarios. The purpose is to prepare the organization for credible incident situations.',N'Prepare the organization for credible incident situations.',N'incident plan; scenario; threat; disruption; preparedness',1,N'Merged into IRP-01 — Merged'),
(298,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-17',N'Define event-to-incident evaluation criteria',N'The organisation must define criteria and procedures for deciding when a security event is an incident. The purpose is to support consistent incident identification.',N'Support consistent incident identification.',N'event evaluation; incident criteria; decision; categorization',1,N'Merged into IRP-08 — Merged'),
(299,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-18',N'Prepare monitoring detection classification and reporting',N'The organisation must define human and automated procedures to monitor, detect, classify, analyse and report events and incidents. The purpose is to create an end-to-end path from observation to reported incident.',N'Create an end-to-end path from observation to reported incident.',N'monitoring; detection; classification; analysis; reporting',1,N'Merged into IRP-06 — Merged'),
(300,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-19',N'Plan incident escalation and closure',N'The organisation must define response, escalation and management-to-conclusion procedures by incident type and category. It must establish the incident response process. It must plan crisis and continuity activation. It must plan controlled incident recovery. The purpose is to ensure incidents progress through controlled stages to closure. It also aims to provide a complete and repeatable response framework. It also aims to coordinate severe-incident response with continuity arrangements. It also aims to restore services safely without reintroducing risk.',N'Ensure incidents progress through controlled stages to closure. Provide a complete and repeatable response framework; Coordinate severe-incident response with continuity arrangements; Restore services safely without reintroducing risk.',N'incident response; assessment; recovery; learning; procedure; response; escalation; type; category; closure; crisis management; continuity plan; activation; severe incident',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(301,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-20',N'Plan crisis and continuity activation',N'The organisation must define when and how crisis management and business continuity plans are activated during incidents. The purpose is to coordinate severe-incident response with continuity arrangements.',N'Coordinate severe-incident response with continuity arrangements.',N'crisis management; continuity plan; activation; severe incident',1,N'Merged into IRP-19 — Merged'),
(302,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-21',N'Plan controlled incident recovery',N'The organisation must define authorization, validation and monitoring steps for controlled recovery from incidents. The purpose is to restore services safely without reintroducing risk.',N'Restore services safely without reintroducing risk.',N'controlled recovery; authorization; validation; restoration',1,N'Merged into IRP-19 — Merged'),
(303,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-22',N'Coordinate external incident parties',N'The organisation must plan coordination with authorities, specialist groups, forums, suppliers and clients. It must meet external incident-reporting duties. The purpose is to improve response and limit wider consequences through external coordination. It also aims to meet legal and contractual deadlines and coordinate boundary-spanning incidents.',N'Improve response and limit wider consequences through external coordination. Meet legal and contractual deadlines and coordinate boundary-spanning incidents.',N'authority; supplier; client; forum; external coordination; external reporting; regulator; deadline; breach notification; cross-border',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(304,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-23',N'Log incident management activities',N'The organisation must define complete, protected and time-synchronized logging of incident decisions and actions. The purpose is to preserve accountability and evidence for review.',N'Preserve accountability and evidence for review.',N'incident log; action; decision; timestamp; protection',1,N'Merged into IRP-02 — Merged'),
(305,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-24',N'Prepare evidence handling',N'The organisation must define how potential evidence is identified, collected, protected, transferred and retained during incidents. The purpose is to preserve evidence integrity and usability.',N'Preserve evidence integrity and usability.',N'evidence; collection; chain of custody; retention; integrity',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(306,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-25',N'Prepare root-cause and post-mortem reviews',N'The organisation must define methods, ownership and timing for root-cause analysis and post-incident review. The purpose is to identify why incidents occurred and what must change.',N'Identify why incidents occurred and what must change.',N'root cause; post-mortem; review; corrective action',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(307,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-26',N'Capture lessons and improve controls',N'The organisation must define how lessons are recorded, approved and used to improve procedures, plans and controls. The purpose is to turn incident experience into stronger prevention and response.',N'Turn incident experience into stronger prevention and response.',N'lesson learned; improvement; control; procedure; plan',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(308,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-27',N'Define immediate event-reporting actions',N'The organisation must require personnel to record relevant details immediately, report to the contact point and take only coordinated actions. The purpose is to protect evidence and prevent uncontrolled responses.',N'Protect evidence and prevent uncontrolled responses.',N'immediate action; event details; report; coordinated action',1,N'Merged into IRP-04 — Merged'),
(309,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-28',N'Use incident forms reports and reporter feedback',N'The organisation must provide reporting forms, formal incident reports and feedback to reporters after closure where possible. The purpose is to support complete reporting and reinforce reporting behaviour.',N'Support complete reporting and reinforce reporting behaviour.',N'incident form; incident report; reporter feedback; closure',1,N'Merged into IRP-02 — Merged'),
(310,25,N'5.24',N'IRP-29',N'Meet external incident-reporting duties',N'The organisation must identify external notification duties and prepare to report to regulators and other parties within required time frames, including cross-border coordination. The purpose is to meet legal and contractual deadlines and coordinate boundary-spanning incidents.',N'Meet legal and contractual deadlines and coordinate boundary-spanning incidents.',N'external reporting; regulator; deadline; breach notification; cross-border',1,N'Merged into IRP-22 — Merged'),
(311,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-01',N'Govern security-event assessment',N'The organisation must define and maintain a controlled process for assessing security events and deciding whether they are incidents. It must define event-to-incident criteria. It must assess every reported security event. It must decide and communicate event status. The purpose is to ensure every security event receives a consistent and accountable decision. It also aims to prevent inconsistent or missed incident declarations. It also aims to ensure no reported event is left without formal assessment. It also aims to trigger the correct handling path without delay.',N'Ensure every security event receives a consistent and accountable decision. Prevent inconsistent or missed incident declarations; Ensure no reported event is left without formal assessment; Trigger the correct handling path without delay.',N'security event; assessment; decision; incident; governance; incident criteria; event; threshold; categorization; point of contact; every event; agreed scheme; incident decision; category',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(312,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-02',N'Maintain an agreed categorization scheme',N'The organisation must define and obtain approval for categories used to classify information security incidents. It must maintain an agreed prioritization scheme. The purpose is to apply consistent incident categories across the organization. It also aims to direct attention and resources according to urgency and impact.',N'Apply consistent incident categories across the organization. Direct attention and resources according to urgency and impact.',N'categorization scheme; category; approval; consistency; prioritization scheme; priority; urgency; incident',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(313,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-03',N'Maintain an agreed prioritization scheme',N'The organisation must define and approve priority levels for information security incidents. The purpose is to direct attention and resources according to urgency and impact.',N'Direct attention and resources according to urgency and impact.',N'prioritization scheme; priority; urgency; incident',1,N'Merged into EVA-02 — Merged'),
(314,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-04',N'Assess incident consequences',N'The organisation must define how actual and potential confidentiality, integrity, availability, operational, legal and stakeholder consequences are identified. The purpose is to base incident decisions on a complete view of possible harm.',N'Base incident decisions on a complete view of possible harm.',N'consequence; impact; confidentiality; integrity; availability',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(315,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-05',N'Define event-to-incident criteria',N'The organisation must maintain clear criteria for deciding whether an information security event qualifies as an incident. The purpose is to prevent inconsistent or missed incident declarations.',N'Prevent inconsistent or missed incident declarations.',N'incident criteria; event; threshold; categorization; decision',1,N'Merged into EVA-01 — Merged'),
(316,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-06',N'Assess every reported security event',N'The organisation must require the designated point of contact to assess each information security event using the agreed scheme. The purpose is to ensure no reported event is left without formal assessment.',N'Ensure no reported event is left without formal assessment.',N'point of contact; every event; assessment; agreed scheme',1,N'Merged into EVA-01 — Merged'),
(317,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-07',N'Use authorized incident decision-makers',N'The organisation must assign assessment and decision authority to personnel responsible for coordinating and responding to incidents. The purpose is to ensure decisions are made by competent and accountable personnel.',N'Ensure decisions are made by competent and accountable personnel.',N'authorized personnel; coordinator; responder; decision authority',1,N'Merged into EVA-09 — Merged'),
(318,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-08',N'Decide and communicate event status',N'The organisation must record whether each event is an incident, its category and priority, and communicate the decision to relevant responders. The purpose is to trigger the correct handling path without delay.',N'Trigger the correct handling path without delay.',N'incident decision; category; priority; communication; responder',1,N'Merged into EVA-01 — Merged'),
(319,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-09',N'Record assessment and decision details',N'The organisation must retain detailed assessment inputs, reasoning, decision, category, priority, decision-maker and timestamps. It must use authorized incident decision-makers. It must verify assessment quality and consistency. The purpose is to support future reference, accountability and verification. It also aims to ensure decisions are made by competent and accountable personnel. It also aims to keep event assessment accurate, repeatable and effective.',N'Support future reference, accountability and verification. Ensure decisions are made by competent and accountable personnel; Keep event assessment accurate, repeatable and effective.',N'authorized personnel; coordinator; responder; decision authority; assessment record; rationale; decision; timestamp; audit trail; quality review; consistency; misclassification; record completeness',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(320,26,N'5.25',N'EVA-10',N'Verify assessment quality and consistency',N'The organisation must review event decisions, scheme use, record completeness and misclassification trends, and correct weaknesses. The purpose is to keep event assessment accurate, repeatable and effective.',N'Keep event assessment accurate, repeatable and effective.',N'quality review; consistency; misclassification; record completeness',1,N'Merged into EVA-09 — Merged'),
(321,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-01',N'Govern documented incident response',N'The organisation must establish, approve, communicate and maintain procedures for responding to information security incidents. It must use a designated competent response team. It must activate crisis and continuity arrangements. It must log all response activities. The purpose is to ensure incidents are handled efficiently and consistently under documented procedures. It also aims to ensure qualified personnel lead and perform response actions. It also aims to coordinate severe-incident response and service continuity. It also aims to maintain a complete and accountable incident-response history.',N'Ensure incidents are handled efficiently and consistently under documented procedures. Ensure qualified personnel lead and perform response actions; Coordinate severe-incident response and service continuity; Maintain a complete and accountable incident-response history.',N'incident response; procedure; governance; communication; response team; competence; authority; availability; designation; crisis management; continuity plan; activation; threshold; response log',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(322,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-02',N'Use a designated competent response team',N'The organisation must assign incident response to a designated team with the authority, availability and competence required. The purpose is to ensure qualified personnel lead and perform response actions.',N'Ensure qualified personnel lead and perform response actions.',N'response team; competence; authority; availability; designation',1,N'Merged into IRS-01 — Merged'),
(323,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-03',N'Contain affected systems',N'The organisation must contain systems and services when incident consequences can spread, while considering operational and evidence needs. The purpose is to limit propagation and reduce further harm.',N'Limit propagation and reduce further harm.',N'containment; affected system; propagation; isolation; harm',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(324,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-04',N'Collect incident evidence promptly',N'The organisation must identify and collect relevant evidence as soon as possible after an incident occurs. The purpose is to preserve reliable evidence before it is lost or altered.',N'Preserve reliable evidence before it is lost or altered.',N'evidence collection; prompt; preservation; incident',1,N'Merged into IRS-05 — Merged'),
(325,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-05',N'Escalate incidents appropriately',N'The organisation must apply defined technical, management, legal and executive escalation according to incident severity and impact. It must collect incident evidence promptly. It must control recovery from incidents. It must formally close and record incidents. The purpose is to bring the right authority and resources into the response promptly. It also aims to preserve reliable evidence before it is lost or altered. It also aims to restore operations without reintroducing the incident or related weakness. It also aims to close incidents only after required actions and evidence are complete.',N'Bring the right authority and resources into the response promptly. Preserve reliable evidence before it is lost or altered; Restore operations without reintroducing the incident or related weakness; Close incidents only after required actions and evidence are complete.',N'evidence collection; prompt; preservation; incident; incident escalation; severity; management; authority; resource; incident recovery; validation; authorization; secure state; incident closure',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(326,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-06',N'Activate crisis and continuity arrangements',N'The organisation must invoke crisis management and business continuity plans when incident conditions meet defined thresholds. The purpose is to coordinate severe-incident response and service continuity.',N'Coordinate severe-incident response and service continuity.',N'crisis management; continuity plan; activation; threshold',1,N'Merged into IRS-01 — Merged'),
(327,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-07',N'Log all response activities',N'The organisation must record response decisions, actions, times, personnel, evidence and outcomes for later analysis. The purpose is to maintain a complete and accountable incident-response history.',N'Maintain a complete and accountable incident-response history.',N'response log; decision; action; timestamp; audit trail',1,N'Merged into IRS-01 — Merged'),
(328,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-08',N'Communicate incidents on a need-to-know basis',N'The organisation must communicate incident existence and relevant details to authorized internal and external parties according to need-to-know. It must coordinate with external parties. The purpose is to share necessary information without causing avoidable disclosure or confusion. It also aims to improve response effectiveness and reduce consequences for others.',N'Share necessary information without causing avoidable disclosure or confusion. Improve response effectiveness and reduce consequences for others.',N'incident communication; need-to-know; internal; external; confidentiality; authority; supplier; client; forum; external coordination',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(329,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-09',N'Coordinate with external parties',N'The organisation must coordinate response with authorities, specialist groups, forums, suppliers and clients where appropriate. The purpose is to improve response effectiveness and reduce consequences for others.',N'Improve response effectiveness and reduce consequences for others.',N'authority; supplier; client; forum; external coordination',1,N'Merged into IRS-08 — Merged'),
(330,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-10',N'Control recovery from incidents',N'The organisation must authorize, validate and monitor recovery actions so affected systems return to a secure and stable state. The purpose is to restore operations without reintroducing the incident or related weakness.',N'Restore operations without reintroducing the incident or related weakness.',N'incident recovery; validation; authorization; secure state',1,N'Merged into IRS-05 — Merged'),
(331,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-11',N'Formally close and record incidents',N'The organisation must confirm response completion, obtain closure approval and retain the final incident record. The purpose is to close incidents only after required actions and evidence are complete.',N'Close incidents only after required actions and evidence are complete.',N'incident closure; approval; final record; completion',1,N'Merged into IRS-05 — Merged'),
(332,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-12',N'Conduct forensic analysis when required',N'The organisation must perform authorized information security forensic analysis using suitable methods and competent personnel. It must perform and communicate root-cause analysis. The purpose is to establish reliable facts and support investigation or legal needs. It also aims to understand why the incident occurred and inform corrective action.',N'Establish reliable facts and support investigation or legal needs. Understand why the incident occurred and inform corrective action.',N'forensic analysis; authorization; competence; investigation; root cause; post-incident analysis; documentation; communication',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(333,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-13',N'Perform and communicate root-cause analysis',N'The organisation must conduct documented post-incident analysis to identify root cause and communicate results under defined procedures. The purpose is to understand why the incident occurred and inform corrective action.',N'Understand why the incident occurred and inform corrective action.',N'root cause; post-incident analysis; documentation; communication',1,N'Merged into IRS-12 — Merged'),
(334,27,N'5.26',N'IRS-14',N'Remediate vulnerabilities and control weaknesses',N'The organisation must identify and manage vulnerabilities and control weaknesses that caused, contributed to or failed to prevent the incident. The purpose is to reduce the chance or impact of recurrence.',N'Reduce the chance or impact of recurrence.',N'vulnerability; control weakness; remediation; recurrence',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(335,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-01',N'Govern incident learning and improvement',N'The organisation must define and maintain procedures for using incident knowledge to strengthen security controls. The purpose is to turn incident experience into managed and accountable improvement.',N'Turn incident experience into managed and accountable improvement.',N'incident learning; improvement; governance; security control',1,N'Merged into LRN-02 — Merged'),
(336,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-02',N'Classify incident types for learning',N'The organisation must define consistent incident-type categories suitable for measurement and trend analysis. It must govern incident learning and improvement. It must monitor incident trends and patterns. It must identify recurring and serious incidents. The purpose is to enable reliable comparison and identification of recurring patterns. It also aims to turn incident experience into managed and accountable improvement. It also aims to detect worsening conditions and improvement opportunities. It also aims to focus improvement on significant and repeated problems.',N'Enable reliable comparison and identification of recurring patterns. Turn incident experience into managed and accountable improvement; Detect worsening conditions and improvement opportunities; Focus improvement on significant and repeated problems.',N'incident learning; improvement; governance; security control; incident type; classification; trend; measurement; incident trend; pattern; severity; cause; analysis; recurring incident',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(337,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-03',N'Quantify incident volumes',N'The organisation must collect and monitor the number and frequency of incidents by relevant category and period. It must quantify incident costs. It must improve the incident management plan. It must improve incident scenarios and procedures. The purpose is to understand incident frequency and changes over time. It also aims to understand financial and resource consequences of incidents. It also aims to keep the plan aligned with real incident experience. It also aims to make future responses more realistic and effective.',N'Understand incident frequency and changes over time. Understand financial and resource consequences of incidents; Keep the plan aligned with real incident experience; Make future responses more realistic and effective.',N'incident volume; count; frequency; monitoring; trend; incident cost; financial impact; resource; measurement; incident plan; evaluation; update; lesson learned; incident scenario',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(338,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-04',N'Quantify incident costs',N'The organisation must define, collect and monitor direct and indirect incident costs using consistent methods. The purpose is to understand financial and resource consequences of incidents.',N'Understand financial and resource consequences of incidents.',N'incident cost; financial impact; resource; measurement',1,N'Merged into LRN-03 — Merged'),
(339,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-05',N'Monitor incident trends and patterns',N'The organisation must analyse incident types, volumes, costs, severity and causes to identify meaningful trends. The purpose is to detect worsening conditions and improvement opportunities.',N'Detect worsening conditions and improvement opportunities.',N'incident trend; pattern; severity; cause; analysis',1,N'Merged into LRN-02 — Merged'),
(340,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-06',N'Improve the incident management plan',N'The organisation must use evaluated incident information to update the incident-management plan. The purpose is to keep the plan aligned with real incident experience.',N'Keep the plan aligned with real incident experience.',N'incident plan; evaluation; update; lesson learned',1,N'Merged into LRN-03 — Merged'),
(341,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-07',N'Improve incident scenarios and procedures',N'The organisation must update response scenarios, playbooks and procedures using lessons from actual incidents. The purpose is to make future responses more realistic and effective.',N'Make future responses more realistic and effective.',N'incident scenario; procedure; playbook; improvement',1,N'Merged into LRN-03 — Merged'),
(342,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-08',N'Identify recurring and serious incidents',N'The organisation must detect recurring or serious incidents and investigate their common characteristics and causes. The purpose is to focus improvement on significant and repeated problems.',N'Focus improvement on significant and repeated problems.',N'recurring incident; serious incident; pattern; cause',1,N'Merged into LRN-02 — Merged'),
(343,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-09',N'Update security risk assessments',N'The organisation must use incident causes, trends and consequences to update information security risk assessments. It must use incidents in awareness and training. The purpose is to keep risk understanding grounded in actual events. It also aims to make security learning practical and relevant to users.',N'Keep risk understanding grounded in actual events. Make security learning practical and relevant to users.',N'risk assessment; incident cause; trend; consequence; update; awareness; training; incident example; response; prevention',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(344,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-10',N'Determine and implement additional controls',N'The organisation must select, approve and implement controls needed to reduce the likelihood or consequences of similar incidents. The purpose is to prevent recurrence and limit future impact.',N'Prevent recurrence and limit future impact.',N'additional control; implementation; likelihood; consequence; recurrence',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(345,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-11',N'Use incidents in awareness and training',N'The organisation must use suitable incident examples to teach what can happen, how to respond and how to avoid recurrence. The purpose is to make security learning practical and relevant to users.',N'Make security learning practical and relevant to users.',N'awareness; training; incident example; response; prevention',1,N'Merged into LRN-09 — Merged'),
(346,28,N'5.27',N'LRN-12',N'Verify improvement effectiveness',N'The organisation must track lesson actions to closure and confirm that plan, risk, control and training improvements achieve the intended result. The purpose is to ensure lessons produce measurable and lasting improvement.',N'Ensure lessons produce measurable and lasting improvement.',N'action closure; effectiveness; verification; improvement',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(347,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-01',N'Govern security evidence management',N'The organisation must establish, approve and implement procedures for managing evidence related to information security events. It must identify potential evidence. It must collect evidence correctly. It must preserve evidence. The purpose is to ensure evidence is managed consistently and effectively. It also aims to prevent relevant evidence from being overlooked or destroyed. It also aims to obtain evidence without unnecessary loss, contamination or alteration. It also aims to maintain evidence integrity and availability for proceedings.',N'Ensure evidence is managed consistently and effectively. Prevent relevant evidence from being overlooked or destroyed; Obtain evidence without unnecessary loss, contamination or alteration; Maintain evidence integrity and availability for proceedings.',N'evidence management; procedure; governance; security event; evidence identification; scope; priority; evidence collection; source; contamination; control; evidence preservation; integrity; protection',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(348,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-02',N'Identify potential evidence',N'The organisation must define how potential physical and digital evidence is recognized, scoped and prioritized when an event is detected. The purpose is to prevent relevant evidence from being overlooked or destroyed.',N'Prevent relevant evidence from being overlooked or destroyed.',N'evidence identification; scope; priority; security event',1,N'Merged into EVD-01 — Merged'),
(349,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-03',N'Collect evidence correctly',N'The organisation must define and follow controlled methods for collecting evidence from relevant sources. The purpose is to obtain evidence without unnecessary loss, contamination or alteration.',N'Obtain evidence without unnecessary loss, contamination or alteration.',N'evidence collection; source; contamination; control',1,N'Merged into EVD-01 — Merged'),
(350,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-04',N'Acquire digital evidence correctly',N'The organisation must define forensic acquisition methods for creating reliable captures or copies of digital evidence. It must maintain evidence admissibility. It must use suitable validated evidence tools. It must confirm authority to collect digital evidence. The purpose is to produce evidence copies suitable for analysis and verification. It also aims to support reliable use of evidence in formal proceedings. It also aims to ensure evidence tools produce reliable and repeatable results. It also aims to prevent unlawful or unauthorized evidence collection.',N'Produce evidence copies suitable for analysis and verification. Support reliable use of evidence in formal proceedings; Ensure evidence tools produce reliable and repeatable results; Prevent unlawful or unauthorized evidence collection.',N'digital evidence; acquisition; forensic image; copy; admissibility; court; disciplinary forum; legal evidence; forensic tool; validation; qualification; reliability; collection authority; entitlement',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(351,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-05',N'Preserve evidence',N'The organisation must protect evidence from alteration, damage, loss or unauthorized access throughout its life cycle. The purpose is to maintain evidence integrity and availability for proceedings.',N'Maintain evidence integrity and availability for proceedings.',N'evidence preservation; integrity; protection; retention',1,N'Merged into EVD-01 — Merged'),
(352,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-06',N'Prepare for disciplinary and legal action',N'The organisation must align evidence procedures with likely internal disciplinary, regulatory and legal uses. The purpose is to keep collected evidence usable for the intended action.',N'Keep collected evidence usable for the intended action.',N'disciplinary action; legal action; regulator; evidence use',1,N'Merged into EVD-18 — Merged'),
(353,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-07',N'Address jurisdictional requirements',N'The organisation must identify and apply evidence requirements across relevant national and legal jurisdictions. The purpose is to maximize the chance that evidence is accepted wherever needed.',N'Maximize the chance that evidence is accepted wherever needed.',N'jurisdiction; legal requirement; admissibility; cross-border',1,N'Merged into EVD-18 — Merged'),
(354,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-08',N'Handle different storage media',N'The organisation must define evidence instructions for each relevant storage-media type. It must use qualified evidence personnel. The purpose is to collect and preserve evidence appropriately across media. It also aims to strengthen the reliability and value of preserved evidence.',N'Collect and preserve evidence appropriately across media. Strengthen the reliability and value of preserved evidence.',N'storage media; evidence handling; device; procedure; qualified personnel; certification; authorization; competence',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(355,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-09',N'Handle powered-on and powered-off devices',N'The organisation must define different evidence actions according to device state and volatility. The purpose is to avoid loss or alteration caused by unsuitable device handling.',N'Avoid loss or alteration caused by unsuitable device handling.',N'powered on; powered off; volatile data; device state',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(356,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-10',N'Maintain evidence admissibility',N'The organisation must collect and manage evidence in a manner suitable for national courts or disciplinary forums. The purpose is to support reliable use of evidence in formal proceedings.',N'Support reliable use of evidence in formal proceedings.',N'admissibility; court; disciplinary forum; legal evidence',1,N'Merged into EVD-04 — Merged'),
(357,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-11',N'Prove record completeness and integrity',N'The organisation must maintain controls and evidence showing records are complete and have not been tampered with. It must maintain chain of custody. The purpose is to demonstrate that evidential records remain trustworthy. It also aims to preserve accountability and evidence integrity across hand-offs.',N'Demonstrate that evidential records remain trustworthy. Preserve accountability and evidence integrity across hand-offs.',N'record completeness; integrity; tamper; authenticity; chain of custody; transfer; possession; access; disposition',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(358,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-12',N'Verify electronic copies against originals',N'The organisation must use documented verification to show electronic evidence copies are identical to their originals. It must verify source-system operation. The purpose is to demonstrate the reliability of forensic copies. It also aims to support confidence in the accuracy of gathered evidence.',N'Demonstrate the reliability of forensic copies. Support confidence in the accuracy of gathered evidence.',N'electronic evidence; original; copy; hash; verification; source system; operation; timestamp; reliability; record',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(359,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-13',N'Verify source-system operation',N'The organisation must retain evidence that source systems were operating correctly when evidential records were created. The purpose is to support confidence in the accuracy of gathered evidence.',N'Support confidence in the accuracy of gathered evidence.',N'source system; operation; timestamp; reliability; record',1,N'Merged into EVD-12 — Merged'),
(360,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-14',N'Maintain chain of custody',N'The organisation must record possession, transfer, access, storage and handling of evidence from collection through final disposition. The purpose is to preserve accountability and evidence integrity across hand-offs.',N'Preserve accountability and evidence integrity across hand-offs.',N'chain of custody; transfer; possession; access; disposition',1,N'Merged into EVD-11 — Merged'),
(361,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-15',N'Use qualified evidence personnel',N'The organisation must use appropriately trained, authorized and, where available, certified personnel for evidence work. The purpose is to strengthen the reliability and value of preserved evidence.',N'Strengthen the reliability and value of preserved evidence.',N'qualified personnel; certification; authorization; competence',1,N'Merged into EVD-08 — Merged'),
(362,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-16',N'Use suitable validated evidence tools',N'The organisation must select, control and, where available, qualify tools used to collect, acquire and preserve evidence. The purpose is to ensure evidence tools produce reliable and repeatable results.',N'Ensure evidence tools produce reliable and repeatable results.',N'forensic tool; validation; qualification; reliability',1,N'Merged into EVD-04 — Merged'),
(363,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-17',N'Confirm authority to collect digital evidence',N'The organisation must verify the organization’s legal and contractual entitlement before collecting evidence across organizational or jurisdictional boundaries. The purpose is to prevent unlawful or unauthorized evidence collection.',N'Prevent unlawful or unauthorized evidence collection.',N'collection authority; entitlement; boundary; digital evidence',1,N'Merged into EVD-04 — Merged'),
(364,29,N'5.28',N'EVD-18',N'Engage legal or law enforcement early',N'The organisation must seek timely legal or law-enforcement advice when legal action may be contemplated and evidence needs are uncertain. It must prepare for disciplinary and legal action. It must address jurisdictional requirements. The purpose is to protect necessary evidence before seriousness and legal needs are fully known. It also aims to keep collected evidence usable for the intended action. It also aims to maximize the chance that evidence is accepted wherever needed.',N'Protect necessary evidence before seriousness and legal needs are fully known. Keep collected evidence usable for the intended action; Maximize the chance that evidence is accepted wherever needed.',N'disciplinary action; legal action; regulator; evidence use; jurisdiction; legal requirement; admissibility; cross-border; legal advice; law enforcement; early involvement; evidence need',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(365,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-01',N'Govern information security during disruption',N'The organisation must define, approve and maintain how information and associated assets will be protected during disruption. It must identify disruption security requirements. It must maintain existing controls during disruption. It must apply compensating controls during disruption. The purpose is to maintain an appropriate level of information security under abnormal conditions. It also aims to make required protection explicit for each credible disruption. It also aims to avoid unnecessary reduction in protection under pressure. It also aims to reduce residual risk created by unavailable controls.',N'Maintain an appropriate level of information security under abnormal conditions. Make required protection explicit for each credible disruption; Avoid unnecessary reduction in protection under pressure; Reduce residual risk created by unavailable controls.',N'disruption; information security; governance; protection; continuity; security requirement; disruption scenario; before; during; after; existing control; maintain; process; compensating control',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(366,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-02',N'Identify disruption security requirements',N'The organisation must determine security requirements that apply before, during and after relevant disruption scenarios. The purpose is to make required protection explicit for each credible disruption.',N'Make required protection explicit for each credible disruption.',N'security requirement; disruption scenario; before; during; after',1,N'Merged into DSR-01 — Merged'),
(367,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-03',N'Define adapted security controls',N'The organisation must determine how normal security controls must be adapted according to the type and conditions of disruption. The purpose is to preserve suitable protection when normal operation is not possible.',N'Preserve suitable protection when normal operation is not possible.',N'adapted control; disruption type; abnormal operation; security',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(368,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-04',N'Integrate security into business continuity',N'The organisation must include information security requirements, roles and actions in business continuity management processes. It must embed controls systems and tools in continuity plans. It must prioritize confidentiality integrity and availability impacts. The purpose is to make security an integral part of continuity decisions and plans. It also aims to ensure continuity arrangements contain the capabilities needed for secure operation. It also aims to protect all three security properties during continuity decisions.',N'Make security an integral part of continuity decisions and plans. Ensure continuity arrangements contain the capabilities needed for secure operation; Protect all three security properties during continuity decisions.',N'business continuity; security requirement; integration; process; security control; supporting system; tool; continuity plan; ICT; BIA; risk assessment; confidentiality; integrity; availability',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(369,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-05',N'Identify critical processes and information',N'The organisation must identify critical business processes, information and associated assets requiring maintained or restored security. The purpose is to focus disruption protection on essential operations and assets.',N'Focus disruption protection on essential operations and assets.',N'critical process; critical information; associated asset; priority',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(370,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-06',N'Develop disruption security plans',N'The organisation must develop documented plans for maintaining or restoring the security of critical information after interruption or failure. The purpose is to provide actionable arrangements for secure continuity and recovery.',N'Provide actionable arrangements for secure continuity and recovery.',N'security plan; interruption; failure; restoration; critical information',1,N'Merged into DSR-09 — Merged'),
(371,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-07',N'Implement disruption security plans',N'The organisation must put planned security controls, responsibilities, resources and procedures into operational readiness. The purpose is to ensure plans can be activated rather than remaining theoretical.',N'Ensure plans can be activated rather than remaining theoretical.',N'plan implementation; readiness; resource; procedure; control',1,N'Merged into DSR-09 — Merged'),
(372,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-08',N'Test disruption security arrangements',N'The organisation must exercise and test plans, controls, systems, tools and compensating measures under realistic scenarios. The purpose is to demonstrate that security can be maintained or restored.',N'Demonstrate that security can be maintained or restored.',N'continuity test; exercise; security control; scenario; evidence',1,N'Merged into DSR-09 — Merged'),
(373,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-09',N'Review and evaluate disruption plans',N'The organisation must review test results, incidents and changes, evaluate effectiveness and update plans. It must develop disruption security plans. It must implement disruption security plans. It must test disruption security arrangements. The purpose is to keep disruption-security arrangements suitable and current. It also aims to provide actionable arrangements for secure continuity and recovery. It also aims to ensure plans can be activated rather than remaining theoretical. It also aims to demonstrate that security can be maintained or restored.',N'Keep disruption-security arrangements suitable and current. Provide actionable arrangements for secure continuity and recovery; Ensure plans can be activated rather than remaining theoretical; Demonstrate that security can be maintained or restored.',N'security plan; interruption; failure; restoration; critical information; plan implementation; readiness; resource; procedure; control; continuity test; exercise; security control; scenario',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(374,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-10',N'Set security restoration levels and times',N'The organisation must define the required security level and time frame for restoring protection after interruption or failure. The purpose is to restore security to an approved level within business needs.',N'Restore security to an approved level within business needs.',N'security restoration; target level; time frame; recovery',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(375,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-11',N'Embed controls systems and tools in continuity plans',N'The organisation must include necessary security controls, supporting systems and tools in business and ICT continuity plans. The purpose is to ensure continuity arrangements contain the capabilities needed for secure operation.',N'Ensure continuity arrangements contain the capabilities needed for secure operation.',N'security control; supporting system; tool; continuity plan; ICT',1,N'Merged into DSR-04 — Merged'),
(376,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-12',N'Maintain existing controls during disruption',N'The organisation must define and operate processes to keep normal security controls functioning wherever possible during disruption. The purpose is to avoid unnecessary reduction in protection under pressure.',N'Avoid unnecessary reduction in protection under pressure.',N'existing control; maintain; disruption; process; protection',1,N'Merged into DSR-01 — Merged'),
(377,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-13',N'Apply compensating controls during disruption',N'The organisation must predefine, authorize and monitor compensating controls where normal controls cannot be maintained. The purpose is to reduce residual risk created by unavailable controls.',N'Reduce residual risk created by unavailable controls.',N'compensating control; unavailable control; authorization; residual risk',1,N'Merged into DSR-01 — Merged'),
(378,30,N'5.29',N'DSR-14',N'Prioritize confidentiality integrity and availability impacts',N'The organisation must use business impact analysis and risk assessment to consider and prioritize confidentiality and integrity loss as well as availability. The purpose is to protect all three security properties during continuity decisions.',N'Protect all three security properties during continuity decisions.',N'BIA; risk assessment; confidentiality; integrity; availability',1,N'Merged into DSR-04 — Merged'),
(379,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-01',N'Govern ICT continuity readiness',N'The organisation must plan, implement, maintain and test ICT readiness based on business continuity objectives and ICT continuity requirements. It must integrate ICT continuity with business continuity. It must develop ICT continuity plans. It must implement ICT continuity solutions. The purpose is to ensure ICT can support organizational objectives during disruption. It also aims to coordinate ICT availability with wider continuity needs. It also aims to provide clear operational instructions for ICT continuity. It also aims to make ICT continuity plans operationally ready.',N'Ensure ICT can support organizational objectives during disruption. Coordinate ICT availability with wider continuity needs; Provide clear operational instructions for ICT continuity; Make ICT continuity plans operationally ready.',N'ICT continuity; readiness; planning; implementation; testing; business continuity; information security; integration; ICT continuity plan; response; recovery; procedure; disruption; continuity solution',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(380,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-02',N'Integrate ICT continuity with business continuity',N'The organisation must align ICT continuity management with business continuity and information security management. The purpose is to coordinate ICT availability with wider continuity needs.',N'Coordinate ICT availability with wider continuity needs.',N'ICT continuity; business continuity; information security; integration',1,N'Merged into ICT-01 — Merged'),
(381,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-03',N'Derive ICT requirements from the BIA',N'The organisation must use approved business impact analysis outputs to define ICT continuity requirements. The purpose is to base ICT recovery decisions on business impact.',N'Base ICT recovery decisions on business impact.',N'BIA; ICT requirement; business impact; continuity',1,N'Merged into ICT-12 — Merged'),
(382,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-04',N'Define impact types and criteria',N'The organisation must define criteria for assessing disruption impacts over time on product- and service-delivery activities. It must assess impact magnitude and duration. The purpose is to measure disruption consequences consistently. It also aims to support evidence-based prioritization and recovery targets.',N'Measure disruption consequences consistently. Support evidence-based prioritization and recovery targets.',N'impact type; impact criteria; disruption; time; activity; impact magnitude; duration; assessment',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(383,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-05',N'Assess impact magnitude and duration',N'The organisation must evaluate the scale and duration of impacts caused by disruption to business activities. The purpose is to support evidence-based prioritization and recovery targets.',N'Support evidence-based prioritization and recovery targets.',N'impact magnitude; duration; disruption; assessment',1,N'Merged into ICT-04 — Merged'),
(384,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-06',N'Identify prioritized business activities',N'The organisation must use BIA results to identify activities requiring prioritized continuity and recovery. The purpose is to focus ICT readiness on essential products and services.',N'Focus ICT readiness on essential products and services.',N'prioritized activity; BIA; product; service; recovery',1,N'Merged into ICT-07 — Merged'),
(385,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-07',N'Set business-activity RTOs',N'The organisation must assign approved recovery time objectives to prioritized business activities. It must identify prioritized business activities. It must set information RPOs. The purpose is to define how quickly essential activities must resume. It also aims to focus ICT readiness on essential products and services. It also aims to limit acceptable data loss during disruption.',N'Define how quickly essential activities must resume. Focus ICT readiness on essential products and services; Limit acceptable data loss during disruption.',N'prioritized activity; BIA; product; service; recovery; RTO; business activity; recovery time; priority; RPO; information; data loss',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(386,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-08',N'Identify supporting resources and ICT services',N'The organisation must determine the people, facilities, information, suppliers and ICT services needed by prioritized activities. It also covers set resource and ict-service RTOs. The purpose is to map critical activities to required recovery resources. It also aims to align supporting recovery with business deadlines.',N'Map critical activities to required recovery resources. Align supporting recovery with business deadlines.',N'resource; ICT service; dependency; prioritized activity; resource RTO; ICT service RTO; recovery',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(387,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-09',N'Set resource and ICT-service RTOs',N'The organisation must assign recovery time objectives to resources and ICT services supporting prioritized activities. The purpose is to align supporting recovery with business deadlines.',N'Align supporting recovery with business deadlines.',N'resource RTO; ICT service RTO; dependency; recovery',1,N'Merged into ICT-08 — Merged'),
(388,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-10',N'Define ICT performance and capacity needs',N'The organisation must specify the performance and capacity required during disruption and recovery. It must respond proactively to ICT disruption risk. The purpose is to ensure recovered ICT can support the required workload. It also aims to reduce disruption impact through early action and cause-independent readiness.',N'Ensure recovered ICT can support the required workload. Reduce disruption impact through early action and cause-independent readiness.',N'performance; capacity; ICT system; disruption; workload; proactive response; disruption warning; detection; any cause',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(389,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-11',N'Set information RPOs',N'The organisation must define recovery point objectives for information supporting prioritized activities. The purpose is to limit acceptable data loss during disruption.',N'Limit acceptable data loss during disruption.',N'RPO; information; data loss; prioritized activity',1,N'Merged into ICT-07 — Merged'),
(390,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-12',N'Assess ICT continuity risks',N'The organisation must perform risk assessment for ICT services and dependencies supporting prioritized activities. It must derive ICT requirements from the BIA. It must select ICT continuity strategies. The purpose is to identify threats and weaknesses that can prevent timely recovery. It also aims to base ICT recovery decisions on business impact. It also aims to provide practical options for prevention, response and recovery.',N'Identify threats and weaknesses that can prevent timely recovery. Base ICT recovery decisions on business impact; Provide practical options for prevention, response and recovery.',N'BIA; ICT requirement; business impact; continuity; ICT risk; dependency; assessment; threat; continuity strategy; solution; before; during; after',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(391,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-13',N'Select ICT continuity strategies',N'The organisation must select suitable strategies and one or more solutions for before, during and after disruption. The purpose is to provide practical options for prevention, response and recovery.',N'Provide practical options for prevention, response and recovery.',N'continuity strategy; solution; before; during; after',1,N'Merged into ICT-12 — Merged'),
(392,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-14',N'Develop ICT continuity plans',N'The organisation must document response and recovery procedures for managing ICT service disruption. The purpose is to provide clear operational instructions for ICT continuity.',N'Provide clear operational instructions for ICT continuity.',N'ICT continuity plan; response; recovery; procedure; disruption',1,N'Merged into ICT-01 — Merged'),
(393,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-15',N'Implement ICT continuity solutions',N'The organisation must deploy and maintain the systems, resources, arrangements and procedures required by selected strategies. The purpose is to make ICT continuity plans operationally ready.',N'Make ICT continuity plans operationally ready.',N'continuity solution; implementation; system; resource; readiness',1,N'Merged into ICT-01 — Merged'),
(394,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-16',N'Establish competent continuity organization',N'The organisation must maintain a structure with personnel having required responsibility, authority and competence to prepare, mitigate and respond. The purpose is to ensure capable and accountable ICT continuity leadership.',N'Ensure capable and accountable ICT continuity leadership.',N'organization; responsibility; authority; competence; personnel',1,N'Merged into ICT-18 — Merged'),
(395,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-17',N'Obtain management approval of plans',N'The organisation must require management approval for ICT continuity plans and significant changes. The purpose is to confirm plans have accountable business authorization.',N'Confirm plans have accountable business authorization.',N'management approval; ICT plan; change; accountability',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(396,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-18',N'Exercise and test ICT continuity',N'The organisation must regularly exercise and test ICT continuity plans, response and recovery procedures against objectives. It must establish competent continuity organization. It must evaluate and improve ICT continuity. The purpose is to demonstrate that recovery works within required levels and times. It also aims to ensure capable and accountable ICT continuity leadership. It also aims to keep ICT readiness effective and current.',N'Demonstrate that recovery works within required levels and times. Ensure capable and accountable ICT continuity leadership; Keep ICT readiness effective and current.',N'organization; responsibility; authority; competence; personnel; exercise; test; recovery; continuity plan; objective; evaluation; test result; improvement; plan update',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(397,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-19',N'Evaluate and improve ICT continuity',N'The organisation must evaluate exercise, test and disruption results and update requirements, strategies, plans and resources. The purpose is to keep ICT readiness effective and current.',N'Keep ICT readiness effective and current.',N'evaluation; test result; improvement; plan update',1,N'Merged into ICT-18 — Merged'),
(398,31,N'5.30',N'ICT-20',N'Respond proactively to ICT disruption risk',N'The organisation must prepare to respond before disruption and when an incident capable of disrupting ICT is detected, regardless of cause. The purpose is to reduce disruption impact through early action and cause-independent readiness.',N'Reduce disruption impact through early action and cause-independent readiness.',N'proactive response; disruption warning; detection; any cause',1,N'Merged into ICT-10 — Merged'),
(399,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-01',N'Govern external information security requirements',N'The organisation must define and maintain a controlled approach for identifying, documenting, applying and updating external information security requirements. The purpose is to ensure legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual duties are managed consistently.',N'Ensure legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual duties are managed consistently.',N'legal; statutory; regulatory; contractual; governance',1,N'Merged into LCR-10 — Merged'),
(400,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-02',N'Maintain a requirements register',N'The organisation must keep a current register of applicable requirements, sources, jurisdictions, owners, obligations and compliance approaches. The purpose is to provide one traceable view of external security duties.',N'Provide one traceable view of external security duties.',N'requirements register; source; jurisdiction; owner; obligation',0,N'Standalone - not merged');

INSERT #prac(seq,sheet_statement_id,statement_reference,practice_ref,practice_name,practice_statement,objective,keywords,is_merged,merge_status) VALUES
(401,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-03',N'Document the compliance approach',N'The organisation must document how each applicable external requirement will be met, evidenced, monitored and reported. The purpose is to translate external duties into practical controls and evidence.',N'Translate external duties into practical controls and evidence.',N'compliance approach; control; evidence; monitoring; reporting',1,N'Merged into LCR-16 — Merged'),
(402,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-04',N'Apply requirements to policies and procedures',N'The organisation must consider external duties when developing or changing information security policies and procedures. The purpose is to keep internal direction aligned with binding obligations.',N'Keep internal direction aligned with binding obligations.',N'policy; procedure; external requirement; compliance',1,N'Merged into LCR-05 — Merged'),
(403,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-05',N'Apply requirements to security controls',N'The organisation must consider external duties when designing, implementing or changing information security controls. It must apply requirements to policies and procedures. It must apply requirements to risk assessment and treatment. The purpose is to ensure controls satisfy relevant external expectations. It also aims to keep internal direction aligned with binding obligations. It also aims to prevent risk decisions from overlooking mandatory duties.',N'Ensure controls satisfy relevant external expectations. Keep internal direction aligned with binding obligations; Prevent risk decisions from overlooking mandatory duties.',N'policy; procedure; external requirement; compliance; security control; design; implementation; change; requirement; risk assessment; risk treatment',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(404,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-06',N'Apply requirements to classification',N'The organisation must consider external duties when classifying information and associated assets for internal use and supplier agreements. The purpose is to align handling and protection with external obligations.',N'Align handling and protection with external obligations.',N'classification; asset; internal need; supplier agreement',1,N'Merged into LCR-09 — Merged'),
(405,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-07',N'Apply requirements to risk assessment and treatment',N'The organisation must consider external duties in security risk assessments and risk-treatment decisions. The purpose is to prevent risk decisions from overlooking mandatory duties.',N'Prevent risk decisions from overlooking mandatory duties.',N'risk assessment; risk treatment; external requirement; compliance',1,N'Merged into LCR-05 — Merged'),
(406,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-08',N'Apply requirements to processes and roles',N'The organisation must consider external duties when defining security processes, roles, responsibilities and authorities. The purpose is to assign clear operational accountability for compliance.',N'Assign clear operational accountability for compliance.',N'process; role; responsibility; authority; compliance',1,N'Merged into LCR-16 — Merged'),
(407,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-09',N'Apply requirements to supplier contracts',N'The organisation must determine supplier security requirements according to applicable duties and the product or service scope. It must apply requirements to classification. It must manage supplier security requirements. The purpose is to flow relevant obligations into supplier arrangements. It also aims to align handling and protection with external obligations. It also aims to ensure supplier arrangements support organizational compliance.',N'Flow relevant obligations into supplier arrangements. Align handling and protection with external obligations; Ensure supplier arrangements support organizational compliance.',N'classification; asset; internal need; supplier agreement; supplier contract; product; service; scope; security requirement; obligation; compliance',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(408,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-10',N'Identify relevant legislation',N'The organisation must identify all legislation relevant to the organization’s information security and business type. It must govern external information security requirements. It must identify relevant regulations. It must monitor legal and regulatory change. The purpose is to maintain awareness of binding legal duties. It also aims to ensure legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual duties are managed consistently. It also aims to maintain awareness of binding regulatory duties. It also aims to keep the compliance baseline current.',N'Maintain awareness of binding legal duties. Ensure legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual duties are managed consistently; Maintain awareness of binding regulatory duties; Keep the compliance baseline current.',N'legal; statutory; regulatory; contractual; governance; legislation; business type; information security; legal duty; regulation; regulator; direction; legal change; regulatory change',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(409,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-11',N'Identify relevant regulations',N'The organisation must identify all regulations and regulatory directions relevant to information security. The purpose is to maintain awareness of binding regulatory duties.',N'Maintain awareness of binding regulatory duties.',N'regulation; regulator; direction; information security',1,N'Merged into LCR-10 — Merged'),
(410,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-12',N'Assess countries of business operation',N'The organisation must identify and apply relevant requirements in every country where the organization conducts business. It must assess foreign products and services. It must assess cross-border information transfers. The purpose is to manage country-specific compliance exposure. It also aims to manage compliance impacts introduced through foreign sourcing. It also aims to ensure cross-border transfers meet applicable duties.',N'Manage country-specific compliance exposure. Manage compliance impacts introduced through foreign sourcing; Ensure cross-border transfers meet applicable duties.',N'country; business operation; jurisdiction; compliance; foreign product; foreign service; country law; sourcing; cross-border transfer; information; law',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(411,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-13',N'Assess foreign products and services',N'The organisation must consider laws and regulations of countries from which products or services are obtained when they affect the organization. The purpose is to manage compliance impacts introduced through foreign sourcing.',N'Manage compliance impacts introduced through foreign sourcing.',N'foreign product; foreign service; country law; sourcing',1,N'Merged into LCR-12 — Merged'),
(412,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-14',N'Assess cross-border information transfers',N'The organisation must identify requirements affecting information transferred across jurisdictional borders. The purpose is to ensure cross-border transfers meet applicable duties.',N'Ensure cross-border transfers meet applicable duties.',N'cross-border transfer; jurisdiction; information; law',1,N'Merged into LCR-12 — Merged'),
(413,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-15',N'Monitor legal and regulatory change',N'The organisation must regularly review identified requirements, track changes and identify new legislation and regulations. The purpose is to keep the compliance baseline current.',N'Keep the compliance baseline current.',N'legal change; regulatory change; monitoring; new law',1,N'Merged into LCR-10 — Merged'),
(414,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-16',N'Assign compliance processes and responsibilities',N'The organisation must define specific processes and named individual responsibilities for meeting each requirement. It must document the compliance approach. It must apply requirements to processes and roles. The purpose is to create accountable execution of compliance duties. It also aims to translate external duties into practical controls and evidence. It also aims to assign clear operational accountability for compliance.',N'Create accountable execution of compliance duties. Translate external duties into practical controls and evidence; Assign clear operational accountability for compliance.',N'compliance approach; control; evidence; monitoring; reporting; process; role; responsibility; authority; compliance; compliance process; individual responsibility; owner; accountability',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(415,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-17',N'Control cryptographic import and export',N'The organisation must identify and comply with restrictions on importing or exporting hardware and software that performs or can support cryptographic functions. The purpose is to prevent prohibited cross-border movement of cryptographic capability.',N'Prevent prohibited cross-border movement of cryptographic capability.',N'cryptography; import; export; hardware; software',1,N'Merged into LCR-21 — Merged'),
(416,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-18',N'Control permitted cryptography use',N'The organisation must identify and comply with legal restrictions on the use, strength, algorithms or applications of cryptography. The purpose is to use cryptography only in legally permitted ways.',N'Use cryptography only in legally permitted ways.',N'cryptography use; restriction; algorithm; legal requirement',1,N'Merged into LCR-21 — Merged'),
(417,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-19',N'Manage authority access to encrypted information',N'The organisation must identify mandatory or discretionary lawful-access requirements applying to encrypted information. The purpose is to address lawful-access duties without uncontrolled disclosure.',N'Address lawful-access duties without uncontrolled disclosure.',N'authority access; encrypted information; lawful access; disclosure',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(418,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-20',N'Validate digital signatures seals and certificates',N'The organisation must identify and meet legal requirements affecting the validity of digital signatures, electronic seals and certificates. The purpose is to ensure electronic trust mechanisms have intended legal effect.',N'Ensure electronic trust mechanisms have intended legal effect.',N'digital signature; electronic seal; certificate; validity',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(419,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-21',N'Obtain legal advice for cryptography',N'The organisation must seek appropriate legal advice, especially when encrypted information or cryptographic tools cross jurisdictions. It must control cryptographic import and export. It must control permitted cryptography use. The purpose is to reduce legal risk in complex cryptographic situations. It also aims to prevent prohibited cross-border movement of cryptographic capability. It also aims to use cryptography only in legally permitted ways.',N'Reduce legal risk in complex cryptographic situations. Prevent prohibited cross-border movement of cryptographic capability; Use cryptography only in legally permitted ways.',N'cryptography; import; export; hardware; software; cryptography use; restriction; algorithm; legal requirement; legal advice; encrypted information; cryptographic tool; border',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(420,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-22',N'Manage client security requirements',N'The organisation must identify, document and meet information security duties in client contracts. It must manage insurance security requirements. The purpose is to fulfil agreed security commitments to clients. It also aims to preserve insurance compliance and coverage expectations.',N'Fulfil agreed security commitments to clients. Preserve insurance compliance and coverage expectations.',N'client contract; security requirement; obligation; compliance; insurance contract; security condition; coverage',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(421,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-23',N'Manage supplier security requirements',N'The organisation must identify, document and meet information security duties in supplier contracts. The purpose is to ensure supplier arrangements support organizational compliance.',N'Ensure supplier arrangements support organizational compliance.',N'supplier contract; security requirement; obligation; compliance',1,N'Merged into LCR-09 — Merged'),
(422,32,N'5.31',N'LCR-24',N'Manage insurance security requirements',N'The organisation must identify, document and meet information security duties and conditions in insurance contracts. The purpose is to preserve insurance compliance and coverage expectations.',N'Preserve insurance compliance and coverage expectations.',N'insurance contract; security condition; obligation; coverage',1,N'Merged into LCR-22 — Merged'),
(423,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-01',N'Govern intellectual property protection',N'The organisation must define and implement procedures for protecting intellectual property rights and proprietary products. It must establish an intellectual property policy. It must protect all forms of intellectual property. It must protect organizational intellectual property. The purpose is to meet applicable intellectual-property and licence obligations consistently. It also aims to provide clear organizational direction for intellectual-property compliance. It also aims to cover the full range of relevant intellectual-property rights. It also aims to prevent loss, misuse or unauthorized disclosure of organizational intellectual property.',N'Meet applicable intellectual-property and licence obligations consistently. Provide clear organizational direction for intellectual-property compliance; Cover the full range of relevant intellectual-property rights; Prevent loss, misuse or unauthorized disclosure of organizational intellectual property.',N'intellectual property; procedure; proprietary product; governance; IP policy; communication; copyright; licence; ownership; design right; trademark; patent; source code; organizational IP',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(424,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-02',N'Establish an intellectual property policy',N'The organisation must define, approve and communicate a topic-specific policy for protecting intellectual property rights. The purpose is to provide clear organizational direction for intellectual-property compliance.',N'Provide clear organizational direction for intellectual-property compliance.',N'IP policy; communication; copyright; licence; ownership',1,N'Merged into IPR-01 — Merged'),
(425,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-03',N'Publish compliant-use procedures',N'The organisation must publish procedures defining permitted use of software, data and information products. It must maintain an intellectual-property asset register. The purpose is to help personnel use protected material lawfully and consistently. It also aims to maintain visibility of protected software, data, documents and other assets.',N'Help personnel use protected material lawfully and consistently. Maintain visibility of protected software, data, documents and other assets.',N'compliant use; software; data; information product; procedure; asset register; IP requirement; document',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(426,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-04',N'Acquire software from reputable sources',N'The organisation must obtain software only through known, reputable and authorized sources. It must review installed software and products. It must control software disposal and transfer. It must comply with public and external-source terms. The purpose is to reduce copyright infringement and untrusted-software risk. It also aims to detect and remove unauthorized or unlicensed products. It also aims to prevent unauthorized retention, use or transfer of licensed software. It also aims to respect usage conditions attached to externally obtained material.',N'Reduce copyright infringement and untrusted-software risk. Detect and remove unauthorized or unlicensed products; Prevent unauthorized retention, use or transfer of licensed software; Respect usage conditions attached to externally obtained material.',N'software acquisition; reputable source; authorized source; copyright; software review; authorized; licensed product; installation; software disposal; transfer; reassignment; licence; public network; external source',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(427,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-05',N'Maintain an intellectual-property asset register',N'The organisation must identify and record assets that carry intellectual-property protection requirements. The purpose is to maintain visibility of protected software, data, documents and other assets.',N'Maintain visibility of protected software, data, documents and other assets.',N'asset register; IP requirement; software; data; document',1,N'Merged into IPR-03 — Merged'),
(428,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-06',N'Retain ownership and licence evidence',N'The organisation must maintain proof of ownership, licences, manuals, purchase records and related entitlements. The purpose is to demonstrate lawful ownership and usage rights.',N'Demonstrate lawful ownership and usage rights.',N'licence evidence; ownership; manual; entitlement; purchase record',1,N'Merged into IPR-09 — Merged'),
(429,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-07',N'Control licence user and resource limits',N'The organisation must monitor and enforce maximum permitted users, devices, processors and other licensed resources. The purpose is to prevent use beyond contractual licence limits.',N'Prevent use beyond contractual licence limits.',N'licence limit; user; device; CPU; resource',1,N'Merged into IPR-09 — Merged'),
(430,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-08',N'Review installed software and products',N'The organisation must regularly confirm that only authorized software and properly licensed products are installed. The purpose is to detect and remove unauthorized or unlicensed products.',N'Detect and remove unauthorized or unlicensed products.',N'software review; authorized; licensed product; installation',1,N'Merged into IPR-04 — Merged'),
(431,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-09',N'Maintain licence conditions',N'The organisation must define and operate procedures for meeting use, copying, backup, location, assignment and renewal conditions. It must retain ownership and licence evidence. It must control licence user and resource limits. It must control machine and backup-copy restrictions. The purpose is to keep ongoing product use within licence terms. It also aims to demonstrate lawful ownership and usage rights. It also aims to prevent use beyond contractual licence limits. It also aims to prevent deployment or copying beyond explicit entitlements.',N'Keep ongoing product use within licence terms. Demonstrate lawful ownership and usage rights; Prevent use beyond contractual licence limits; Prevent deployment or copying beyond explicit entitlements.',N'licence evidence; ownership; manual; entitlement; purchase record; licence limit; user; device; CPU; resource; licence condition; use; copy; backup',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(432,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-10',N'Control software disposal and transfer',N'The organisation must define approved procedures for disposing of software or transferring it to another party or device. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized retention, use or transfer of licensed software.',N'Prevent unauthorized retention, use or transfer of licensed software.',N'software disposal; transfer; reassignment; licence',1,N'Merged into IPR-04 — Merged'),
(433,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-11',N'Comply with public and external-source terms',N'The organisation must identify and follow terms for software, information and data obtained from public networks or external sources. The purpose is to respect usage conditions attached to externally obtained material.',N'Respect usage conditions attached to externally obtained material.',N'public network; external source; terms; software; information',1,N'Merged into IPR-04 — Merged'),
(434,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-12',N'Control commercial recording use',N'The organisation must prevent unauthorized duplication, conversion or extraction from commercial audio, video and other recordings. The purpose is to comply with copyright and licence restrictions for recordings.',N'Comply with copyright and licence restrictions for recordings.',N'commercial recording; audio; video; duplication; extraction',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(435,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-13',N'Control copying of documents and standards',N'The organisation must prevent unauthorized full or partial copying of standards, books, articles, reports and other protected documents. The purpose is to respect copyright and licence conditions for published material.',N'Respect copyright and licence conditions for published material.',N'standard; book; article; report; copying; copyright',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(436,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-14',N'Protect all forms of intellectual property',N'The organisation must apply suitable protection to copyrights, design rights, trademarks, patents and source-code licences. The purpose is to cover the full range of relevant intellectual-property rights.',N'Cover the full range of relevant intellectual-property rights.',N'copyright; design right; trademark; patent; source code',1,N'Merged into IPR-01 — Merged'),
(437,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-15',N'Control machine and backup-copy restrictions',N'The organisation must enforce licence limits on approved machines and permitted backup copies. The purpose is to prevent deployment or copying beyond explicit entitlements.',N'Prevent deployment or copying beyond explicit entitlements.',N'specified machine; backup copy; licence restriction; deployment',1,N'Merged into IPR-09 — Merged'),
(438,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-16',N'Govern externally acquired data',N'The organisation must require a data-sharing agreement or equivalent legal instrument for externally acquired data where appropriate. It must define permitted processing of acquired data. It must record external data provenance. The purpose is to establish lawful and clear rights for external data use. It also aims to prevent data use beyond granted rights. It also aims to support traceability and lawful reuse of data.',N'Establish lawful and clear rights for external data use. Prevent data use beyond granted rights; Support traceability and lawful reuse of data.',N'external data; data-sharing agreement; legal instrument; right; permitted processing; acquired data; use; sharing; retention; data provenance; origin; provider; acquisition; rights',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(439,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-17',N'Define permitted processing of acquired data',N'The organisation must document what processing, use, sharing, modification and retention are permitted for externally acquired data. The purpose is to prevent data use beyond granted rights.',N'Prevent data use beyond granted rights.',N'permitted processing; acquired data; use; sharing; retention',1,N'Merged into IPR-16 — Merged'),
(440,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-18',N'Record external data provenance',N'The organisation must record the origin, provider, acquisition basis and relevant rights for externally acquired data. The purpose is to support traceability and lawful reuse of data.',N'Support traceability and lawful reuse of data.',N'data provenance; origin; provider; acquisition; rights',1,N'Merged into IPR-16 — Merged'),
(441,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-19',N'Use only owned licensed or authorized material',N'The organisation must restrict organizational use to material it developed, licensed or was authorized to use by the rights holder. The purpose is to prevent infringement of third-party intellectual-property rights.',N'Prevent infringement of third-party intellectual-property rights.',N'owned material; licensed material; authorization; infringement',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(442,33,N'5.32',N'IPR-20',N'Protect organizational intellectual property',N'The organisation must manage risks of personnel and third parties failing to protect the organization’s own intellectual-property rights. The purpose is to prevent loss, misuse or unauthorized disclosure of organizational intellectual property.',N'Prevent loss, misuse or unauthorized disclosure of organizational intellectual property.',N'organizational IP; personnel; third party; misuse; disclosure',1,N'Merged into IPR-01 — Merged'),
(443,34,N'5.33',N'REC-01',N'Govern records protection',N'The organisation must define and implement controls and procedures for protecting records throughout their life cycle. It must align with records-management policy. It must apply information classification to records. The purpose is to protect records consistently as business and management needs change. It also aims to maintain coherent and compliant record controls. It also aims to match record controls to sensitivity and importance.',N'Protect records consistently as business and management needs change. Maintain coherent and compliant record controls; Match record controls to sensitivity and importance.',N'records; lifecycle; governance; protection; procedure; records policy; alignment; requirement; guideline; classification; record protection; sensitivity; handling',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(444,34,N'5.33',N'REC-02',N'Prevent record loss and destruction',N'The organisation must protect records against accidental or unauthorized loss and destruction. The purpose is to preserve required records and business evidence.',N'Preserve required records and business evidence.',N'record loss; destruction; backup; protection; evidence',1,N'Merged into REC-11 — Merged'),
(445,34,N'5.33',N'REC-03',N'Prevent record falsification and manipulation',N'The organisation must protect records from unauthorized alteration, fabrication and manipulation. The purpose is to maintain trustworthy records of activities and transactions.',N'Maintain trustworthy records of activities and transactions.',N'falsification; manipulation; alteration; record integrity',1,N'Merged into REC-11 — Merged'),
(446,34,N'5.33',N'REC-04',N'Prevent unauthorized record access and release',N'The organisation must restrict record access and disclosure to authorized purposes and recipients. The purpose is to protect record confidentiality and controlled availability.',N'Protect record confidentiality and controlled availability.',N'unauthorized access; release; disclosure; record; confidentiality',1,N'Merged into REC-11 — Merged'),
(447,34,N'5.33',N'REC-05',N'Preserve record authenticity',N'The organisation must maintain evidence that records are what they claim to be and originate from the stated source. The purpose is to keep records credible as evidence of business activity.',N'Keep records credible as evidence of business activity.',N'record authenticity; origin; evidence; source',1,N'Merged into REC-06 — Merged'),
(448,34,N'5.33',N'REC-06',N'Preserve record reliability',N'The organisation must ensure records accurately and consistently represent the events, transactions or activities documented. It must preserve record authenticity. It must preserve record usability. It must maintain record chain of custody. The purpose is to support dependable business and compliance decisions. It also aims to keep records credible as evidence of business activity. It also aims to ensure retained records remain practically useful. It also aims to preserve accountability and evidential value across hand-offs.',N'Support dependable business and compliance decisions. Keep records credible as evidence of business activity; Ensure retained records remain practically useful; Preserve accountability and evidential value across hand-offs.',N'record authenticity; origin; evidence; source; record reliability; transaction; activity; accuracy; record usability; accessibility; understanding; purpose; chain of custody; possession',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(449,34,N'5.33',N'REC-07',N'Preserve record integrity',N'The organisation must protect completeness and correctness of records and associated metadata over time. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized or undetected change.',N'Prevent unauthorized or undetected change.',N'record integrity; completeness; metadata; change',1,N'Merged into REC-22 — Merged'),
(450,34,N'5.33',N'REC-08',N'Preserve record usability',N'The organisation must keep records accessible, understandable and usable for their required business or compliance purpose. The purpose is to ensure retained records remain practically useful.',N'Ensure retained records remain practically useful.',N'record usability; accessibility; understanding; purpose',1,N'Merged into REC-06 — Merged'),
(451,34,N'5.33',N'REC-09',N'Issue storage and handling guidelines',N'The organisation must define guidelines for storing, handling, transferring and accessing physical and electronic records. The purpose is to apply consistent protection during normal record handling.',N'Apply consistent protection during normal record handling.',N'storage; handling; transfer; access; guideline',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(452,34,N'5.33',N'REC-10',N'Maintain record chain of custody',N'The organisation must document possession, transfer and handling where record custody must be demonstrated. The purpose is to preserve accountability and evidential value across hand-offs.',N'Preserve accountability and evidential value across hand-offs.',N'chain of custody; possession; transfer; handling; record',1,N'Merged into REC-06 — Merged'),
(453,34,N'5.33',N'REC-11',N'Control record disposal',N'The organisation must define and apply authorized disposal methods that prevent unauthorized recovery or release. It must prevent record loss and destruction. It must prevent record falsification and manipulation. It must prevent unauthorized record access and release. The purpose is to dispose of records securely when no longer required. It also aims to preserve required records and business evidence. It also aims to maintain trustworthy records of activities and transactions. It also aims to protect record confidentiality and controlled availability.',N'Dispose of records securely when no longer required. Preserve required records and business evidence; Maintain trustworthy records of activities and transactions; Protect record confidentiality and controlled availability.',N'record loss; destruction; backup; protection; evidence; falsification; manipulation; alteration; record integrity; unauthorized access; release; disclosure; record; confidentiality',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(454,34,N'5.33',N'REC-12',N'Align with records-management policy',N'The organisation must keep storage, handling, custody and disposal guidelines aligned with the records-management policy and other requirements. The purpose is to maintain coherent and compliant record controls.',N'Maintain coherent and compliant record controls.',N'records policy; alignment; requirement; guideline',1,N'Merged into REC-01 — Merged'),
(455,34,N'5.33',N'REC-13',N'Maintain a retention schedule',N'The organisation must define record categories and approved retention periods in a current retention schedule. The purpose is to retain each record for the required period.',N'Retain each record for the required period.',N'retention schedule; record category; period; approval',1,N'Merged into REC-14 — Merged'),
(456,34,N'5.33',N'REC-14',N'Identify records and retention periods',N'The organisation must ensure storage systems identify each record and its applicable retention period. It must maintain a retention schedule. It must apply legal regulatory and societal retention needs. The purpose is to make retention status visible and enforceable. It also aims to retain each record for the required period. It also aims to meet external expectations for record availability and protection.',N'Make retention status visible and enforceable. Retain each record for the required period; Meet external expectations for record availability and protection.',N'retention schedule; record category; period; approval; record identification; retention period; storage system; law; regulation; societal expectation; retention',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(457,34,N'5.33',N'REC-15',N'Apply legal regulatory and societal retention needs',N'The organisation must consider national or regional law, regulation and relevant community or societal expectations when setting retention and protection. The purpose is to meet external expectations for record availability and protection.',N'Meet external expectations for record availability and protection.',N'law; regulation; societal expectation; retention',1,N'Merged into REC-14 — Merged'),
(458,34,N'5.33',N'REC-16',N'Apply information classification to records',N'The organisation must use the organization’s classification scheme when deciding how specific records are protected. The purpose is to match record controls to sensitivity and importance.',N'Match record controls to sensitivity and importance.',N'classification; record protection; sensitivity; handling',1,N'Merged into REC-01 — Merged'),
(459,34,N'5.33',N'REC-17',N'Categorize record types and storage media',N'The organisation must define record types, retention periods and permitted physical or electronic storage media. It must protect storage media from deterioration. The purpose is to apply appropriate storage to different record classes. It also aims to prevent physical or technical degradation of retained records.',N'Apply appropriate storage to different record classes. Prevent physical or technical degradation of retained records.',N'record type; storage media; physical; electronic; retention; media deterioration; manufacturer; storage; monitoring',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(460,34,N'5.33',N'REC-18',N'Ensure timely record retrieval',N'The organisation must choose and operate storage systems that retrieve required records within an acceptable time and format. The purpose is to provide records when needed for business or compliance.',N'Provide records when needed for business or compliance.',N'record retrieval; time frame; format; storage system',1,N'Merged into REC-22 — Merged'),
(461,34,N'5.33',N'REC-19',N'Maintain long-term media and format readability',N'The organisation must ensure electronic records, media and formats remain accessible and readable throughout retention despite technology change. The purpose is to prevent loss of access caused by obsolescence.',N'Prevent loss of access caused by obsolescence.',N'format readability; media; technology change; migration',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(462,34,N'5.33',N'REC-20',N'Retain cryptographic keys and supporting programs',N'The organisation must retain keys, certificates, programs and dependencies needed to decrypt or validate records for their retention period. The purpose is to keep encrypted or digitally signed records accessible and verifiable.',N'Keep encrypted or digitally signed records accessible and verifiable.',N'cryptographic key; program; encrypted archive; digital signature',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(463,34,N'5.33',N'REC-21',N'Protect storage media from deterioration',N'The organisation must follow manufacturer handling recommendations and monitor media deterioration. The purpose is to prevent physical or technical degradation of retained records.',N'Prevent physical or technical degradation of retained records.',N'media deterioration; manufacturer; storage; monitoring',1,N'Merged into REC-17 — Merged'),
(464,34,N'5.33',N'REC-22',N'Maintain essential record metadata',N'The organisation must capture and preserve metadata describing record context, content, structure and management over time. It must preserve record integrity. It must ensure timely record retrieval. The purpose is to keep records understandable, traceable and manageable. It also aims to prevent unauthorized or undetected change. It also aims to provide records when needed for business or compliance.',N'Keep records understandable, traceable and manageable. Prevent unauthorized or undetected change; Provide records when needed for business or compliance.',N'record integrity; completeness; metadata; change; record retrieval; time frame; format; storage system; record metadata; context; content; structure; management',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(465,35,N'5.34',N'PII-01',N'Govern privacy and PII protection',N'The organisation must establish governance for preserving privacy and protecting PII across the organization and its services. The purpose is to provide clear direction and oversight for privacy protection.',N'Provide clear direction and oversight for privacy protection.',N'privacy governance; PII protection; oversight; accountability',1,N'Merged into PII-03 — Merged'),
(466,35,N'5.34',N'PII-02',N'Identify applicable privacy requirements',N'The organisation must identify and maintain applicable privacy laws, regulations and contractual requirements for every PII processing activity. It must maintain privacy procedures. It must appoint privacy leadership. It must provide privacy information. The purpose is to know the privacy duties that each activity must meet. It also aims to turn privacy requirements into repeatable work. It also aims to provide accountable leadership and guidance for privacy. It also aims to support fair and transparent processing.',N'Know the privacy duties that each activity must meet. Turn privacy requirements into repeatable work; Provide accountable leadership and guidance for privacy; Support fair and transparent processing.',N'privacy law; regulation; contract; requirement; jurisdiction; privacy procedure; PII handling; implementation; lifecycle; privacy officer; authority; independence; management; guidance',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(467,35,N'5.34',N'PII-03',N'Maintain a privacy and PII policy',N'The organisation must establish, approve, communicate and review a topic-specific policy for privacy and protection of PII. It must govern privacy and PII protection. It must communicate privacy requirements. The purpose is to set consistent rules for handling PII. It also aims to provide clear direction and oversight for privacy protection. It also aims to ensure everyone handling PII understands the rules.',N'Set consistent rules for handling PII. Provide clear direction and oversight for privacy protection; Ensure everyone handling PII understands the rules.',N'privacy governance; PII protection; oversight; accountability; privacy policy; PII policy; approval; communication; review; interested party; personnel; service provider; responsibility',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(468,35,N'5.34',N'PII-04',N'Maintain privacy procedures',N'The organisation must develop and implement procedures for preserving privacy and protecting PII throughout processing. The purpose is to turn privacy requirements into repeatable work.',N'Turn privacy requirements into repeatable work.',N'privacy procedure; PII handling; implementation; lifecycle',1,N'Merged into PII-02 — Merged'),
(469,35,N'5.34',N'PII-05',N'Communicate privacy requirements',N'The organisation must communicate the privacy policy, procedures and individual responsibilities to relevant personnel, service providers and interested parties. The purpose is to ensure everyone handling PII understands the rules.',N'Ensure everyone handling PII understands the rules.',N'communication; interested party; personnel; service provider; responsibility',1,N'Merged into PII-03 — Merged'),
(470,35,N'5.34',N'PII-06',N'Appoint privacy leadership',N'The organisation must appoint a responsible privacy leader, such as a privacy officer, with defined authority, independence and access to management. The purpose is to provide accountable leadership and guidance for privacy.',N'Provide accountable leadership and guidance for privacy.',N'privacy officer; authority; independence; management; guidance',1,N'Merged into PII-02 — Merged'),
(471,35,N'5.34',N'PII-07',N'Assign PII responsibilities',N'The organisation must define and assign responsibilities for collecting, processing, storing, sharing, transferring and deleting PII. The purpose is to make accountability clear at every processing stage.',N'Make accountability clear at every processing stage.',N'PII owner; role; responsibility; processor; accountability',1,N'Merged into PII-24 — Merged'),
(472,35,N'5.34',N'PII-08',N'Maintain a PII inventory',N'The organisation must identify PII, its owners, locations, systems, formats, sensitivity and responsible processing parties. It must classify and label PII. It must maintain PII accuracy. It must control PII retention and deletion. The purpose is to maintain visibility of PII that requires protection. It also aims to match protection to the sensitivity of PII. It also aims to prevent harm and poor decisions caused by inaccurate PII. It also aims to avoid keeping PII longer than necessary.',N'Maintain visibility of PII that requires protection. Match protection to the sensitivity of PII; Prevent harm and poor decisions caused by inaccurate PII; Avoid keeping PII longer than necessary.',N'PII inventory; data owner; system; location; sensitivity; PII classification; label; handling; metadata; PII accuracy; correction; completeness; currency; dispute',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(473,35,N'5.34',N'PII-09',N'Map PII processing activities',N'The organisation must document PII sources, purposes, processing steps, recipients, storage locations, transfers and disposal points. It must establish processing authority. The purpose is to understand how PII moves and is used. It also aims to prevent processing without a valid and recorded basis.',N'Understand how PII moves and is used. Prevent processing without a valid and recorded basis.',N'processing record; data flow; purpose; recipient; lifecycle; processing authority; legal basis; contract; approval',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(474,35,N'5.34',N'PII-10',N'Classify and label PII',N'The organisation must classify PII by sensitivity and apply handling labels or metadata where appropriate. The purpose is to match protection to the sensitivity of PII.',N'Match protection to the sensitivity of PII.',N'PII classification; label; sensitivity; handling; metadata',1,N'Merged into PII-08 — Merged'),
(475,35,N'5.34',N'PII-11',N'Establish processing authority',N'The organisation must document the applicable legal, regulatory or contractual authority for each PII processing purpose. The purpose is to prevent processing without a valid and recorded basis.',N'Prevent processing without a valid and recorded basis.',N'processing authority; legal basis; contract; purpose; approval',1,N'Merged into PII-09 — Merged'),
(476,35,N'5.34',N'PII-12',N'Provide privacy information',N'The organisation must give relevant people clear and timely information about PII collection, use, sharing, retention and rights where required. The purpose is to support fair and transparent processing.',N'Support fair and transparent processing.',N'privacy notice; transparency; collection; use; rights',1,N'Merged into PII-02 — Merged'),
(477,35,N'5.34',N'PII-13',N'Manage consent where required',N'The organisation must obtain, record, update and withdraw consent where consent is required for PII processing. The purpose is to keep consent valid, demonstrable and easy to manage.',N'Keep consent valid, demonstrable and easy to manage.',N'consent; withdrawal; record; preference; processing',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(478,35,N'5.34',N'PII-14',N'Minimize PII collection and use',N'The organisation must collect, access, use and disclose only the PII needed for an approved purpose. It must restrict access to PII. The purpose is to reduce privacy risk by limiting unnecessary PII. It also aims to prevent unauthorized access to PII.',N'Reduce privacy risk by limiting unnecessary PII. Prevent unauthorized access to PII.',N'data minimization; collection; access; disclosure; necessity; PII access; least privilege; authorization; review; removal',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(479,35,N'5.34',N'PII-15',N'Limit PII to approved purposes',N'The organisation must use PII only for documented and compatible purposes unless a new authority and approval are obtained. It must respond to PII incidents and breaches. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized or unexpected use of PII. It also aims to limit harm and meet breach response duties.',N'Prevent unauthorized or unexpected use of PII. Limit harm and meet breach response duties.',N'purpose limitation; secondary use; approval; compatibility; PII breach; incident; notification; containment; investigation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(480,35,N'5.34',N'PII-16',N'Maintain PII accuracy',N'The organisation must keep PII accurate, complete and current where accuracy matters, and correct or flag disputed data promptly. The purpose is to prevent harm and poor decisions caused by inaccurate PII.',N'Prevent harm and poor decisions caused by inaccurate PII.',N'PII accuracy; correction; completeness; currency; dispute',1,N'Merged into PII-08 — Merged'),
(481,35,N'5.34',N'PII-17',N'Control PII retention and deletion',N'The organisation must define retention periods and securely delete, anonymize or return PII when it is no longer required. The purpose is to avoid keeping PII longer than necessary.',N'Avoid keeping PII longer than necessary.',N'PII retention; deletion; anonymization; return; schedule',1,N'Merged into PII-08 — Merged'),
(482,35,N'5.34',N'PII-18',N'Handle individual privacy requests',N'The organisation must receive, verify, track and respond to applicable requests concerning access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection or portability. The purpose is to meet applicable individual rights within required time limits.',N'Meet applicable individual rights within required time limits.',N'privacy request; access; correction; deletion; portability',1,N'Merged into PII-20 — Merged'),
(483,35,N'5.34',N'PII-19',N'Perform privacy impact assessments',N'The organisation must assess privacy risks before high-risk or materially changed PII processing and document treatment and approval. It must maintain privacy evidence and records. The purpose is to identify and reduce privacy risk before harm occurs. It also aims to demonstrate that privacy duties are understood and met.',N'Identify and reduce privacy risk before harm occurs. Demonstrate that privacy duties are understood and met.',N'privacy impact assessment; PIA; risk; mitigation; approval; privacy evidence; record; accountability; audit trail; retention',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(484,35,N'5.34',N'PII-20',N'Apply privacy by design and default',N'The organisation must embed privacy requirements and protective defaults into projects, systems, products, services and changes. It must handle individual privacy requests. It must monitor privacy compliance. It must manage privacy exceptions and changes. The purpose is to build privacy protection into solutions from the start. It also aims to meet applicable individual rights within required time limits. It also aims to detect and correct privacy control failures. It also aims to keep deviations and change-related privacy risks controlled.',N'Build privacy protection into solutions from the start. Meet applicable individual rights within required time limits; Detect and correct privacy control failures; Keep deviations and change-related privacy risks controlled.',N'privacy request; access; correction; deletion; portability; privacy by design; privacy by default; project; system; change; privacy monitoring; compliance; testing; metric',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(485,35,N'5.34',N'PII-21',N'Restrict access to PII',N'The organisation must grant PII access only to authorized roles with a valid need, and review and remove access promptly. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized access to PII.',N'Prevent unauthorized access to PII.',N'PII access; least privilege; authorization; review; removal',1,N'Merged into PII-14 — Merged'),
(486,35,N'5.34',N'PII-22',N'Protect PII with cryptography and masking',N'The organisation must use suitable encryption, pseudonymization, masking or tokenization based on privacy risk and requirements. The purpose is to reduce exposure of PII in storage, use and transmission.',N'Reduce exposure of PII in storage, use and transmission.',N'encryption; pseudonymization; masking; tokenization; PII',1,N'Merged into PII-24 — Merged'),
(487,35,N'5.34',N'PII-23',N'Secure PII transfers',N'The organisation must authorize and protect PII transfers, verify recipients and retain transfer evidence. It must control cross-border PII transfers. The purpose is to prevent loss, interception or unauthorized disclosure during transfer. It also aims to meet national restrictions on international PII transfer.',N'Prevent loss, interception or unauthorized disclosure during transfer. Meet national restrictions on international PII transfer.',N'PII transfer; recipient; authorization; transmission; evidence; cross-border transfer; country; safeguard; approval; restriction',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(488,35,N'5.34',N'PII-24',N'Control PII processors and providers',N'The organisation must assess, contract, instruct and monitor service providers and other parties that process PII. It must assign PII responsibilities. It must protect PII with cryptography and masking. The purpose is to ensure external processing meets privacy requirements. It also aims to make accountability clear at every processing stage. It also aims to reduce exposure of PII in storage, use and transmission.',N'Ensure external processing meets privacy requirements. Make accountability clear at every processing stage; Reduce exposure of PII in storage, use and transmission.',N'PII owner; role; responsibility; processor; accountability; encryption; pseudonymization; masking; tokenization; PII; PII processor; service provider; contract; due diligence',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(489,35,N'5.34',N'PII-25',N'Control cross-border PII transfers',N'The organisation must identify transfer locations and apply required approvals, safeguards and restrictions before PII moves across borders. The purpose is to meet national restrictions on international PII transfer.',N'Meet national restrictions on international PII transfer.',N'cross-border transfer; country; safeguard; approval; restriction',1,N'Merged into PII-23 — Merged'),
(490,35,N'5.34',N'PII-26',N'Respond to PII incidents and breaches',N'The organisation must detect, assess, contain, investigate, record and notify PII incidents within applicable time limits. The purpose is to limit harm and meet breach response duties.',N'Limit harm and meet breach response duties.',N'PII breach; incident; notification; containment; investigation',1,N'Merged into PII-15 — Merged'),
(491,35,N'5.34',N'PII-27',N'Train people who handle PII',N'The organisation must provide role-based privacy training and guidance before access and at planned intervals. The purpose is to ensure PII is handled by informed and capable people.',N'Ensure PII is handled by informed and capable people.',N'privacy training; awareness; role-based; guidance; competence',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(492,35,N'5.34',N'PII-28',N'Monitor privacy compliance',N'The organisation must monitor, test and report compliance with privacy policy, procedures, legal duties and protective controls. The purpose is to detect and correct privacy control failures.',N'Detect and correct privacy control failures.',N'privacy monitoring; compliance; testing; metric; reporting',1,N'Merged into PII-20 — Merged'),
(493,35,N'5.34',N'PII-29',N'Manage privacy exceptions and changes',N'The organisation must approve, time-limit, monitor and close privacy exceptions, and reassess controls after legal, business or technology changes. The purpose is to keep deviations and change-related privacy risks controlled.',N'Keep deviations and change-related privacy risks controlled.',N'privacy exception; change; approval; expiry; reassessment',1,N'Merged into PII-20 — Merged'),
(494,35,N'5.34',N'PII-30',N'Maintain privacy evidence and records',N'The organisation must retain current evidence of privacy decisions, processing, notices, requests, assessments, incidents, transfers and reviews. The purpose is to demonstrate that privacy duties are understood and met.',N'Demonstrate that privacy duties are understood and met.',N'privacy evidence; record; accountability; audit trail; retention',1,N'Merged into PII-19 — Merged'),
(495,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-01',N'Govern independent information security reviews',N'The organisation must define accountability, authority and oversight for independent reviews. The purpose is to ensure reviews are planned, objective and acted upon.',N'Ensure reviews are planned, objective and acted upon.',N'independent review; governance; accountability; oversight',1,N'Merged into IRV-19 — Merged'),
(496,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-02',N'Maintain an independent review process',N'The organisation must document the method for planning, performing, reporting and following up independent reviews. The purpose is to make reviews consistent and repeatable.',N'Make reviews consistent and repeatable.',N'review process; method; planning; reporting; follow-up',1,N'Merged into IRV-19 — Merged'),
(497,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-03',N'Define the review scope',N'The organisation must cover the information security management approach and its implementation across people, processes and technology. It must review people arrangements. It must review security processes. It must review security technologies. The purpose is to ensure no important part of security management is omitted. It also aims to confirm people-related controls support effective security. It also aims to confirm processes work as intended. It also aims to confirm technology supports required protection.',N'Ensure no important part of security management is omitted. Confirm people-related controls support effective security; Confirm processes work as intended; Confirm technology supports required protection.',N'review scope; people; process; technology; implementation; role; competence; accountability; personnel; security process; operation; consistency; security technology; maintenance',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(498,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-04',N'Schedule reviews at planned intervals',N'The organisation must set a risk-based schedule for periodic independent reviews. The purpose is to review security management regularly.',N'Review security management regularly.',N'review schedule; planned interval; periodic; risk',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(499,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-05',N'Require management to initiate reviews',N'The organisation must assign management responsibility for planning and starting independent reviews. It must initiate corrective actions. The purpose is to provide visible sponsorship and timely initiation. It also aims to resolve weaknesses and restore required performance.',N'Provide visible sponsorship and timely initiation. Resolve weaknesses and restore required performance.',N'management; initiate; sponsor; review plan; corrective action; inadequacy; remediation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(500,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-06',N'Review the security management approach',N'The organisation must assess the design and direction of the organization’s approach to information security. It must identify improvement opportunities. The purpose is to confirm the overall approach remains appropriate. It also aims to drive continual improvement from independent insight.',N'Confirm the overall approach remains appropriate. Drive continual improvement from independent insight.',N'security approach; direction; design; assessment; improvement; opportunity; recommendation; review',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(501,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-07',N'Review people arrangements',N'The organisation must assess security roles, competence, accountability and personnel arrangements. The purpose is to confirm people-related controls support effective security.',N'Confirm people-related controls support effective security.',N'people; role; competence; accountability; personnel',1,N'Merged into IRV-03 — Merged'),
(502,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-08',N'Review security processes',N'The organisation must assess whether security processes are defined, implemented and consistently operated. The purpose is to confirm processes work as intended.',N'Confirm processes work as intended.',N'security process; implementation; operation; consistency',1,N'Merged into IRV-03 — Merged'),
(503,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-09',N'Review security technologies',N'The organisation must assess whether security technologies are appropriate, implemented and maintained. The purpose is to confirm technology supports required protection.',N'Confirm technology supports required protection.',N'security technology; implementation; maintenance; protection',1,N'Merged into IRV-03 — Merged'),
(504,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-10',N'Assess continuing suitability',N'The organisation must evaluate whether the security approach remains suitable for current needs and risks. The purpose is to keep security aligned with the organization.',N'Keep security aligned with the organization.',N'suitability; current need; risk; alignment',1,N'Merged into IRV-12 — Merged'),
(505,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-11',N'Assess continuing adequacy',N'The organisation must evaluate whether security arrangements are sufficient in scope and depth. The purpose is to identify missing or insufficient protection.',N'Identify missing or insufficient protection.',N'adequacy; sufficiency; scope; protection gap',1,N'Merged into IRV-12 — Merged'),
(506,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-12',N'Assess continuing effectiveness',N'The organisation must evaluate whether security arrangements achieve their intended results. It must assess continuing suitability. It must assess continuing adequacy. The purpose is to confirm controls and management practices work. It also aims to keep security aligned with the organization. It also aims to identify missing or insufficient protection.',N'Confirm controls and management practices work. Keep security aligned with the organization; Identify missing or insufficient protection.',N'suitability; current need; risk; alignment; adequacy; sufficiency; scope; protection gap; effectiveness; result; control; performance',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(507,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-13',N'Identify improvement opportunities',N'The organisation must record opportunities to improve the security approach and implementation. The purpose is to drive continual improvement from independent insight.',N'Drive continual improvement from independent insight.',N'improvement; opportunity; recommendation; review',1,N'Merged into IRV-06 — Merged'),
(508,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-14',N'Assess the need for policy and control changes',N'The organisation must evaluate whether policies, topic-specific policies and other controls need revision. The purpose is to keep security direction and controls current.',N'Keep security direction and controls current.',N'policy change; control change; topic policy; revision',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(509,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-15',N'Ensure reviewer independence',N'The organisation must use reviewers who are independent of the area being reviewed. It must ensure reviewer competence. The purpose is to protect objectivity and credibility of conclusions. It also aims to produce reliable and informed review results.',N'Protect objectivity and credibility of conclusions. Produce reliable and informed review results.',N'reviewer independence; objectivity; conflict; area; reviewer competence; skill; knowledge; experience',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(510,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-16',N'Ensure reviewer competence',N'The organisation must select reviewers with suitable knowledge, skills and experience. The purpose is to produce reliable and informed review results.',N'Produce reliable and informed review results.',N'reviewer competence; skill; knowledge; experience',1,N'Merged into IRV-15 — Merged'),
(511,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-17',N'Avoid line-authority conflicts',N'The organisation must ensure reviewers are not in the line of authority for the area assessed. The purpose is to prevent management influence over the assessment.',N'Prevent management influence over the assessment.',N'line authority; conflict; independence; reporting line',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(512,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-18',N'Report review results to management',N'The organisation must report results to the initiating management and, where appropriate, top management. The purpose is to ensure findings reach accountable decision-makers.',N'Ensure findings reach accountable decision-makers.',N'review result; management report; top management; finding',1,N'Merged into IRV-19 — Merged'),
(513,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-19',N'Maintain independent review records',N'The organisation must retain plans, evidence, findings, reports, decisions and follow-up records. It must govern independent information security reviews. It must maintain an independent review process. It must report review results to management. The purpose is to preserve an audit trail of reviews and actions. It also aims to ensure reviews are planned, objective and acted upon. It also aims to make reviews consistent and repeatable. It also aims to ensure findings reach accountable decision-makers.',N'Preserve an audit trail of reviews and actions. Ensure reviews are planned, objective and acted upon; Make reviews consistent and repeatable; Ensure findings reach accountable decision-makers.',N'independent review; governance; accountability; oversight; review process; method; planning; reporting; follow-up; review result; management report; top management; finding; review record',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(514,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-20',N'Initiate corrective actions',N'The organisation must require management to correct inadequate security management or implementation identified by reviews. The purpose is to resolve weaknesses and restore required performance.',N'Resolve weaknesses and restore required performance.',N'corrective action; inadequacy; remediation; management',1,N'Merged into IRV-05 — Merged'),
(515,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-21',N'Trigger reviews after legal changes',N'The organisation must consider an independent review when relevant laws or regulations change. The purpose is to adapt security management to changed obligations.',N'Adapt security management to changed obligations.',N'law change; regulation change; trigger; review',1,N'Merged into IRV-24 — Merged'),
(516,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-22',N'Trigger reviews after significant incidents',N'The organisation must consider an independent review after a significant information security incident. The purpose is to learn whether management arrangements need change.',N'Learn whether management arrangements need change.',N'significant incident; trigger; independent review; learning',1,N'Merged into IRV-24 — Merged'),
(517,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-23',N'Trigger reviews after business or service changes',N'The organisation must consider an independent review when starting or changing a business, product or service. The purpose is to address risks introduced by major organizational change.',N'Address risks introduced by major organizational change.',N'business change; product; service; trigger; risk',1,N'Merged into IRV-24 — Merged'),
(518,36,N'5.35',N'IRV-24',N'Trigger reviews after control changes',N'The organisation must consider an independent review after significant changes to security controls or procedures. It must trigger reviews after legal changes. It must trigger reviews after significant incidents. It must trigger reviews after business or service changes. The purpose is to confirm changed controls remain suitable and effective. It also aims to adapt security management to changed obligations. It also aims to learn whether management arrangements need change. It also aims to address risks introduced by major organizational change.',N'Confirm changed controls remain suitable and effective. Adapt security management to changed obligations; Learn whether management arrangements need change; Address risks introduced by major organizational change.',N'law change; regulation change; trigger; review; significant incident; independent review; learning; business change; product; service; risk; control change; procedure change; effectiveness',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(519,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-01',N'Govern security compliance reviews',N'The organisation must define accountability and oversight for reviewing compliance with security requirements. It must schedule regular compliance reviews. It must review compliance with other regulations. The purpose is to ensure compliance reviews are owned and consistently managed. It also aims to check compliance before weaknesses persist. It also aims to cover all relevant compliance duties.',N'Ensure compliance reviews are owned and consistently managed. Check compliance before weaknesses persist; Cover all relevant compliance duties.',N'compliance review; governance; accountability; oversight; schedule; regular review; interval; risk; regulation; requirement; obligation; compliance',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(520,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-02',N'Maintain a compliance review method',N'The organisation must document how compliance will be measured, reviewed, recorded and reported. The purpose is to make reviews consistent and repeatable.',N'Make reviews consistent and repeatable.',N'review method; measurement; evidence; reporting',1,N'Merged into CMP-16 — Merged'),
(521,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-03',N'Assign managers and information owners',N'The organisation must assign managers and service, product or information owners to review requirements in their areas. The purpose is to place compliance accountability with responsible owners.',N'Place compliance accountability with responsible owners.',N'manager; service owner; product owner; information owner',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(522,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-04',N'Schedule regular compliance reviews',N'The organisation must set planned review intervals based on risk and requirement. The purpose is to check compliance before weaknesses persist.',N'Check compliance before weaknesses persist.',N'schedule; regular review; interval; risk',1,N'Merged into CMP-01 — Merged'),
(523,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-05',N'Review compliance with the security policy',N'The organisation must check implementation and operation against the main information security policy. It must review compliance with topic-specific policies. It must record identified non-compliance. It must identify causes of non-compliance. The purpose is to confirm security direction is followed. It also aims to confirm detailed policy requirements are followed. It also aims to make deficiencies visible and traceable. It also aims to address underlying causes rather than symptoms.',N'Confirm security direction is followed. Confirm detailed policy requirements are followed; Make deficiencies visible and traceable; Address underlying causes rather than symptoms.',N'security policy; compliance; implementation; operation; topic policy; requirement; non-compliance; finding; evidence; owner; risk; root cause; analysis; weakness',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(524,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-06',N'Review compliance with topic-specific policies',N'The organisation must check implementation and operation against applicable topic-specific policies. The purpose is to confirm detailed policy requirements are followed.',N'Confirm detailed policy requirements are followed.',N'topic policy; compliance; requirement; operation',1,N'Merged into CMP-05 — Merged'),
(525,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-07',N'Review compliance with security rules',N'The organisation must check activities and configurations against applicable information security rules. The purpose is to detect rule violations and control bypass.',N'Detect rule violations and control bypass.',N'security rule; configuration; violation; control',1,N'Merged into CMP-16 — Merged'),
(526,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-08',N'Review compliance with security standards',N'The organisation must check systems, services and activities against approved information security standards. The purpose is to maintain consistent minimum protection.',N'Maintain consistent minimum protection.',N'security standard; system; service; baseline',1,N'Merged into CMP-16 — Merged'),
(527,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-09',N'Review compliance with other regulations',N'The organisation must include other applicable regulatory and organizational requirements in reviews. The purpose is to cover all relevant compliance duties.',N'Cover all relevant compliance duties.',N'regulation; requirement; obligation; compliance',1,N'Merged into CMP-01 — Merged'),
(528,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-10',N'Use automated compliance measurement',N'The organisation must use suitable automated measurement and reporting tools where efficient and reliable. The purpose is to improve review coverage and timeliness.',N'Improve review coverage and timeliness.',N'automation; measurement; reporting tool; monitoring',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(529,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-11',N'Record identified non-compliance',N'The organisation must document each non-compliance, affected requirement, evidence, owner, risk and status. The purpose is to make deficiencies visible and traceable.',N'Make deficiencies visible and traceable.',N'non-compliance; finding; evidence; owner; risk',1,N'Merged into CMP-05 — Merged'),
(530,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-12',N'Identify causes of non-compliance',N'The organisation must analyze why each non-compliance occurred. The purpose is to address underlying causes rather than symptoms.',N'Address underlying causes rather than symptoms.',N'root cause; non-compliance; analysis; weakness',1,N'Merged into CMP-05 — Merged'),
(531,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-13',N'Evaluate corrective action needs',N'The organisation must assess whether corrective action is required and prioritize it according to risk. The purpose is to select proportionate treatment for findings.',N'Select proportionate treatment for findings.',N'corrective action; evaluation; priority; risk',1,N'Merged into CMP-15 — Merged'),
(532,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-14',N'Implement corrective actions',N'The organisation must assign, track and complete approved actions to restore compliance. The purpose is to correct deficiencies in a controlled manner.',N'Correct deficiencies in a controlled manner.',N'corrective action; owner; tracking; remediation',1,N'Merged into CMP-15 — Merged'),
(533,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-15',N'Verify corrective action effectiveness',N'The organisation must review completed actions to confirm compliance and identify remaining weaknesses. It must evaluate corrective action needs. It must implement corrective actions. It must track overdue corrective actions. The purpose is to ensure remediation produces the intended result. It also aims to select proportionate treatment for findings. It also aims to correct deficiencies in a controlled manner. It also aims to prevent unresolved non-compliance from being forgotten.',N'Ensure remediation produces the intended result. Select proportionate treatment for findings; Correct deficiencies in a controlled manner; Prevent unresolved non-compliance from being forgotten.',N'corrective action; evaluation; priority; risk; owner; tracking; remediation; effectiveness review; verification; weakness; overdue action; progress; next review; escalation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(534,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-16',N'Maintain compliance review records',N'The organisation must retain review results, findings, decisions, actions and verification evidence. It must maintain a compliance review method. It must review compliance with security rules. It must review compliance with security standards. The purpose is to preserve evidence of review and remediation. It also aims to make reviews consistent and repeatable. It also aims to detect rule violations and control bypass. It also aims to maintain consistent minimum protection.',N'Preserve evidence of review and remediation. Make reviews consistent and repeatable; Detect rule violations and control bypass; Maintain consistent minimum protection.',N'review method; measurement; evidence; reporting; security rule; configuration; violation; control; security standard; system; service; baseline; review record; result',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(535,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-17',N'Report results to independent reviewers',N'The organisation must provide relevant review and corrective-action results during independent reviews. The purpose is to support complete and informed independent assessment.',N'Support complete and informed independent assessment.',N'independent review; result; report; corrective action',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(536,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-18',N'Complete actions according to risk',N'The organisation must set and meet corrective-action time frames appropriate to the compliance risk. The purpose is to resolve higher risks promptly.',N'Resolve higher risks promptly.',N'risk; due date; timely action; remediation',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(537,37,N'5.36',N'CMP-19',N'Track overdue corrective actions',N'The organisation must address incomplete action progress at the next scheduled review and escalate where needed. The purpose is to prevent unresolved non-compliance from being forgotten.',N'Prevent unresolved non-compliance from being forgotten.',N'overdue action; progress; next review; escalation',1,N'Merged into CMP-15 — Merged'),
(538,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-01',N'Govern documented operating procedures',N'The organisation must define ownership, approval and oversight for secure operating procedures. It must review update and authorize procedures. The purpose is to ensure operating instructions are controlled and accountable. It also aims to keep operating instructions current and controlled.',N'Ensure operating instructions are controlled and accountable. Keep operating instructions current and controlled.',N'operating procedure; governance; owner; approval; procedure review; update; authorization; change',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(539,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-02',N'Identify activities requiring procedures',N'The organisation must determine which operational security activities need documented instructions. The purpose is to focus documentation on activities where consistency matters.',N'Focus documentation on activities where consistency matters.',N'procedure need; operational activity; risk; documentation',1,N'Merged into SOP-05 — Merged'),
(540,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-03',N'Document activities performed by many people',N'The organisation must prepare common procedures when multiple people must perform an activity consistently. The purpose is to reduce variation and human error.',N'Reduce variation and human error.',N'many users; consistency; common procedure; error',1,N'Merged into SOP-04 — Merged'),
(541,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-04',N'Document rarely performed activities',N'The organisation must prepare procedures for activities that may be forgotten between uses. It must document activities performed by many people. It must document schedules and dependencies. It must document maintenance activities. The purpose is to support correct performance of infrequent work. It also aims to reduce variation and human error. It also aims to prevent failures caused by incorrect scheduling. It also aims to keep facilities and systems reliable and protected.',N'Support correct performance of infrequent work. Reduce variation and human error; Prevent failures caused by incorrect scheduling; Keep facilities and systems reliable and protected.',N'many users; consistency; common procedure; error; rare activity; infrequent; instruction; memory; schedule; dependency; sequence; system; timing; maintenance',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(542,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-05',N'Document new high-risk activities',N'The organisation must prepare procedures before new activities where incorrect performance creates risk. It must identify activities requiring procedures. It must document activities before handover. The purpose is to control risk during introduction of new work. It also aims to focus documentation on activities where consistency matters. It also aims to maintain safe operation through personnel changes.',N'Control risk during introduction of new work. Focus documentation on activities where consistency matters; Maintain safe operation through personnel changes.',N'procedure need; operational activity; risk; documentation; new activity; procedure; implementation; handover; new personnel; knowledge transfer',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(543,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-06',N'Document activities before handover',N'The organisation must prepare and update procedures before transferring work to new personnel. The purpose is to maintain safe operation through personnel changes.',N'Maintain safe operation through personnel changes.',N'handover; new personnel; knowledge transfer; procedure',1,N'Merged into SOP-05 — Merged'),
(544,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-07',N'Name responsible individuals',N'The organisation must specify accountable and responsible individuals within each procedure. The purpose is to make operational responsibility clear.',N'Make operational responsibility clear.',N'responsible person; accountable; role; procedure',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(545,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-08',N'Document secure installation',N'The organisation must provide instructions for securely installing systems and components. It must document secure configuration. It must document automated information processing. It must document resilience operations. The purpose is to prevent insecure deployment. It also aims to maintain secure and consistent settings. It also aims to protect information handled automatically. It also aims to support continued secure operation during disruption.',N'Prevent insecure deployment. Maintain secure and consistent settings; Protect information handled automatically; Support continued secure operation during disruption.',N'secure installation; system; component; deployment; secure configuration; setting; baseline; automated processing; information; operation; resilience; continuity; disruption',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(546,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-09',N'Document secure configuration',N'The organisation must provide instructions for approved and secure system configuration. The purpose is to maintain secure and consistent settings.',N'Maintain secure and consistent settings.',N'secure configuration; setting; baseline; system',1,N'Merged into SOP-08 — Merged'),
(547,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-10',N'Document automated information processing',N'The organisation must describe secure operation and control of automated information processing. The purpose is to protect information handled automatically.',N'Protect information handled automatically.',N'automated processing; information; system; operation',1,N'Merged into SOP-08 — Merged'),
(548,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-11',N'Document manual information handling',N'The organisation must describe secure steps for manual processing and handling of information. It must document error handling. It must document storage media handling. The purpose is to protect information outside automated workflows. It also aims to restore correct operation after errors. It also aims to protect information throughout media handling.',N'Protect information outside automated workflows. Restore correct operation after errors; Protect information throughout media handling.',N'manual processing; information handling; workflow; protection; error handling; detection; correction; escalation; storage media; handling; movement; disposal',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(549,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-12',N'Document backup operations',N'The organisation must define backup execution, monitoring, failure handling and evidence requirements. The purpose is to ensure backups are performed securely and reliably.',N'Ensure backups are performed securely and reliably.',N'backup; monitoring; failure; evidence; operation',1,N'Merged into SOP-21 — Merged'),
(550,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-13',N'Document resilience operations',N'The organisation must define routine and exceptional steps that maintain operational resilience. The purpose is to support continued secure operation during disruption.',N'Support continued secure operation during disruption.',N'resilience; continuity; disruption; operation',1,N'Merged into SOP-08 — Merged'),
(551,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-14',N'Document schedules and dependencies',N'The organisation must specify timing, sequence and dependencies with other systems and activities. The purpose is to prevent failures caused by incorrect scheduling.',N'Prevent failures caused by incorrect scheduling.',N'schedule; dependency; sequence; system; timing',1,N'Merged into SOP-04 — Merged'),
(552,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-15',N'Document error handling',N'The organisation must provide instructions for detecting, recording, correcting and escalating processing errors. The purpose is to restore correct operation after errors.',N'Restore correct operation after errors.',N'error handling; detection; correction; escalation',1,N'Merged into SOP-11 — Merged'),
(553,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-16',N'Document exceptional conditions',N'The organisation must define safe actions and restrictions for unusual conditions during job execution. It must document system restart and recovery. The purpose is to control risk when normal procedures do not apply. It also aims to restore systems safely and predictably.',N'Control risk when normal procedures do not apply. Restore systems safely and predictably.',N'exception; unusual condition; restriction; job execution; restart; recovery; system failure; instruction',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(554,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-17',N'Control utility program use',N'The organisation must document restrictions and approvals for utility programs used during operations. It must use consistent procedures tools and utilities. The purpose is to prevent powerful tools from bypassing controls. It also aims to reduce variation and improve secure operation.',N'Prevent powerful tools from bypassing controls. Reduce variation and improve secure operation.',N'utility program; restriction; approval; privileged tool; consistency; common procedure; tool; utility; system',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(555,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-18',N'Maintain support and escalation contacts',N'The organisation must list internal and external support and escalation contacts for operational difficulty. The purpose is to enable timely help and escalation.',N'Enable timely help and escalation.',N'support contact; escalation; external support; difficulty',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(556,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-19',N'Document storage media handling',N'The organisation must specify secure use, movement, storage and disposal of media. The purpose is to protect information throughout media handling.',N'Protect information throughout media handling.',N'storage media; handling; movement; disposal; protection',1,N'Merged into SOP-11 — Merged'),
(557,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-20',N'Document system restart and recovery',N'The organisation must provide tested restart and recovery instructions for system failure. The purpose is to restore systems safely and predictably.',N'Restore systems safely and predictably.',N'restart; recovery; system failure; instruction',1,N'Merged into SOP-16 — Merged'),
(558,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-21',N'Document audit trail and monitoring operations',N'The organisation must define management of audit trails, system logs and video monitoring information. It must document backup operations. It must document capacity performance and security monitoring. The purpose is to preserve reliable operational and security evidence. It also aims to ensure backups are performed securely and reliably. It also aims to detect operational and security issues promptly.',N'Preserve reliable operational and security evidence. Ensure backups are performed securely and reliably; Detect operational and security issues promptly.',N'backup; monitoring; failure; evidence; operation; audit trail; system log; video monitoring; capacity; performance; security monitoring; alert',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(559,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-22',N'Document capacity performance and security monitoring',N'The organisation must specify monitoring steps, thresholds, alerts, response and records. The purpose is to detect operational and security issues promptly.',N'Detect operational and security issues promptly.',N'capacity; performance; security monitoring; alert',1,N'Merged into SOP-21 — Merged'),
(560,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-23',N'Document maintenance activities',N'The organisation must provide secure instructions, schedules and evidence requirements for maintenance. The purpose is to keep facilities and systems reliable and protected.',N'Keep facilities and systems reliable and protected.',N'maintenance; schedule; instruction; evidence',1,N'Merged into SOP-04 — Merged'),
(561,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-24',N'Review update and authorize procedures',N'The organisation must review procedures when needed, update them and require authorization for changes. The purpose is to keep operating instructions current and controlled.',N'Keep operating instructions current and controlled.',N'procedure review; update; authorization; change',1,N'Merged into SOP-01 — Merged'),
(562,38,N'5.37',N'SOP-25',N'Use consistent procedures tools and utilities',N'The organisation must manage similar systems consistently with common procedures, tools and utilities where feasible. The purpose is to reduce variation and improve secure operation.',N'Reduce variation and improve secure operation.',N'consistency; common procedure; tool; utility; system',1,N'Merged into SOP-17 — Merged'),
(563,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-01',N'Govern security terms of employment',N'The organisation must define ownership and approval for information security employment and equivalent contractual terms. The purpose is to ensure security duties are consistently included and enforced.',N'Ensure security duties are consistently included and enforced.',N'employment terms; security responsibility; contract; governance',1,N'Merged into EMP-15 — Merged'),
(564,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-02',N'Align terms with security policies',N'The organisation must reflect the main security policy and relevant topic-specific policies in contractual obligations. It must review terms after requirement changes. The purpose is to connect personnel duties to approved security direction. It also aims to keep contractual obligations current.',N'Connect personnel duties to approved security direction. Keep contractual obligations current.',N'security policy; topic policy; employment; obligation; legal change; policy change; contract review; update',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(565,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-03',N'State organizational responsibilities',N'The organisation must document the organization’s information security commitments and responsibilities toward personnel. The purpose is to clarify mutual security obligations.',N'Clarify mutual security obligations.',N'organization responsibility; personnel; contract; security',1,N'Merged into EMP-04 — Merged'),
(566,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-04',N'State personnel responsibilities',N'The organisation must document the information security responsibilities personnel must fulfil in their roles. It must state organizational responsibilities. It must state information classification duties. It must state asset management duties. The purpose is to ensure personnel understand expected secure behaviour. It also aims to clarify mutual security obligations. It also aims to maintain required protection throughout information handling. It also aims to protect assigned assets and services.',N'Ensure personnel understand expected secure behaviour. Clarify mutual security obligations; Maintain required protection throughout information handling; Protect assigned assets and services.',N'organization responsibility; personnel; contract; security; personnel responsibility; role; security duty; behaviour; classification; labelling; handling; asset; facility; service',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(567,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-05',N'Require confidentiality commitments',N'The organisation must require suitable confidentiality or non-disclosure commitments before access to confidential information. The purpose is to protect confidential information from the start of access.',N'Protect confidential information from the start of access.',N'confidentiality; NDA; access; agreement',1,N'Merged into EMP-13 — Merged'),
(568,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-06',N'State legal responsibilities and rights',N'The organisation must include relevant legal duties and rights such as intellectual property and privacy obligations. It must state consequences of security violations. The purpose is to make legal expectations clear to personnel. It also aims to deter violations and support fair enforcement.',N'Make legal expectations clear to personnel. Deter violations and support fair enforcement.',N'law; rights; copyright; privacy; employment; violation; consequence; disciplinary; security requirement',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(569,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-07',N'State information classification duties',N'The organisation must define personnel duties for classifying, labelling and handling information. The purpose is to maintain required protection throughout information handling.',N'Maintain required protection throughout information handling.',N'classification; labelling; handling; personnel',1,N'Merged into EMP-04 — Merged'),
(570,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-08',N'State asset management duties',N'The organisation must define responsibilities for organizational information, assets, facilities and services handled by personnel. The purpose is to protect assigned assets and services.',N'Protect assigned assets and services.',N'asset; facility; service; personnel; responsibility',1,N'Merged into EMP-04 — Merged'),
(571,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-09',N'Protect interested-party information',N'The organisation must define duties for handling information received from customers, suppliers and other interested parties. The purpose is to meet entrusted-information obligations.',N'Meet entrusted-information obligations.',N'interested party; customer; supplier; information handling',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(572,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-10',N'State consequences of security violations',N'The organisation must describe potential action when personnel disregard security requirements. The purpose is to deter violations and support fair enforcement.',N'Deter violations and support fair enforcement.',N'violation; consequence; disciplinary; security requirement',1,N'Merged into EMP-06 — Merged'),
(573,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-11',N'Communicate duties before employment',N'The organisation must explain information security roles and responsibilities during the pre-employment process. The purpose is to enable informed acceptance before engagement.',N'Enable informed acceptance before engagement.',N'pre-employment; communication; duty; candidate',1,N'Merged into EMP-15 — Merged'),
(574,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-12',N'Obtain agreement to security terms',N'The organisation must record personnel acceptance of security terms appropriate to their role and access. The purpose is to create clear and demonstrable commitment.',N'Create clear and demonstrable commitment.',N'acceptance; signature; security terms; access',1,N'Merged into EMP-13 — Merged'),
(575,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-13',N'Scale terms to access and risk',N'The organisation must tailor security terms to the nature and extent of access to systems, services and assets. It must require confidentiality commitments. It must obtain agreement to security terms. The purpose is to apply proportionate obligations. It also aims to protect confidential information from the start of access. It also aims to create clear and demonstrable commitment.',N'Apply proportionate obligations. Protect confidential information from the start of access; Create clear and demonstrable commitment.',N'confidentiality; NDA; access; agreement; acceptance; signature; security terms; role risk; proportionality; contract',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(576,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-14',N'Review terms after requirement changes',N'The organisation must review and update terms when laws, regulations or security policies change. The purpose is to keep contractual obligations current.',N'Keep contractual obligations current.',N'legal change; policy change; contract review; update',1,N'Merged into EMP-02 — Merged'),
(577,39,N'6.2',N'EMP-15',N'Continue duties after employment',N'The organisation must define security responsibilities that remain valid for a stated period after employment or contract ends. It must govern security terms of employment. It must communicate duties before employment. The purpose is to protect information after personnel leave. It also aims to ensure security duties are consistently included and enforced. It also aims to enable informed acceptance before engagement.',N'Protect information after personnel leave. Ensure security duties are consistently included and enforced; Enable informed acceptance before engagement.',N'employment terms; security responsibility; contract; governance; pre-employment; communication; duty; candidate; post-employment; continuing duty; confidentiality',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(578,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-01',N'Govern the security learning programme',N'The organisation must define ownership, scope, approval and oversight for awareness, education and training. It must measure programme effectiveness. The purpose is to maintain a coordinated and accountable programme. It also aims to improve programme results using evidence.',N'Maintain a coordinated and accountable programme. Improve programme results using evidence.',N'awareness; education; training; governance; programme; effectiveness; metric; behaviour; improvement',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(579,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-02',N'Align learning with policies and procedures',N'The organisation must base learning content on current security policies, topic policies and procedures. The purpose is to teach the requirements personnel must follow.',N'Teach the requirements personnel must follow.',N'policy; procedure; learning content; alignment',1,N'Merged into TRN-14 — Merged'),
(580,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-03',N'Reflect information and controls',N'The organisation must design learning around protected information and implemented security controls. The purpose is to make training relevant to actual organizational risks.',N'Make training relevant to actual organizational risks.',N'information; control; risk; training design',1,N'Merged into TRN-20 — Merged'),
(581,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-04',N'Cover personnel and interested parties',N'The organisation must include internal personnel and relevant consultants, supplier personnel and other parties. It must use repeated awareness activities. The purpose is to extend awareness to everyone who can affect security. It also aims to maintain sustained awareness.',N'Extend awareness to everyone who can affect security. Maintain sustained awareness.',N'personnel; consultant; supplier; interested party; campaign; schedule; repetition; new personnel',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(582,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-05',N'Provide induction learning',N'The organisation must deliver appropriate awareness and training to new personnel before or shortly after access. The purpose is to establish secure behaviour from the beginning.',N'Establish secure behaviour from the beginning.',N'induction; onboarding; new personnel; access',1,N'Merged into TRN-14 — Merged'),
(583,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-06',N'Train after role changes',N'The organisation must provide updated learning when personnel move to roles with substantially different security requirements. The purpose is to prepare personnel for changed duties and access.',N'Prepare personnel for changed duties and access.',N'role change; transfer; updated training; responsibility',1,N'Merged into TRN-11 — Merged'),
(584,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-07',N'Repeat learning periodically',N'The organisation must schedule regular updates and reinforcement activities. The purpose is to keep security knowledge current and visible.',N'Keep security knowledge current and visible.',N'periodic; refresher; reinforcement; schedule',1,N'Merged into TRN-14 — Merged'),
(585,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-08',N'Assess learner understanding',N'The organisation must test understanding after awareness, education or training activities. It must keep specialist knowledge current. The purpose is to confirm knowledge transfer. It also aims to maintain up-to-date technical competence.',N'Confirm knowledge transfer. Maintain up-to-date technical competence.',N'assessment; understanding; test; knowledge transfer; professional development; current knowledge; conference; newsletter',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(586,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-09',N'Measure programme effectiveness',N'The organisation must evaluate whether learning activities improve knowledge and behaviour. The purpose is to improve programme results using evidence.',N'Improve programme results using evidence.',N'effectiveness; metric; behaviour; improvement',1,N'Merged into TRN-01 — Merged'),
(587,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-10',N'Teach individual security responsibilities',N'The organisation must explain each audience’s responsibilities and how to fulfil them. It must teach applicable rules and obligations. It must teach personal accountability. It must teach basic security procedures. The purpose is to turn awareness into responsible action. It also aims to improve compliance with security obligations. It also aims to encourage responsible security behaviour. It also aims to enable correct everyday security actions.',N'Turn awareness into responsible action. Improve compliance with security obligations; Encourage responsible security behaviour; Enable correct everyday security actions.',N'responsibility; role; behaviour; accountability; rule; law; standard; contract; compliance; action; inaction; information protection; basic procedure; event reporting',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(588,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-11',N'Plan learning by role',N'The organisation must tailor content, depth and frequency to internal and external personnel roles. It must train after role changes. It must publish support contacts and resources. The purpose is to deliver relevant learning to each audience. It also aims to prepare personnel for changed duties and access. It also aims to help personnel obtain timely guidance.',N'Deliver relevant learning to each audience. Prepare personnel for changed duties and access; Help personnel obtain timely guidance.',N'role change; transfer; updated training; responsibility; role-based; audience; content; frequency; contact; resource; advice; learning material',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(589,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-12',N'Use repeated awareness activities',N'The organisation must schedule campaigns and activities over time and include new personnel. The purpose is to maintain sustained awareness.',N'Maintain sustained awareness.',N'campaign; schedule; repetition; new personnel',1,N'Merged into TRN-04 — Merged'),
(590,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-13',N'Apply incident lessons',N'The organisation must update learning content using lessons from security incidents. The purpose is to prevent recurrence through shared learning.',N'Prevent recurrence through shared learning.',N'incident lesson; awareness; update; prevention',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(591,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-14',N'Use suitable learning channels',N'The organisation must use appropriate physical and virtual channels such as briefings, e-learning and campaigns. It must align learning with policies and procedures. It must provide induction learning. It must repeat learning periodically. The purpose is to make learning accessible and engaging. It also aims to teach the requirements personnel must follow. It also aims to establish secure behaviour from the beginning. It also aims to keep security knowledge current and visible.',N'Make learning accessible and engaging. Teach the requirements personnel must follow; Establish secure behaviour from the beginning; Keep security knowledge current and visible.',N'policy; procedure; learning content; alignment; induction; onboarding; new personnel; access; periodic; refresher; reinforcement; schedule; channel; e-learning',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(592,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-15',N'Communicate management commitment',N'The organisation must explain management’s commitment to information security. The purpose is to reinforce organizational priority and leadership.',N'Reinforce organizational priority and leadership.',N'management commitment; leadership; awareness; culture',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(593,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-16',N'Teach applicable rules and obligations',N'The organisation must cover policies, standards, laws, regulations, contracts and agreements relevant to personnel. The purpose is to improve compliance with security obligations.',N'Improve compliance with security obligations.',N'rule; law; standard; contract; compliance',1,N'Merged into TRN-10 — Merged'),
(594,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-17',N'Teach personal accountability',N'The organisation must explain accountability for actions, inaction and protection of organizational and third-party information. The purpose is to encourage responsible security behaviour.',N'Encourage responsible security behaviour.',N'accountability; action; inaction; information protection',1,N'Merged into TRN-10 — Merged'),
(595,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-18',N'Teach basic security procedures',N'The organisation must cover essential procedures, baseline controls, event reporting and password security. The purpose is to enable correct everyday security actions.',N'Enable correct everyday security actions.',N'basic procedure; event reporting; password; baseline',1,N'Merged into TRN-10 — Merged'),
(596,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-19',N'Publish support contacts and resources',N'The organisation must provide contact points and resources for security advice and further learning. The purpose is to help personnel obtain timely guidance.',N'Help personnel obtain timely guidance.',N'contact; resource; advice; learning material',1,N'Merged into TRN-11 — Merged'),
(597,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-20',N'Maintain technical training plans',N'The organisation must identify and implement role-specific training plans for technical teams. It must reflect information and controls. It must address technical skill gaps. The purpose is to build skills needed to secure technology. It also aims to make training relevant to actual organizational risks. It also aims to ensure required expertise is available.',N'Build skills needed to secure technology. Make training relevant to actual organizational risks; Ensure required expertise is available.',N'information; control; risk; training design; technical training; plan; skill; team; skill gap; mentoring; recruitment; specialist',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(598,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-21',N'Address technical skill gaps',N'The organisation must identify missing security skills and acquire them through training, mentoring, recruitment or specialists. The purpose is to ensure required expertise is available.',N'Ensure required expertise is available.',N'skill gap; mentoring; recruitment; specialist',1,N'Merged into TRN-20 — Merged'),
(599,40,N'6.3',N'TRN-22',N'Keep specialist knowledge current',N'The organisation must support continuing professional development through current materials, events and communities. The purpose is to maintain up-to-date technical competence.',N'Maintain up-to-date technical competence.',N'professional development; current knowledge; conference; newsletter',1,N'Merged into TRN-08 — Merged'),
(600,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-01',N'Govern the disciplinary process',N'The organisation must define ownership, authority, approval and oversight for security-related disciplinary action. It must formalize disciplinary procedures. It must protect subject identity. It must maintain disciplinary evidence and outcomes. The purpose is to ensure fair, consistent and lawful handling. It also aims to create a repeatable and controlled process. It also aims to maintain privacy and fairness. It also aims to demonstrate fair and consistent handling.',N'Ensure fair, consistent and lawful handling. Create a repeatable and controlled process; Maintain privacy and fairness; Demonstrate fair and consistent handling.',N'disciplinary; governance; authority; security violation; procedure; investigation; decision; appeal; record; identity; privacy; confidentiality; evidence; action',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed');

INSERT #prac(seq,sheet_statement_id,statement_reference,practice_ref,practice_name,practice_statement,objective,keywords,is_merged,merge_status) VALUES
(601,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-02',N'Formalize disciplinary procedures',N'The organisation must document investigation, decision, action, appeal and recordkeeping steps. The purpose is to create a repeatable and controlled process.',N'Create a repeatable and controlled process.',N'procedure; investigation; decision; appeal; record',1,N'Merged into DSP-01 — Merged'),
(602,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-04',N'Verify violations before action',N'The organisation must confirm with reliable evidence that a security policy violation occurred before initiating discipline. It must handle deliberate serious violations promptly. The purpose is to prevent unsupported or unfair action. It also aims to limit ongoing harm and exposure.',N'Prevent unsupported or unfair action. Limit ongoing harm and exposure.',N'verification; evidence; violation; investigation; deliberate violation; immediate action; serious; harm',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(603,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-05',N'Apply graduated responses',N'The organisation must define increasing responses appropriate to the circumstances and seriousness of violations. The purpose is to apply proportionate consequences.',N'Apply proportionate consequences.',N'graduated response; proportionate; consequence; severity',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(604,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-06',N'Assess breach nature and gravity',N'The organisation must consider who, what, when, how, seriousness and consequences. The purpose is to base decisions on complete circumstances.',N'Base decisions on complete circumstances.',N'nature; gravity; consequence; breach',1,N'Merged into DSP-09 — Merged'),
(605,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-07',N'Assess intent',N'The organisation must distinguish malicious or deliberate action from accidental behaviour. The purpose is to match response to intent and risk.',N'Match response to intent and risk.',N'intent; malicious; accidental; assessment',1,N'Merged into DSP-09 — Merged'),
(606,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-08',N'Assess repeat offences',N'The organisation must consider whether the matter is a first or repeated offence. The purpose is to escalate persistent non-compliance appropriately.',N'Escalate persistent non-compliance appropriately.',N'repeat offence; first offence; history; escalation',1,N'Merged into DSP-09 — Merged'),
(607,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-09',N'Assess prior training',N'The organisation must consider whether the person received appropriate training and understood the requirement. It must assess breach nature and gravity. It must assess intent. It must assess repeat offences. The purpose is to support fair and informed decisions. It also aims to base decisions on complete circumstances. It also aims to match response to intent and risk. It also aims to escalate persistent non-compliance appropriately.',N'Support fair and informed decisions. Base decisions on complete circumstances; Match response to intent and risk; Escalate persistent non-compliance appropriately.',N'nature; gravity; consequence; breach; intent; malicious; accidental; assessment; repeat offence; first offence; history; escalation; training; awareness',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(608,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-10',N'Meet legal and contractual requirements',N'The organisation must apply relevant legal, statutory, regulatory, contractual and business requirements. The purpose is to keep disciplinary action lawful and enforceable.',N'Keep disciplinary action lawful and enforceable.',N'law; regulation; contract; employment; discipline',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(609,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-11',N'Handle deliberate serious violations promptly',N'The organisation must allow immediate proportionate action for deliberate serious security violations. The purpose is to limit ongoing harm and exposure.',N'Limit ongoing harm and exposure.',N'deliberate violation; immediate action; serious; harm',1,N'Merged into DSP-04 — Merged'),
(610,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-12',N'Protect subject identity',N'The organisation must protect the identity and personal information of individuals subject to action as required. The purpose is to maintain privacy and fairness.',N'Maintain privacy and fairness.',N'identity; privacy; confidentiality; disciplinary',1,N'Merged into DSP-01 — Merged'),
(611,41,N'6.4',N'DSP-13',N'Maintain disciplinary evidence and outcomes',N'The organisation must retain authorized evidence, decisions, actions, appeals and closure records. The purpose is to demonstrate fair and consistent handling.',N'Demonstrate fair and consistent handling.',N'evidence; decision; action; appeal; record',1,N'Merged into DSP-01 — Merged'),
(612,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-01',N'Govern termination and role-change security',N'The organisation must define ownership and oversight for security during employment and contract transitions. It must define continuing security duties. It must treat role changes as exit and entry. It must communicate employment changes. The purpose is to coordinate complete and timely transition controls. It also aims to protect organizational interests after transition. It also aims to apply complete access and responsibility transitions. It also aims to keep working relationships and authority current.',N'Coordinate complete and timely transition controls. Protect organizational interests after transition; Apply complete access and responsibility transitions; Keep working relationships and authority current.',N'termination; role change; governance; transition; continuing duty; security; exit; entry; communication; notification',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(613,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-02',N'Define continuing security duties',N'The organisation must identify responsibilities that remain valid after termination or role change. The purpose is to protect organizational interests after transition.',N'Protect organizational interests after transition.',N'continuing duty; termination; role change; security',1,N'Merged into EXT-01 — Merged'),
(614,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-03',N'Continue confidentiality duties',N'The organisation must define and enforce confidentiality obligations that continue after employment or contract ends. It must continue intellectual property duties. It must record duties in binding terms. It must define duration of continuing duties. The purpose is to prevent post-employment disclosure. It also aims to protect organizational ownership and rights. It also aims to make post-transition duties clear and enforceable. It also aims to avoid uncertainty over obligation periods.',N'Prevent post-employment disclosure. Protect organizational ownership and rights; Make post-transition duties clear and enforceable; Avoid uncertainty over obligation periods.',N'confidentiality; post-employment; disclosure; duty; intellectual property; knowledge; rights; contract; employment terms; continuing duty; agreement; duration; obligation; period',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(615,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-04',N'Continue intellectual property duties',N'The organisation must define continuing responsibilities for intellectual property and proprietary knowledge. The purpose is to protect organizational ownership and rights.',N'Protect organizational ownership and rights.',N'intellectual property; knowledge; post-employment; rights',1,N'Merged into EXT-03 — Merged'),
(616,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-05',N'Record duties in binding terms',N'The organisation must include continuing responsibilities in employment terms, contracts or other agreements. The purpose is to make post-transition duties clear and enforceable.',N'Make post-transition duties clear and enforceable.',N'contract; employment terms; continuing duty; agreement',1,N'Merged into EXT-03 — Merged'),
(617,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-06',N'Define duration of continuing duties',N'The organisation must state how long each post-employment or post-contract responsibility remains valid. The purpose is to avoid uncertainty over obligation periods.',N'Avoid uncertainty over obligation periods.',N'duration; post-employment; obligation; period',1,N'Merged into EXT-03 — Merged'),
(618,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-07',N'Treat role changes as exit and entry',N'The organisation must manage a role change as termination of the old role and initiation of the new role. The purpose is to apply complete access and responsibility transitions.',N'Apply complete access and responsibility transitions.',N'role change; exit; entry; transition',1,N'Merged into EXT-01 — Merged'),
(619,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-08',N'Identify departing responsibilities',N'The organisation must identify security roles, duties, ownership and approvals held by the departing or transferring person. It must transfer security responsibilities. The purpose is to prevent unowned security work. It also aims to maintain continuity and accountability.',N'Prevent unowned security work. Maintain continuity and accountability.',N'responsibility; owner; departure; role transfer; handover; responsibility transfer; continuity',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(620,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-09',N'Transfer security responsibilities',N'The organisation must assign and hand over identified security duties to authorized individuals. The purpose is to maintain continuity and accountability.',N'Maintain continuity and accountability.',N'handover; responsibility transfer; owner; continuity',1,N'Merged into EXT-08 — Merged'),
(621,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-10',N'Communicate employment changes',N'The organisation must notify relevant personnel and interested parties of approved role or employment changes. The purpose is to keep working relationships and authority current.',N'Keep working relationships and authority current.',N'communication; termination; role change; notification',1,N'Merged into EXT-01 — Merged'),
(622,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-11',N'Communicate changed procedures and contacts',N'The organisation must update and communicate operating procedures, responsibilities and contact details after transitions. The purpose is to prevent confusion and unauthorized reliance.',N'Prevent confusion and unauthorized reliance.',N'procedure; contact; update; transition',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(623,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-12',N'Notify customers and suppliers',N'The organisation must inform relevant customers, suppliers and external contacts when responsibilities or authority change. It must apply controls to external personnel. The purpose is to maintain trusted and authorized external dealings. It also aims to protect information during external workforce changes.',N'Maintain trusted and authorized external dealings. Protect information during external workforce changes.',N'customer; supplier; contact; authority; notification; contractor; supplier personnel; termination; transition',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(624,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-13',N'Apply controls to external personnel',N'The organisation must apply termination and role-change controls to contractors and supplier personnel. The purpose is to protect information during external workforce changes.',N'Protect information during external workforce changes.',N'contractor; supplier personnel; termination; transition',1,N'Merged into EXT-12 — Merged'),
(625,42,N'6.5',N'EXT-14',N'Verify transition completion',N'The organisation must confirm continuing duties, responsibility transfer, communications and related exit controls are complete. The purpose is to close security gaps caused by transitions.',N'Close security gaps caused by transitions.',N'verification; completion; transition; evidence',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(626,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-01',N'Govern confidentiality agreements',N'The organisation must define ownership, approval and oversight for confidentiality and non-disclosure agreements. It must obtain signed agreements. It must review agreements periodically and after change. The purpose is to ensure agreements are consistent and enforceable. It also aims to create demonstrable commitment before disclosure. It also aims to keep agreements current and suitable.',N'Ensure agreements are consistent and enforceable. Create demonstrable commitment before disclosure; Keep agreements current and suitable.',N'confidentiality; NDA; governance; approval; signature; personnel; interested party; access; periodic review; change; template; requirement',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(627,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-02',N'Identify agreement requirements',N'The organisation must determine where confidentiality agreements are required based on information and access. It must define agreement duration. It must define termination actions. It must define audit and monitoring rights. The purpose is to apply agreements to relevant parties and risks. It also aims to maintain protection for the required period. It also aims to secure information at the end of access. It also aims to enable assurance over sensitive information use.',N'Apply agreements to relevant parties and risks. Maintain protection for the required period; Secure information at the end of access; Enable assurance over sensitive information use.',N'requirement; information; access; NDA; duration; indefinite; public information; term; termination; action; agreement; audit right; monitoring; sensitive',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(628,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-03',N'Use legally enforceable terms',N'The organisation must draft agreements using terms enforceable in the applicable jurisdiction. It must scale terms to information sensitivity. The purpose is to support effective legal protection. It also aims to apply proportionate confidentiality protection.',N'Support effective legal protection. Apply proportionate confidentiality protection.',N'legal; enforceable; jurisdiction; agreement; classification; sensitivity; use; access; terms',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(629,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-04',N'Obtain signed agreements',N'The organisation must ensure personnel and relevant parties sign agreements before receiving confidential access. The purpose is to create demonstrable commitment before disclosure.',N'Create demonstrable commitment before disclosure.',N'signature; personnel; interested party; access',1,N'Merged into NDA-01 — Merged'),
(630,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-05',N'Scale terms to information sensitivity',N'The organisation must set terms according to information type, classification, use and permitted access. The purpose is to apply proportionate confidentiality protection.',N'Apply proportionate confidentiality protection.',N'classification; sensitivity; use; access; terms',1,N'Merged into NDA-03 — Merged'),
(631,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-06',N'Define protected information',N'The organisation must clearly describe the confidential information covered by the agreement. It must define permitted use. The purpose is to avoid ambiguity over protected content. It also aims to prevent unauthorized secondary use.',N'Avoid ambiguity over protected content. Prevent unauthorized secondary use.',N'protected information; definition; confidential; scope; permitted use; purpose; right; confidential information',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(632,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-07',N'Define agreement duration',N'The organisation must state the agreement term and any indefinite or public-availability conditions. The purpose is to maintain protection for the required period.',N'Maintain protection for the required period.',N'duration; indefinite; public information; term',1,N'Merged into NDA-02 — Merged'),
(633,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-08',N'Define termination actions',N'The organisation must state required actions when the agreement or relationship terminates. The purpose is to secure information at the end of access.',N'Secure information at the end of access.',N'termination; action; agreement; access',1,N'Merged into NDA-02 — Merged'),
(634,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-09',N'Define signatory responsibilities',N'The organisation must state duties to prevent unauthorized access, use and disclosure. The purpose is to make protective behaviour explicit.',N'Make protective behaviour explicit.',N'signatory; responsibility; unauthorized disclosure; protection',1,N'Merged into NDA-13 — Merged'),
(635,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-10',N'Define information and IP ownership',N'The organisation must state ownership of information, trade secrets and intellectual property. The purpose is to protect proprietary rights and clarify control.',N'Protect proprietary rights and clarify control.',N'ownership; trade secret; intellectual property; information',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(636,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-11',N'Define permitted use',N'The organisation must state authorized purposes and signatory rights to use confidential information. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized secondary use.',N'Prevent unauthorized secondary use.',N'permitted use; purpose; right; confidential information',1,N'Merged into NDA-06 — Merged'),
(637,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-12',N'Define audit and monitoring rights',N'The organisation must include audit or monitoring rights for highly sensitive circumstances where appropriate. The purpose is to enable assurance over sensitive information use.',N'Enable assurance over sensitive information use.',N'audit right; monitoring; sensitive; agreement',1,N'Merged into NDA-02 — Merged'),
(638,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-13',N'Require leakage reporting',N'The organisation must define how unauthorized disclosure or suspected leakage must be reported. It must define signatory responsibilities. It must require information return. It must require secure destruction. The purpose is to enable timely response to confidentiality events. It also aims to make protective behaviour explicit. It also aims to recover confidential material when access ends. It also aims to prevent recovery after authorized disposal.',N'Enable timely response to confidentiality events. Make protective behaviour explicit; Recover confidential material when access ends; Prevent recovery after authorized disposal.',N'signatory; responsibility; unauthorized disclosure; protection; leakage; reporting; incident; return; information; copy; media; termination; destruction; disposal',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(639,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-14',N'Require information return',N'The organisation must define information, copies, media and assets that must be returned at termination. The purpose is to recover confidential material when access ends.',N'Recover confidential material when access ends.',N'return; information; copy; media; termination',1,N'Merged into NDA-13 — Merged'),
(640,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-15',N'Require secure destruction — Confidentiality or non-disclosure agreements',N'The organisation must define approved destruction and evidence requirements where return is not required. The purpose is to prevent recovery after authorized disposal.',N'Prevent recovery after authorized disposal.',N'destruction; disposal; evidence; confidential',1,N'Merged into NDA-13 — Merged'),
(641,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-16',N'Define non-compliance actions',N'The organisation must state expected actions and consequences for agreement violations. It must address applicable jurisdictions. The purpose is to support deterrence and enforcement. It also aims to meet local legal requirements.',N'Support deterrence and enforcement. Meet local legal requirements.',N'non-compliance; consequence; violation; enforcement; jurisdiction; compliance; legal review; enforceability',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(642,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-17',N'Address applicable jurisdictions',N'The organisation must review agreement compliance and enforceability for each relevant jurisdiction. The purpose is to meet local legal requirements.',N'Meet local legal requirements.',N'jurisdiction; compliance; legal review; enforceability',1,N'Merged into NDA-16 — Merged'),
(643,43,N'6.6',N'NDA-18',N'Review agreements periodically and after change',N'The organisation must review requirements and templates regularly and when influencing conditions change. The purpose is to keep agreements current and suitable.',N'Keep agreements current and suitable.',N'periodic review; change; template; requirement',1,N'Merged into NDA-01 — Merged'),
(644,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-01',N'Govern secure remote working',N'The organisation must define ownership, approval, oversight and risk acceptance for remote work. It must maintain a remote-working policy. It must deploy remote systems securely. It must address remote-working insurance. The purpose is to ensure remote work is authorized and controlled. It also aims to provide consistent rules for remote work. It also aims to prevent insecure remote provisioning. It also aims to manage financial exposure from remote arrangements.',N'Ensure remote work is authorized and controlled. Provide consistent rules for remote work; Prevent insecure remote provisioning; Manage financial exposure from remote arrangements.',N'remote working; governance; approval; risk; remote policy; condition; restriction; responsibility; deployment; initialization; remote system; secure; insurance; equipment',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(645,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-02',N'Maintain a remote-working policy',N'The organisation must define conditions, restrictions, responsibilities and permitted arrangements. The purpose is to provide consistent rules for remote work.',N'Provide consistent rules for remote work.',N'remote policy; condition; restriction; responsibility',1,N'Merged into RMT-01 — Merged'),
(646,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-03',N'Assess remote locations and jurisdictions',N'The organisation must consider physical security, local environment and applicable jurisdictions. It must secure the remote physical environment. It must maintain remote backup and continuity. It must monitor and audit remote activity. The purpose is to adapt controls to location-specific risks and law. It also aims to protect equipment and information outside premises. It also aims to maintain information availability and resilience. It also aims to detect misuse and security events.',N'Adapt controls to location-specific risks and law. Protect equipment and information outside premises; Maintain information availability and resilience; Detect misuse and security events.',N'location; jurisdiction; physical security; remote; physical environment; cabinet; workspace; protection; backup; recovery; continuity; audit; monitoring; remote access',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(647,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-04',N'Secure the remote physical environment',N'The organisation must define physical safeguards such as secure rooms, cabinets and positioning. The purpose is to protect equipment and information outside premises.',N'Protect equipment and information outside premises.',N'physical environment; cabinet; workspace; protection',1,N'Merged into RMT-03 — Merged'),
(648,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-05',N'Secure transport between locations',N'The organisation must define safe transport of devices, media, documents and other assets. The purpose is to prevent loss or exposure in transit.',N'Prevent loss or exposure in transit.',N'transport; device; media; document; remote',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(649,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-06',N'Apply clear-desk printing and disposal rules',N'The organisation must define remote clear-desk, printing, storage and secure disposal practices. The purpose is to protect hardcopy and media in remote locations.',N'Protect hardcopy and media in remote locations.',N'clear desk; printing; storage; disposal',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(650,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-07',N'Enable remote event reporting',N'The organisation must provide accessible reporting channels and instructions for remote security events. The purpose is to support prompt reporting outside premises.',N'Support prompt reporting outside premises.',N'event reporting; remote; channel; instruction',1,N'Merged into RMT-20 — Merged'),
(651,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-08',N'Define permitted remote environments',N'The organisation must specify acceptable and prohibited physical remote working environments. It must define permitted work information and systems. The purpose is to avoid work in unsuitable locations. It also aims to limit remote activity to approved scope.',N'Avoid work in unsuitable locations. Limit remote activity to approved scope.',N'permitted environment; prohibited location; remote work; permitted work; classification; system; service',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(652,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-09',N'Protect remote communications',N'The organisation must define secure communication methods according to information and system sensitivity. It must protect remote devices from threats. It must configure remote device safeguards. The purpose is to protect information over remote links. It also aims to maintain secure remote endpoints. It also aims to protect devices and data if unattended or lost.',N'Protect information over remote links. Maintain secure remote endpoints; Protect devices and data if unattended or lost.',N'communication; remote access; sensitivity; encryption; firewall; malware; patch; endpoint; screen lock; inactivity; tracking; remote wipe',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(653,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-10',N'Control remote access methods',N'The organisation must authorize and secure remote access, including virtual desktop use where appropriate. The purpose is to limit exposure from remote endpoints.',N'Limit exposure from remote endpoints.',N'remote access; virtual desktop; authorization; endpoint',1,N'Merged into RMT-26 — Merged'),
(654,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-11',N'Control privately owned equipment',N'The organisation must define whether and how personal devices can process or access organizational information. It must provide approved equipment and storage. The purpose is to manage risk from equipment outside organizational control. It also aims to enable secure remote work with approved resources.',N'Manage risk from equipment outside organizational control. Enable secure remote work with approved resources.',N'BYOD; personal device; control; information; equipment; storage furniture; approved; remote',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(655,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-12',N'Prevent household and visitor access',N'The organisation must protect equipment and information from family, friends and visitors. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized access in private locations.',N'Prevent unauthorized access in private locations.',N'family; visitor; unauthorized access; remote',1,N'Merged into RMT-26 — Merged'),
(656,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-13',N'Prevent public-place exposure',N'The organisation must define safeguards against observation, theft and unauthorized access in public places. It must secure home and public networks. The purpose is to protect information during mobile and public work. It also aims to reduce communication and network exposure.',N'Protect information during mobile and public work. Reduce communication and network exposure.',N'public place; shoulder surfing; theft; mobile; home network; public network; wireless; configuration',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(657,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-14',N'Secure home and public networks',N'The organisation must set requirements and restrictions for home, wireless and public network use. The purpose is to reduce communication and network exposure.',N'Reduce communication and network exposure.',N'home network; public network; wireless; configuration',1,N'Merged into RMT-13 — Merged'),
(658,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-15',N'Protect remote devices from threats',N'The organisation must require firewalls, malware protection, updates and other endpoint safeguards. The purpose is to maintain secure remote endpoints.',N'Maintain secure remote endpoints.',N'firewall; malware; patch; endpoint',1,N'Merged into RMT-09 — Merged'),
(659,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-16',N'Deploy remote systems securely',N'The organisation must use secure methods to deploy and initialize systems remotely. The purpose is to prevent insecure remote provisioning.',N'Prevent insecure remote provisioning.',N'deployment; initialization; remote system; secure',1,N'Merged into RMT-01 — Merged'),
(660,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-17',N'Use strong remote authentication',N'The organisation must apply secure authentication and privilege enablement, avoiding weak single-factor access. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized network access.',N'Prevent unauthorized network access.',N'authentication; MFA; privilege; remote access',1,N'Merged into RMT-26 — Merged'),
(661,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-18',N'Provide approved equipment and storage',N'The organisation must provide suitable controlled equipment and storage furniture where personal equipment is prohibited. The purpose is to enable secure remote work with approved resources.',N'Enable secure remote work with approved resources.',N'equipment; storage furniture; approved; remote',1,N'Merged into RMT-11 — Merged'),
(662,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-19',N'Define permitted work information and systems',N'The organisation must specify allowed work, information classifications and authorized systems and services. The purpose is to limit remote activity to approved scope.',N'Limit remote activity to approved scope.',N'permitted work; classification; system; service',1,N'Merged into RMT-08 — Merged'),
(663,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-20',N'Train remote workers and support staff',N'The organisation must provide role-relevant guidance for secure remote business and technical support. It must enable remote event reporting. It must provide remote support and maintenance. The purpose is to build secure remote-working behaviour and support. It also aims to support prompt reporting outside premises. It also aims to maintain secure and reliable remote equipment.',N'Build secure remote-working behaviour and support. Support prompt reporting outside premises; Maintain secure and reliable remote equipment.',N'event reporting; remote; channel; instruction; training; remote worker; support staff; guidance; support; maintenance; hardware; software',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(664,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-21',N'Configure remote device safeguards',N'The organisation must use screen locks, inactivity timers, tracking and remote wipe where appropriate. The purpose is to protect devices and data if unattended or lost.',N'Protect devices and data if unattended or lost.',N'screen lock; inactivity; tracking; remote wipe',1,N'Merged into RMT-09 — Merged'),
(665,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-22',N'Provide remote support and maintenance',N'The organisation must define authorized hardware and software support and maintenance arrangements. The purpose is to maintain secure and reliable remote equipment.',N'Maintain secure and reliable remote equipment.',N'support; maintenance; hardware; software',1,N'Merged into RMT-20 — Merged'),
(666,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-23',N'Address remote-working insurance',N'The organisation must assess and maintain suitable insurance where required. The purpose is to manage financial exposure from remote arrangements.',N'Manage financial exposure from remote arrangements.',N'insurance; remote working; equipment; risk',1,N'Merged into RMT-01 — Merged'),
(667,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-24',N'Maintain remote backup and continuity',N'The organisation must define backup, recovery and business continuity arrangements for remote work. The purpose is to maintain information availability and resilience.',N'Maintain information availability and resilience.',N'backup; recovery; continuity; remote',1,N'Merged into RMT-03 — Merged'),
(668,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-25',N'Monitor and audit remote activity',N'The organisation must apply proportionate audit logging and security monitoring to remote access and work. The purpose is to detect misuse and security events.',N'Detect misuse and security events.',N'audit; monitoring; remote access; logging',1,N'Merged into RMT-03 — Merged'),
(669,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-26',N'Revoke remote authority and access',N'The organisation must remove remote access rights and privileges promptly when no longer required. It must control remote access methods. It must prevent household and visitor access. It must use strong remote authentication. The purpose is to prevent continued unauthorized access. It also aims to limit exposure from remote endpoints. It also aims to prevent unauthorized access in private locations. It also aims to prevent unauthorized network access.',N'Prevent continued unauthorized access. Limit exposure from remote endpoints; Prevent unauthorized access in private locations; Prevent unauthorized network access.',N'remote access; virtual desktop; authorization; endpoint; family; visitor; unauthorized access; remote; authentication; MFA; privilege; revocation; access right; termination',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(670,44,N'6.7',N'RMT-27',N'Govern remote working requirements',N'The organisation must define, approve, implement and keep current the scope, criteria, ownership, controls and evidence requirements for remote and hybrid work, virtual work and remote maintenance using organisational or approved personal equipment. It must apply these requirements before remote work is approved, whenever the location, role, equipment, access or risk changes, during periodic reviews, and when remote work ends. It must verify compliance at least annually, review effectiveness after significant change, respond to failures within the applicable response time, and allow bypass only through a documented and approved exception with risk treatment and a review or expiry date. The purpose is to ensure remote working requirements remain complete, effective, current, consistently applied and supported by reliable evidence.',N'Ensure remote working requirements remain complete, effective, current, consistently applied and supported by reliable evidence.',N'remote working; hybrid work; virtual work; remote maintenance; governance; scope; criteria; ownership; approval; controls; evidence; review; exception',0,N'Completed - reconstructed from obligation requirements'),
(671,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-01',N'Govern security event reporting',N'The organisation must define ownership, channels, responsibilities and oversight for event reporting. It must provide accessible reporting mechanisms. It must require timely event reporting. The purpose is to ensure consistent and accountable reporting. It also aims to remove barriers to timely reporting. It also aims to minimize incident impact through early notice.',N'Ensure consistent and accountable reporting. Remove barriers to timely reporting; Minimize incident impact through early notice.',N'event reporting; governance; channel; responsibility; mechanism; accessible; available; reporting; timely; personnel; user; suspected event',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(672,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-02',N'Provide accessible reporting mechanisms',N'The organisation must offer easy, accessible and available methods for reporting events. The purpose is to remove barriers to timely reporting.',N'Remove barriers to timely reporting.',N'mechanism; accessible; available; reporting',1,N'Merged into EVR-01 — Merged'),
(673,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-03',N'Require timely event reporting',N'The organisation must require personnel and users to report observed or suspected events as quickly as possible. The purpose is to minimize incident impact through early notice.',N'Minimize incident impact through early notice.',N'timely; personnel; user; suspected event',1,N'Merged into EVR-01 — Merged'),
(674,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-04',N'Communicate reporting procedures and contacts',N'The organisation must explain what to report, how to report and the responsible contact point. The purpose is to enable correct routing of reports.',N'Enable correct routing of reports.',N'procedure; contact; communication; report',1,N'Merged into EVR-07 — Merged'),
(675,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-05',N'Report ineffective security controls',N'The organisation must report controls that are missing, failed or not operating effectively. The purpose is to detect control weaknesses before further harm.',N'Detect control weaknesses before further harm.',N'ineffective control; failure; weakness; report',1,N'Merged into EVR-13 — Merged'),
(676,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-06',N'Report confidentiality integrity or availability breaches',N'The organisation must report actual or suspected compromise of information security properties. The purpose is to enable response to information compromise.',N'Enable response to information compromise.',N'confidentiality; integrity; availability; breach',1,N'Merged into EVR-09 — Merged'),
(677,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-07',N'Report human errors',N'The organisation must report mistakes that could create or have created security impact. It must communicate reporting procedures and contacts. It must report abnormal system behaviour. The purpose is to correct errors and prevent escalation. It also aims to enable correct routing of reports. It also aims to identify possible incidents and service risks.',N'Correct errors and prevent escalation. Enable correct routing of reports; Identify possible incidents and service risks.',N'procedure; contact; communication; report; human error; mistake; impact; reporting; malfunction; anomaly; software; hardware',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(678,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-08',N'Report policy and standards non-compliance',N'The organisation must report violations of security policies, topic policies and applicable standards. The purpose is to detect and address non-compliance.',N'Detect and address non-compliance.',N'policy; standard; non-compliance; violation',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(679,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-09',N'Report physical security breaches',N'The organisation must report unauthorized physical access, damage or failure of physical safeguards. It must report confidentiality integrity or availability breaches. It must report access violations. The purpose is to protect facilities, equipment and information. It also aims to enable response to information compromise. It also aims to enable rapid access-control response.',N'Protect facilities, equipment and information. Enable response to information compromise; Enable rapid access-control response.',N'confidentiality; integrity; availability; breach; physical security; unauthorized access; damage; access violation; unauthorized; privilege; suspicious',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(680,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-10',N'Report unauthorized system changes',N'The organisation must report changes that bypassed the approved change-management process. The purpose is to detect uncontrolled change and risk.',N'Detect uncontrolled change and risk.',N'unauthorized change; change management; system; report',1,N'Merged into EVR-13 — Merged'),
(681,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-11',N'Report abnormal system behaviour',N'The organisation must report software or hardware malfunctions and unusual behaviour. The purpose is to identify possible incidents and service risks.',N'Identify possible incidents and service risks.',N'malfunction; anomaly; software; hardware',1,N'Merged into EVR-07 — Merged'),
(682,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-12',N'Report access violations',N'The organisation must report unauthorized or suspicious access attempts and privilege misuse. The purpose is to enable rapid access-control response.',N'Enable rapid access-control response.',N'access violation; unauthorized; privilege; suspicious',1,N'Merged into EVR-09 — Merged'),
(683,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-13',N'Report suspected vulnerabilities',N'The organisation must report suspected weaknesses through authorized channels without testing them. It must report ineffective security controls. It must report unauthorized system changes. It must report suspected malware. The purpose is to enable safe vulnerability assessment. It also aims to detect control weaknesses before further harm. It also aims to detect uncontrolled change and risk. It also aims to support rapid containment and investigation.',N'Enable safe vulnerability assessment. Detect control weaknesses before further harm; Detect uncontrolled change and risk; Support rapid containment and investigation.',N'ineffective control; failure; weakness; report; unauthorized change; change management; system; vulnerability; authorized channel; malware; infection; suspicion; containment',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(684,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-14',N'Report suspected malware',N'The organisation must report signs of possible malware infection promptly. The purpose is to support rapid containment and investigation.',N'Support rapid containment and investigation.',N'malware; infection; suspicion; containment',1,N'Merged into EVR-13 — Merged'),
(685,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-15',N'Prohibit unauthorized vulnerability testing',N'The organisation must instruct personnel not to prove or exploit suspected vulnerabilities. The purpose is to prevent damage, evidence loss and legal exposure.',N'Prevent damage, evidence loss and legal exposure.',N'vulnerability testing; prohibition; evidence; liability',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(686,45,N'6.8',N'EVR-16',N'Preserve event report evidence',N'The organisation must record reports, timestamps, affected assets and initial actions. The purpose is to support triage, investigation and legal needs.',N'Support triage, investigation and legal needs.',N'event record; timestamp; evidence; affected asset',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(687,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-01',N'Define perimeter scope and requirements',N'The organisation must identify protected areas, the information and other assets inside them, and the security level each boundary must provide. The purpose is to make every physical security boundary risk-based, approved and traceable to the assets it protects.',N'Make every physical security boundary risk-based, approved and traceable to the assets it protects.',N'protected area; asset; requirement; boundary; risk; approval',1,N'Merged into PPS-08 — Merged'),
(688,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-02',N'Design layered security perimeters',N'The organisation must use one or more physical barriers and separate areas with different security needs through suitable internal boundaries and controlled transition points. It must manage shared sites and internal secure areas. The purpose is to use layered and zoned protection so one weak boundary does not expose higher-risk assets. It also aims to maintain appropriate separation inside shared or multi-use premises.',N'Use layered and zoned protection so one weak boundary does not expose higher-risk assets. Maintain appropriate separation inside shared or multi-use premises.',N'layered barrier; zoning; internal boundary; transition point; secure area; shared site; lockable office; internal barrier; tenant; secure room; separation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(689,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-03',N'Maintain solid site and building construction',N'The organisation must keep perimeter walls, roofs, ceilings and floors physically sound, continuous and resistant to easy break-in. The purpose is to prevent entry through weak, damaged or incomplete building fabric.',N'Prevent entry through weak, damaged or incomplete building fabric.',N'solid construction; wall; roof; ceiling; floor; break-in resistance',1,N'Merged into PPS-10 — Merged'),
(690,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-04',N'Protect external doors',N'The organisation must protect every external door against unauthorized access using suitable locks, alarms, bars or equivalent control mechanisms. It must secure windows and glazing. The purpose is to ensure exterior doors do not become an easy route into protected areas. It also aims to prevent unauthorized access through windows and vulnerable glazing.',N'Ensure exterior doors do not become an easy route into protected areas. Prevent unauthorized access through windows and vulnerable glazing.',N'external door; lock; alarm; bar; unauthorized access; door security; window; glazing; ground level; external protection; unattended',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(691,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-05',N'Secure windows and glazing',N'The organisation must lock windows when areas are unattended and add external protection where risk requires it, particularly at ground level. The purpose is to prevent unauthorized access through windows and vulnerable glazing.',N'Prevent unauthorized access through windows and vulnerable glazing.',N'window; glazing; ground level; lock; external protection; unattended',1,N'Merged into PPS-04 — Merged'),
(692,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-06',N'Protect ventilation and service openings',N'The organisation must identify ventilation points and other perimeter penetrations and protect them against unauthorized entry or interference. It must inspect, test and maintain perimeters. The purpose is to close less obvious access routes through vents, ducts and service penetrations. It also aims to keep physical security controls effective throughout their service life.',N'Close less obvious access routes through vents, ducts and service penetrations. Keep physical security controls effective throughout their service life.',N'ventilation; duct; service opening; penetration; grille; tamper protection; inspection; testing; maintenance; defect; repair; effectiveness',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(693,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-07',N'Control fire doors on the perimeter',N'The organisation must alarm, monitor and test perimeter fire doors together with adjoining walls, using suitable resistance standards and failsafe operation. The purpose is to preserve both life safety and perimeter resistance at fire-door openings.',N'Preserve both life safety and perimeter resistance at fire-door openings.',N'fire door; alarm; monitoring; resistance; wall; failsafe; test',1,N'Merged into PPS-08 — Merged'),
(694,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-08',N'Alarm and monitor perimeter integrity',N'The organisation must use suitable alarms and monitoring to detect unauthorized access, damage, interference and loss of perimeter effectiveness. It must define perimeter scope and requirements. It must control fire doors on the perimeter. The purpose is to detect perimeter failures quickly enough for a controlled response. It also aims to make every physical security boundary risk-based, approved and traceable to the assets it protects. It also aims to preserve both life safety and perimeter resistance at fire-door openings.',N'Detect perimeter failures quickly enough for a controlled response. Make every physical security boundary risk-based, approved and traceable to the assets it protects; Preserve both life safety and perimeter resistance at fire-door openings.',N'protected area; asset; requirement; boundary; risk; approval; fire door; alarm; monitoring; resistance; wall; failsafe; test; intrusion',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(695,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-09',N'Inspect, test and maintain perimeters',N'The organisation must perform planned inspections, tests and maintenance for barriers, doors, windows, openings, alarms and other perimeter components. The purpose is to keep physical security controls effective throughout their service life.',N'Keep physical security controls effective throughout their service life.',N'inspection; testing; maintenance; defect; repair; effectiveness',1,N'Merged into PPS-06 — Merged'),
(696,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-10',N'Manage perimeter changes and temporary works',N'The organisation must assess and control construction, refurbishment, maintenance and temporary works that can weaken or bypass a security perimeter. It must maintain solid site and building construction. It must strengthen protection during increased threats. The purpose is to prevent planned work from creating uncontrolled physical access paths. It also aims to prevent entry through weak, damaged or incomplete building fabric. It also aims to increase perimeter protection quickly and consistently during heightened risk.',N'Prevent planned work from creating uncontrolled physical access paths. Prevent entry through weak, damaged or incomplete building fabric; Increase perimeter protection quickly and consistently during heightened risk.',N'solid construction; wall; roof; ceiling; floor; break-in resistance; construction; refurbishment; temporary work; change; contractor; opening; increased threat; escalation',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(697,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-11',N'Manage shared sites and internal secure areas',N'The organisation must use lockable offices, continuous internal barriers and added boundaries where different organizations or activities share a building or site. The purpose is to maintain appropriate separation inside shared or multi-use premises.',N'Maintain appropriate separation inside shared or multi-use premises.',N'shared site; lockable office; internal barrier; tenant; secure room; separation',1,N'Merged into PPS-02 — Merged'),
(698,46,N'7.1',N'PPS-12',N'Strengthen protection during increased threats',N'The organisation must define scalable physical measures that can be activated when threat conditions rise and withdrawn through controlled approval. The purpose is to increase perimeter protection quickly and consistently during heightened risk.',N'Increase perimeter protection quickly and consistently during heightened risk.',N'increased threat; escalation; strengthened controls; temporary barrier; readiness',1,N'Merged into PPS-10 — Merged'),
(699,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-01',N'Physical Access Authorization',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for physical access authorization, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers periodic access review and revocation. It also covers supplier and third-party access. It also covers access logs and authentication records. It also covers access cards biometrics and two-factor entry. The purpose is to ensure physical access authorization is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure periodic access review and revocation is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure supplier and third-party access is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure access logs and authentication records is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure access cards biometrics and two-factor entry is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure physical access authorization is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure periodic access review and revocation is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure supplier and third-party access is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure access logs and authentication records is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence; Ensure access cards biometrics and two-factor entry is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'physical access authorization; physical security; 7.2; periodic access review and revocation; supplier and third-party access; access logs and authentication records; access cards biometrics and two-factor entry',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(700,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-03',N'Access Logs And Authentication Records',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for access logs and authentication records, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure access logs and authentication records is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure access logs and authentication records is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'access logs and authentication records; physical security; 7.2',1,N'Merged into ENT-01 — Merged'),
(701,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-04',N'Access Cards Biometrics And Two-Factor Entry',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for access cards biometrics and two-factor entry, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure access cards biometrics and two-factor entry is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure access cards biometrics and two-factor entry is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'access cards biometrics and two-factor entry; physical security; 7.2',1,N'Merged into ENT-01 — Merged'),
(702,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-05',N'Reception And Visible Identification',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for reception and visible identification, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers visitor identity recording and supervision. It also covers keys lock codes and key audits. The purpose is to ensure reception and visible identification is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure visitor identity recording and supervision is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure keys lock codes and key audits is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure reception and visible identification is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure visitor identity recording and supervision is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence; Ensure keys lock codes and key audits is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'reception and visible identification; physical security; 7.2; visitor identity recording and supervision; keys lock codes and key audits',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(703,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-07',N'Visitor Identity Recording And Supervision',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for visitor identity recording and supervision, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure visitor identity recording and supervision is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure visitor identity recording and supervision is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'visitor identity recording and supervision; physical security; 7.2',1,N'Merged into ENT-05 — Merged'),
(704,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-08',N'Keys Lock Codes And Key Audits',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for keys lock codes and key audits, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure keys lock codes and key audits is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure keys lock codes and key audits is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'keys lock codes and key audits; physical security; 7.2',1,N'Merged into ENT-05 — Merged'),
(705,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-09',N'Emergency Exits And Other Entry Points',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for emergency exits and other entry points, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers higher-threat and shared-building entry controls. The purpose is to ensure emergency exits and other entry points is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure higher-threat and shared-building entry controls is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure emergency exits and other entry points is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure higher-threat and shared-building entry controls is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'emergency exits and other entry points; physical security; 7.2; higher-threat and shared-building entry controls',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(706,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-10',N'Delivery And Loading Area Separation',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for delivery and loading area separation, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers incoming delivery inspection and registration. The purpose is to ensure delivery and loading area separation is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure incoming delivery inspection and registration is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure delivery and loading area separation is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure incoming delivery inspection and registration is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'delivery and loading area separation; physical security; 7.2; incoming delivery inspection and registration',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(707,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-11',N'Incoming Delivery Inspection And Registration',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for incoming delivery inspection and registration, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure incoming delivery inspection and registration is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure incoming delivery inspection and registration is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'incoming delivery inspection and registration; physical security; 7.2',1,N'Merged into ENT-10 — Merged'),
(708,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-12',N'Higher-Threat And Shared-Building Entry Controls',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for higher-threat and shared-building entry controls, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure higher-threat and shared-building entry controls is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure higher-threat and shared-building entry controls is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'higher-threat and shared-building entry controls; physical security; 7.2',1,N'Merged into ENT-09 — Merged'),
(709,47,N'7.2',N'ENT-13',N'Physical Access Authorization and Related Controls',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for physical access authorization, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers periodic access review and revocation. It also covers supplier and third-party access. It also covers access logs and authentication records. It also covers access cards biometrics and two-factor entry. The purpose is to ensure physical access authorization is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure periodic access review and revocation is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure supplier and third-party access is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure access logs and authentication records is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure access cards biometrics and two-factor entry is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure physical access authorization is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure periodic access review and revocation is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure supplier and third-party access is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure access logs and authentication records is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence; Ensure access cards biometrics and two-factor entry is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'physical access authorization; physical security; 7.2; periodic access review and revocation; supplier and third-party access; access logs and authentication records; access cards biometrics and two-factor entry',0,N'Added from obligation registers — name variant; review required'),
(710,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-01',N'Secure Office And Room Design',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for secure office and room design, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers electromagnetic shielding assessment. The purpose is to ensure secure office and room design is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure electromagnetic shielding assessment is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure secure office and room design is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure electromagnetic shielding assessment is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'secure office and room design; physical security; 7.3; electromagnetic shielding assessment',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(711,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-02',N'Critical Facility Location Away From Public Access',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for critical facility location away from public access, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure critical facility location away from public access is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure critical facility location away from public access is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'critical facility location away from public access; physical security; 7.3',1,N'Merged into OFF-08 — Merged'),
(712,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-03',N'Unobtrusive Building Appearance',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for unobtrusive building appearance, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers removal of signs revealing processing activities. It also covers visual privacy from outside. The purpose is to ensure unobtrusive building appearance is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure removal of signs revealing processing activities is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure visual privacy from outside is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure unobtrusive building appearance is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure removal of signs revealing processing activities is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence; Ensure visual privacy from outside is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'unobtrusive building appearance; physical security; 7.3; removal of signs revealing processing activities; visual privacy from outside',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(713,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-04',N'Removal Of Signs Revealing Processing Activities',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for removal of signs revealing processing activities, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure removal of signs revealing processing activities is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure removal of signs revealing processing activities is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'removal of signs revealing processing activities; physical security; 7.3',1,N'Merged into OFF-03 — Merged'),
(714,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-05',N'Visual Privacy From Outside',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for visual privacy from outside, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure visual privacy from outside is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure visual privacy from outside is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'visual privacy from outside; physical security; 7.3',1,N'Merged into OFF-03 — Merged'),
(715,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-07',N'Electromagnetic Shielding Assessment',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for electromagnetic shielding assessment, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure electromagnetic shielding assessment is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure electromagnetic shielding assessment is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'electromagnetic shielding assessment; physical security; 7.3',1,N'Merged into OFF-01 — Merged'),
(716,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-08',N'Confidential Facility Directory Restrictions',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for confidential facility directory restrictions, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers critical facility location away from public access. It also covers internal map and location restrictions. The purpose is to ensure confidential facility directory restrictions is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure critical facility location away from public access is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure internal map and location restrictions is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure confidential facility directory restrictions is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure critical facility location away from public access is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence; Ensure internal map and location restrictions is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'critical facility location away from public access; physical security; 7.3; confidential facility directory restrictions; internal map and location restrictions',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(717,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-09',N'Internal Map And Location Restrictions',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for internal map and location restrictions, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. The purpose is to ensure internal map and location restrictions is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure internal map and location restrictions is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'internal map and location restrictions; physical security; 7.3',1,N'Merged into OFF-08 — Merged'),
(718,48,N'7.3',N'OFF-10',N'Secure Office And Room Design and Related Controls',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for secure office and room design, proportionate to the protected assets and physical security risk. It also covers electromagnetic shielding assessment. The purpose is to ensure secure office and room design is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure electromagnetic shielding assessment is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure secure office and room design is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure electromagnetic shielding assessment is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'secure office and room design; physical security; 7.3; electromagnetic shielding assessment',0,N'Added from obligation registers — name variant; review required'),
