(971,71,N'8.12',N'DLP-11',N'Personnel Monitoring Privacy And Legal Assessment',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for personnel monitoring privacy and legal assessment, proportionate to business need, information classification and security risk. The purpose is to ensure personnel monitoring privacy and legal assessment is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure personnel monitoring privacy and legal assessment is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'personnel monitoring privacy and legal assessment; technology security; 8.12',1,N'Merged into DLP-02 — Merged'),
(972,71,N'8.12',N'DLP-12',N'DLP Tool Tuning Incident Response And Effectiveness Review',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for DLP tool tuning incident response and effectiveness review, proportionate to business need, information classification and security risk. The purpose is to ensure DLP tool tuning incident response and effectiveness review is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure DLP tool tuning incident response and effectiveness review is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'DLP tool tuning incident response and effectiveness review; technology security; 8.12',1,N'Merged into DLP-10 — Merged'),
(973,71,N'8.12',N'DLP-13',N'Sensitive Information Identification And Classification and Related Controls',N'The organisation must define, implement and maintain practical controls for sensitive information identification and classification, proportionate to business need, information classification and security risk. It also covers copy paste upload and transmission restriction. It also covers screenshot photograph training and auditing. The purpose is to ensure sensitive information identification and classification is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure copy paste upload and transmission restriction is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. It also aims to ensure screenshot photograph training and auditing is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'Ensure sensitive information identification and classification is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence. Ensure copy paste upload and transmission restriction is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence; Ensure screenshot photograph training and auditing is authorized, effective, monitored and supported by evidence.',N'sensitive information identification and classification; technology security; 8.12; copy paste upload and transmission restriction; screenshot photograph training and auditing',0,N'Added from obligation registers — name variant; review required'),
(974,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-01',N'Set backup requirements and plans',N'The organisation must define backup rules and plans for information, software and systems. It must set the backup scope, method, frequency, retention, recovery point and restoration steps according to business need and criticality. It must run and monitor backups. It also covers backup records and restoration procedures. It also covers pre-backup data-loss detection. The purpose is to make sure every important system has clear, approved and usable backup requirements. It also aims to produce complete and reliable backup copies at the required time. It also aims to ensure backup records and restoration procedures supports agreed recovery and continuity needs. It also aims to ensure pre-backup data-loss detection supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Make sure every important system has clear, approved and usable backup requirements. Produce complete and reliable backup copies at the required time; Ensure backup records and restoration procedures supports agreed recovery and continuity needs; Ensure pre-backup data-loss detection supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'backup policy; backup plan; scope; frequency; retention; RPO; restoration; scheduled backup; monitoring; backup record; failure; completeness; backup records and restoration procedures; technology security',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(975,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-02',N'Run and monitor backups',N'The organisation must perform scheduled backups, keep accurate and complete backup records, detect missing data before backup, monitor each backup job and address failures. The purpose is to produce complete and reliable backup copies at the required time.',N'Produce complete and reliable backup copies at the required time.',N'scheduled backup; monitoring; backup record; failure; completeness',1,N'Merged into BKP-01 — Merged'),
(976,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-03',N'Protect backup copies',N'The organisation must store backup copies in a secure remote location and protect them from unauthorised access, physical damage and environmental threats. It must use encryption when the risk requires it. It also covers remote backup location and disaster separation. It also covers backup encryption and confidentiality. The purpose is to keep backup copies confidential, intact and available after a main-site incident. It also aims to ensure remote backup location and disaster separation supports agreed recovery and continuity needs. It also aims to ensure backup encryption and confidentiality supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Keep backup copies confidential, intact and available after a main-site incident. Ensure remote backup location and disaster separation supports agreed recovery and continuity needs; Ensure backup encryption and confidentiality supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'remote backup; physical protection; environmental protection; access; encryption; remote backup location and disaster separation; technology security; backup encryption and confidentiality',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(977,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-04',N'Test restoration and recovery',N'The organisation must regularly test backup media and restore copies to a separate test system. It must confirm that restoration procedures meet recovery time and continuity needs and cover the full critical system. It also covers complete-system recovery and continuity testing. The purpose is to prove that backup copies can restore the required service within the agreed time. It also aims to ensure complete-system recovery and continuity testing supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Prove that backup copies can restore the required service within the agreed time. Ensure complete-system recovery and continuity testing supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'restore test; backup media; RTO; recovery; continuity; critical system; complete-system recovery and continuity testing; technology security',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(978,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-05',N'Manage cloud backup and retention',N'The organisation must define how cloud information, applications and systems are backed up, confirm provider responsibilities, keep copies for the approved period and securely delete expired backup information. It also covers cloud backup responsibilities retention and secure deletion. The purpose is to apply the same recovery and information-life-cycle controls to cloud and retained backups. It also aims to ensure cloud backup responsibilities retention and secure deletion supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Apply the same recovery and information-life-cycle controls to cloud and retained backups. Ensure cloud backup responsibilities retention and secure deletion supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'cloud backup; provider; retention; archive; secure deletion; lifecycle; cloud backup responsibilities retention and secure deletion; technology security',0,N'Reviewed - all merged sources addressed'),
(979,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-06',N'Backup Records And Restoration Procedures',N'The organisation must define and maintain controls for backup records and restoration procedures so backup copies remain complete, secure and recoverable. The purpose is to ensure backup records and restoration procedures supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Ensure backup records and restoration procedures supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'backup records and restoration procedures; technology security',1,N'Merged into BKP-01 — Merged'),
(980,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-07',N'Recovery Point Frequency Extent And Criticality',N'The organisation must define and maintain controls for recovery point frequency extent and criticality so backup copies remain complete, secure and recoverable. The purpose is to ensure recovery point frequency extent and criticality supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Ensure recovery point frequency extent and criticality supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'recovery point frequency extent and criticality; technology security',0,N'Standalone - not merged'),
(981,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-08',N'Remote Backup Location And Disaster Separation',N'The organisation must define and maintain controls for remote backup location and disaster separation so backup copies remain complete, secure and recoverable. The purpose is to ensure remote backup location and disaster separation supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Ensure remote backup location and disaster separation supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'remote backup location and disaster separation; technology security',1,N'Merged into BKP-03 — Merged'),
(982,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-09',N'Backup Encryption And Confidentiality',N'The organisation must define and maintain controls for backup encryption and confidentiality so backup copies remain complete, secure and recoverable. The purpose is to ensure backup encryption and confidentiality supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Ensure backup encryption and confidentiality supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'backup encryption and confidentiality; technology security',1,N'Merged into BKP-03 — Merged'),
(983,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-10',N'Pre-Backup Data-Loss Detection',N'The organisation must define and maintain controls for pre-backup data-loss detection so backup copies remain complete, secure and recoverable. The purpose is to ensure pre-backup data-loss detection supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Ensure pre-backup data-loss detection supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'pre-backup data-loss detection; technology security',1,N'Merged into BKP-01 — Merged'),
(984,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-11',N'Complete-System Recovery And Continuity Testing',N'The organisation must define and maintain controls for complete-system recovery and continuity testing so backup copies remain complete, secure and recoverable. The purpose is to ensure complete-system recovery and continuity testing supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Ensure complete-system recovery and continuity testing supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'complete-system recovery and continuity testing; technology security',1,N'Merged into BKP-04 — Merged'),
(985,72,N'8.13',N'BKP-12',N'Cloud Backup Responsibilities Retention And Secure Deletion',N'The organisation must define and maintain controls for cloud backup responsibilities retention and secure deletion so backup copies remain complete, secure and recoverable. The purpose is to ensure cloud backup responsibilities retention and secure deletion supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'Ensure cloud backup responsibilities retention and secure deletion supports agreed recovery and continuity needs.',N'cloud backup responsibilities retention and secure deletion; technology security',1,N'Merged into BKP-05 — Merged'),
